{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment","id":399463,"title":"Will Geist get the 2e treatment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-09T15:36:56-08:00","id":399463,"title":"Will Geist get the 2e treatment?","content":"As it says in the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T15:41:57-08:00","id":399481,"title":"","content":"Probably, but it is not in this year schedule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4055,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","user":"Felipe","date":". 02-09-2015, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T16:33:57-08:00","id":399507,"title":"","content":"One way or another we'll probably see come GenCon 2015. Fingers crossed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:48:33-08:00","id":399625,"title":"","content":"Man, I hope so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T10:23:11-08:00","id":400488,"title":"","content":"Probably; the core idea is great, but there's a LOT of improvements that could be made. I got half way through writing a 2E geist, came up with great ideas (in my biased opinion) and had great fun doing so; I can't see why Onyx Path would feel differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T21:43:01-08:00","id":403001,"title":"","content":"As above, I hope so but I don't expect to see it until 2016/17. But that's OK. Part of the reason Geist copes so much flak &amp; complaints is because it was rushed to production and the writing/editing suffered.<br /> <br /> Eg; kerobori have several dots of keys. 1.1 fixed some of this but honestly I know the authors could have done better. Hopefully when the time comes to write 2nd edition, they'll have all the time they really need to give us the best Bound/Sin-Eaters the WoD isccapable of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T09:09:07-07:00","id":434118,"title":"","content":"I really hope so especially since Geist got the royal shaft during the transition time from White Wolf to Onyx Path. Only 1 supplement book to its name despite all of the potential it has. That, and the Geist core has numerous errors that were never able to be addressed beyond a sort of version 1.1 release of the book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5284-sanaelar","name":"Sanaelar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5284_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T22:25:32-07:00","id":435280,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest impediment is lack of a developer. For Dark Eras, Onyx Path went with McFarland's wife to take up the Geist section. As far as I know, she doesn't have experience developing something as massive as Geist 2.0 would have to be. The usual developers have their hands full for some time. I'm not even sure they have any interest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T23:53:28-07:00","id":435389,"title":"","content":"I hope Geist does get a 2nd ed, though I imagine it will be a couple of years at the very least before any serious strides are made in that direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:07:31-07:00","id":435785,"title":"","content":"We'd have to keep buying books in the meantime, with the quality of what's come out so far though that's not a problem for me.<br /> <br /> I assumed Baron would be writing for Geist though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:27:52-07:00","id":436050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=435389#post435389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope Geist does get a 2nd ed, though I imagine it will be a couple of years at the very least before any serious strides are made in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>It will probably be next year. They have so far schedule 2 per year(Werewolf and Mage were supposed to come out last year If I'm not mistalen), so I'm pretty hopeful that 2016 will be the year of Hunter and Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:46:26-07:00","id":436059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=436050#post436050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It will probably be next year. They have so far schedule 2 per year(Werewolf and Mage were supposed to come out last year If I'm not mistalen), so I'm pretty hopeful that 2016 will be the year of Hunter and Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it follows the established pattern, we'll know by some time in early August.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T20:12:12-07:00","id":436604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=436059#post436059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it follows the established pattern, we'll know by some time in early August.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm very curious about who they would choose to be the developer as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T22:48:54-07:00","id":436750,"title":"","content":"Hard to say without even knowing if they will release a new line next year or not. Assuming his wife enjoyed her experience, my guess is McFarland. Bailey needs to work on Mars, and everything else she will do. Hill is a possibility. I think it would be easier to guess who the writers might be. &gt;.&gt; Samedi","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T20:26:55-08:00","id":763709,"title":"","content":"I also hope that Geist gets a new edition. I think there will be some significant changes to it - the stuff I've read about Ghosts in the GMC really gives me the impression that 2nd edition Ghosts are a bit different than in 1e. It just appears they have backed away a bit from the idea that all ghosts are on autopilot without Sin-Eater plasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9255-docsteve2020","name":"DocSteve2020","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T20:50:58-08:00","id":763723,"title":"","content":"It's more or less a matter or time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T21:01:16-08:00","id":763726,"title":"","content":"Yes, it will, along with &quot;Hunter the Vigil&quot; if I understood the White Wolf writers at Gencon correctly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T00:09:47-08:00","id":763822,"title":"","content":"Hunter is already on the list; no real doubts about that. I still keep my fingers crossed that things will go smoothly and we'll get sin-eater 2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T00:29:03-08:00","id":763831,"title":"","content":"...I'm confused. Didn't CCP sell WW to Paradox a week ago. Onyx Path may well have been planning to do so, but they need to confirm they are allowed to do so.<br /> <br /> Given the personal history of the people involved, I think the worst case scenario may be that only the books already with contracted authors/writers will be finished. Geist 2nd edition is not currently in development so it does not pass my pessimistic opinion. However, the conversations between Paradox &amp; OP is still ongoing. We won't know anything for certain until it is over. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm very much looking forward to Geist 2nd Edtion featuring the _______ Chronicles. If we are lucky, we may see some early open development Dec 2016/Jan 2017.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T09:04:44-08:00","id":764115,"title":"","content":"I will preface this with, &quot;I hereby acknowledge I am horribly biased and not at all impartial.&quot; But I would be very happy to see the Baroness snap up main writing for Geist the Sin-Eaters 2e. After having played under her for 5 years in The Balance of Shadows, a 5-shot Monster Mash with Sin-Eaters, and numerous other games with and without Geists, I can say that her time is more than due. I also don't feel terribly bad in saying that it might be worth adding similar comments if you agree. As was mentioned above, the &quot;usual&quot; writers are a little busy right now and the Baroness has a proven (documented here even) track record of great plots and ideas. So yes please, bring on the 2e Sin-Eaters. And I'll wave my Jolly Nerak Flag atop my pirate ship manned by a skeletal crew all the way to Davie Jones' Locker!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":2668,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","user":"Asmenedas","date":".  Feud with Autocorrect 11-12-2015, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T09:10:43-08:00","id":764117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=763831#post763831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I'm confused. Didn't CCP sell WW to Paradox a week ago. Onyx Path may well have been planning to do so, but they need to confirm they are allowed to do so.<br /> <br /> Given the personal history of the people involved, I think the worst case scenario may be that only the books already with contracted authors/writers will be finished. Geist 2nd edition is not currently in development so it does not pass my pessimistic opinion. However, the conversations between Paradox &amp; OP is still ongoing. We won't know anything for certain until it is over.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm very much looking forward to Geist 2nd Edtion featuring the _______ Chronicles. If we are lucky, we may see some early open development Dec 2016/Jan 2017.</div> </div> </div> </div>So far it seems like everything Onyx Path had a plan for is going ahead.<br /> <br /> Putting that aside, I say again, I feel confident it's a matter of time. I have no real idea though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:55:11-08:00","id":764320,"title":"","content":"I'm just going to keep saying that there will be Geist 2E until there is. I have no other alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T23:41:47-08:00","id":764748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=764117#post764117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far it seems like everything Onyx Path had a plan for is going ahead.<br /> <br /> Putting that aside, I say again, I feel confident it's a matter of time. I have no real idea though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have mentioned that I was responding to hellovg comment. Which was about White Wolf @ Gencon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T06:02:47-08:00","id":773027,"title":"","content":"It looks like everything that was in the works is going forward. So I believe we will see a Geist 2nd edition. Having read and followed the Balance of Shadows story I would in all honesty like to see the Baroness be given a chunk of the writing. The themes in Geist need to balance the joy of living and the sorrow of death something that the Balance of Shadows chronicle does admirable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T14:02:51-08:00","id":773410,"title":"","content":"Hopefully it'll receive a fairly major revamp. Of all of the nWoD games it has the biggest identity crisis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T15:51:42-08:00","id":773483,"title":"","content":"I keep seeing that Geist has an identity crisis, and lists of what stories you can't tell. Which to be honest I don't understand. Example: You can't tell mysteries with Geist.<br /> Of course you can in my planned chronicle the players will be introduced to a problem brought to them by a ghost. The ghost needs to have justice for her death the authorities have solved the case the killer was her boyfriend. Except the ghost insists that he is innocent. The players have only the ghost's word. How do they clear an innocent man of murder and still bring the true killer to justice. <br /> Running a Geist chronicle just takes a bit more work than Vampire or the others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:30:46-08:00","id":774405,"title":"","content":"One problem is that it doesn't know if it wants to tell Wraith stories or Hunter-like stories. The other problem is that the English usage of Geist means spirit and not ghost. One implication is that Geist should cover Claimed more broadly. <br /> <br /> Personally, if it gets a second edition then I'd like to see it hew more closely to that broader spirit aspect. If the preference is for it to be the &quot;after death&quot; game then I submit that it should be rebranded as something like Revenant: the Risen. As it stands right now, it's the only game line where you don't know what the focus of the game is just by reading the title. <br /> <br /> These matters have been discussed in other threads here. A little hunting on your part should reward you with a fuller discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:38:39-08:00","id":774408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774405#post774405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it stands right now, it's the only game line where you don't know what the focus of the game is just by reading the title.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure you do. Geists, specifically, those that bond with Sin-Eaters (much as Werewolf: the Forsaken is about werewolves, more specifically, the Forsaken variety).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T17:45:40-08:00","id":774417,"title":"","content":"What was a Geist again? Hint, they have nothing to do with real life sin-eaters.<br /> <br /> Also where's the info about this bonding thing you speak of? It's not in the title. If anything I'd guess that whatever a Geist is, it eats sins.<br /> <br /> Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Hunter, Mummy, Demon, and Beast are pretty clear on what you'll be playing. Promethean is a little harder but we do get we'll be doing something forbidden. Geist on the other hand...<br /> <br /> My guess is that the authors were being too clever (if only they had spent more time writing the game...1.0 was tragically bad) when they chose the title. They were hoping to evoke one of it's German senses (in German it means ghost as well as spirit). But in English it only means Spirit, and frankly it's one of the most esoteric English words they possibly could have chosen.<br /> <br /> So yeah. Geist has a branding problem, and compared to the other games here, a very small fanbase.<br /> <br /> The fact that it had to pillage so much material from oWoD Wraith doesn't help much either. Wraith has a huge fanbase compared to it and a nWoD Wraith would be a better gamble than revitalizing a misnamed game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-25-2015, 08:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T20:47:15-08:00","id":774515,"title":"","content":"Alright, I just want to say I try not to give the writers too much shit about 1.0. That happened during the insanity of the CCP buyout of White Wolf. I'm surprised it got out that door, and so I like to cut them some slack. It's got a lot of good ideas, and it just needs to execute them better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:24:13-08:00","id":774528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What was a Geist again?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Geist. They're in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hint, they have nothing to do with real life sin-eaters.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Vampires do with real-life vampires? Or Mages with real-life mages? It's all mythological mining.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also where's the info about this bonding thing you speak of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, in the book. It's pretty clear all through character creation, really.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Hunter, Mummy, Demon, and Beast are pretty clear on what you'll be playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not really. Vampire? So an undead who drinks blood. But Requiem contains far more than that. Werewolf? Where is the expectation of half-spirits and the Shadow coming from just that name? Mage? Where to begin. And Beast gives one <i>no</i> clue about what the heck you'll be playing as, given it is a very generic name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My guess is that the authors were being too clever (if only they had spent more time writing the game...1.0 was tragically bad) when they chose the title. They were hoping to evoke one of it's German senses (in German it means ghost as well as spirit). But in English it only means Spirit, and frankly it's one of the most esoteric English words they possibly could have chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geist. As in poltergeist. A known name for a ghost (or, rather, type of ghost). Pretty clear phonetic connections to specters there. Guess what happens when you type &quot;etymology geist&quot; into google? ghost ---&gt; geist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wraith has a huge fanbase compared to it</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really comparing it to a game that has already been out for years when it was made. Really?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774417#post774417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a nWoD Wraith would be a better gamble than revitalizing a misnamed game.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception that Geist has a distinct tone (IMHO, better), better integration (as opposed to being utterly separate from the main play area), and isn't just a tired rewash of an already existing gameline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T00:25:25-08:00","id":774581,"title":"","content":"If they made 2e Geist about spirits or a remake of Wraith I'd be rather disappointed. I really like the themes present in Geist. Enjoying life and teamwork are rather hard things to find in the world of darkness, and it stands out IMO. Giving it a spirit focus would simply step on werewolf's toes, and making it wraith would just make it generic and dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T06:18:04-08:00","id":774726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774528#post774528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Geist. They're in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good title is like a brand. I should be able to tell instantly by looking at the name what I'm being sold. Even Abrams provides logical titles for his movies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774528#post774528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Vampires do with real-life vampires? Or Mages with real-life mages? It's all mythological mining.</div> </div> </div> </div>No its all about branding. Vampire is a game about Vampires. Werewolf is a game about Werewolves. Etc. Etc. I shouldn't need to read the game book to figure out what is the game is about. This is a branding issue and one of its many problems.<br /> <br /> If it were meant to be a poltergeist game then the title would be poltergeist and the mechanics would be for poltergeists. But that isn't the case. It's not a game about specters either. It's not even really about sin-eaters (so simply false advertising there).<br /> <br /> It's a game about people who return from the dead. Geist =/= back from the dead. Geist =/= ghost (in English anyway). <br /> <br /> I don't know why people are so attached to the title anyway. I'm not arguing that a 2nd Ed. should be more or less aligned with Wraith. I'm saying that's a route that could be taken. It's not necessary though. Like Rose is rumored to, I already have a good idea for a Wraith game that dovetails nicely with this misnamed game and the other nWoD games. Whether or not it sees the light of day as a fan splat depends on a lot of factors.<br /> <br /> I digress though. Rebranding Geist for its second edition is not a bad thing. Remember that the goal of second editions is to revitalize sales. By changing the name to something more on point, like Revenant: the Risen, new players encountering the brand for the first time will easily tell what the game is about.<br /> <br /> This isn't any different than any other rebranding. Take for example, changing a school's name from something like graduate school of library and information sciences to the school of information sciences. It isn't the case that the school's mission is different or that the teachers are different or that librarians are no longer taught there. The brand is changed to promote the school's growth. Advertising to the world something that was always true. Librarians aren't the only people produced by the school. Graduate students aren't the only students taught there. Rebranding positions the school for growth.<br /> <br /> YMMV, but rebranding can do the same thing for Geist. The title should reflect what's in the book without someone having to actually read the book. <br /> <br /> All of the second editions have been quite a bit different from their first editions anyway. Just look at the role that pack plays in the new Werewolf. There's no reason to shy away from a name change if it revitalizes the game. That's my two pence anyway.<br /> <br /> I hope you consider it seriously. Without some kind of shakeup, this fanbase is likely to remain small. Try to think strategically about what will best grow the game's fanbase. Don't cling to anything that serves as a significant barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T09:49:44-08:00","id":774874,"title":"","content":"Geist does not have a branding issue. Sin-Eaters according to belief take on the sins of another to purify the person for the after life which is exactly what characters do. They help ghosts resolve issues and allow them to pass on. Geist reflects the spirit that empowers a person to perform that duty. I also imagine as the time gets closer for the 20th anniversary edition of Wraith to be released a translation guide will happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T11:52:20-08:00","id":774941,"title":"","content":"The power of Geist's branding <i>is</i> its' dissonance in correlation to its' evocation. The title does leave a question, but it is one that I haven ever seen anyone fail to seek answers for.<br /> <br /> It's not about telling you what you're doing, it's about hooking you.<br /> <br /> As contrast, consider that Mummy the Curse is theoretically super clear, but no one wants to play it because no one likes the initial image. Had it a better question title instead of an answer title, Mummy would be bigger now than it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T12:13:34-08:00","id":774955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774726#post774726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A good title is like a brand. I should be able to tell instantly by looking at the name what I'm being sold. Even Abrams provides logical titles for his movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can. It's a game about Geists and Sin-Eaters. It sounds more like a personal failure of understanding. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774726#post774726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No its all about branding. Vampire is a game about Vampires. Werewolf is a game about Werewolves. Etc. Etc. I shouldn't need to read the game book to figure out what is the game is about. This is a branding issue and one of its many problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please see above regarding names not being nearly as helpful as you seem to think. Also factor in that the game breaks uncommon, if not new, ground (as opposed to the massive footprint the big 3 have). Kinda hard to use Big Name recognition when you are essentially doing a new thing. Promethean and Beast have it far worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774726#post774726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it were meant to be a poltergeist game then the title would be poltergeist and the mechanics would be for poltergeists. But that isn't the case. It's not a game about specters either. It's not even really about sin-eaters (so simply false advertising there).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about Poltergeists. It's about Geists. As stated. Perhaps you are reading more into things?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774726#post774726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without some kind of shakeup, this fanbase is likely to remain small. Try to think strategically about what will best grow the game's fanbase. Don't cling to anything that serves as a significant barrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Geist really needs to grow is to not be a one-book-wonder tossed out the door in the middle of a change-over. Added editing and breaking out some of the material into additional books (which can afford to concentrate on the subjects in greater depth), would be improvement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T13:55:43-08:00","id":775016,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry that you disagree. But if you say Vampire to room full of people, they usually know what that means. The same is not true of Geist. It's going to be hard to sell to new players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:08:34-08:00","id":775023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774955#post774955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please see above regarding names not being nearly as helpful as you seem to think. Also factor in that the game breaks uncommon, if not new, ground (as opposed to the massive footprint the big 3 have). Kinda hard to use Big Name recognition when you are essentially doing a new thing. Promethean and Beast have it far worse.<br /> <br /> All Geist really needs to grow is to not be a one-book-wonder tossed out the door in the middle of a change-over. Added editing and breaking out some of the material into additional books (which can afford to concentrate on the subjects in greater depth), would be improvement.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few things. The powers, general underworld portion of the setting and the dualistic nature of the sin-eaters are all ripped right out of cWoD Wraith. There was nothing groundbreaking about this game.<br /> <br /> Also I'm sorry that you don't agree about names but you are wrong. Even people who do not play rpgs are going to understand that Beast: the Primordial is about primordial creatures. Geist provides no such benefits. A name like Sin-eaters: the Ridden would be more meaningful.<br /> <br /> Finally, sorry you missed it but Geist did have a sourcebook (which frankly was much better put together than the 1.0 version of the Geist). Honestly though, one shouldn't lean on supplements to do more than supplement. Everything you need to play a fulfilling game should be provided by the base rulebook.<br /> <br /> All that being said I'm pretty sure we're just talking past each other at this point. You have your position and I have mine. Will there be a second edition of this game? Hard to say. I'd rather see a nWoD take on Wraith. I don't think I'm alone. I'm way more likely to support that kickstarter than one to update this really rather imperfect game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 11-26-2015, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T14:38:24-08:00","id":775034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=775023#post775023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm sorry that you don't agree about names but you are wrong. Even people who do not play rpgs are going to understand that Beast: the Primordial is about primordial creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't about Trilobites, so it is already misleading. Beast: something animalistic. The Primordial: something really old. It's about really old animals? Nope. Nightmare monster that eat people souls and consume fear? ...I guess you <i>could</i> get tho &quot;Beast&quot; from there, but it isn't intuitive.<br /> <br /> So, no. Promethean is about Titans, or (non-metaphorically) Fire-Stealers either. Again, the name requires additional elaboration.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=775023#post775023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist provides no such benefits. A name like Sin-eaters: the Ridden would be more meaningful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, they aren't Ridden. That is a term with specific ramifications, which does not apply to the Bound.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=775023#post775023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, sorry you missed it but Geist did have a sourcebook (which frankly was much better put together than the 1.0 version of the Geist). Honestly though, one shouldn't lean on supplements to do more than supplement. Everything you need to play a fulfilling game should be provided by the base rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It had a single book. Let's compare the amount of depth and development of the other lines when limited only to their core book. Pretty much in the same boat. You have a workable game, but there is much that could be elaborated upon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=775023#post775023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that being said I'm pretty sure we're just talking past each other at this point. You have your position and I have mine. Will there be a second edition of this game? Hard to say. I'd rather see a nWoD take on Wraith. I don't think I'm alone. I'm way more likely to support that kickstarter than one to update this really rather imperfect game.</div> </div> </div> </div>nWoD Wraith wouldn't work very well. It works in oWoD because each gameline was very much entirely self contained - it could easily get away with keeping the play area predominately to its Underworld. nWoD games all use a common framework (mortal baseline, before adding supernatural template; uses the &quot;World of Darkness&quot; primarily, with additional &quot;worlds&quot; being optional add-ins), and ghost mechanics have already been established. To accurately replicate Wraith, it would basically be ignoring the rest of the world and need to build up the Underworld far more. And if you start using a mortal baseline... you pretty much have more Geist than not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T14:35:03-08:00","id":776211,"title":"","content":"The making of a <b>Wraith</b> game does not really impact <b>Geist</b> one way or the other.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are something we have some grasp of (people who came back from the dead somehow outside the Zombie or Vampire idiom) but they tend to be very different in different interpretations. One could call them &quot;Revenants&quot; I suppose, (or to be vulgar, &quot;Crows&quot; is a term I have actually heard for Sin-Eaters) but there is not a single accepted term for the concept. I'd admit &quot;Revenant: the Noun&quot; one be easy to quickly parse if one did not want to read anything about what the game is about, but there still is not a single recognizable term like Werewolf or Vampire. Even then, there can be major deviations...Look at <b>Demon: The Descent</b> or honestly either <b>Werewolf</b> game.<br /> <br /> I am always mystified by people talking about not knowing how to play a game. My <b>Changeling</b> game (which is all about adjustment to their new life, socializing, romance, dealing with loyalists), for example, is pretty different than my previous <b>Changeling</b> game (which was more directly about battling Gentry, high level politics, and exploring strange mysteries in an isolated town), and nothing like a second GM's <b>Changeling</b> game in the area (which has a lot of crossover, combat, hedge exploration, and such). Similarly, my two <b>Geist</b> games have been pretty different. Hell, <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> is a classic, and there are so many ways to play that game I always tell people running it to come to a consensus about what it is about...it can be all heavy PvP, all poltics, humanity, angst, setting mysteries, Gehenna...there is so much to do with it. <b>Requiem</b> is not dissimilar, and those three two and Changeling are some of the most successful games WW has had.<br /> <br /> Maybe Geist is not for you. That's fine. There are plenty of games, even good games, that are not for me. But that is not relevant to if it should get a 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 11-28-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T16:49:38-08:00","id":776269,"title":"","content":"<br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Geists and Werewolves share a lot of challenges in their design, but having played 2nd edition Forsaken I would love to see something like that with Sin Eaters. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">I have a controversial suggestion for a default chronicle. I would take some inspiration from Bleach. I actually hate anime, so I would want to drop a lot of the anime tropes. However bleach has a superficially similar set up. It has people who bring ghosts to the after life and they have spirits bounded to them who help them do that. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">What Bleach had was a fundamentally unjust society which was a great source of conflict throughout the show. In the &quot;Soul Society&quot;, which is an underworld/after life resembling feudal japan, a brutal caste of samurai rule over the dead and manage the flow of souls from one life to the next. Even a few of the &quot;Captains&quot; are entirely ruled by their vices. This sounds like a pretty scary dread domain ruled over by very powerful Sin Eaters, maybe the Sin Eaters are bound to service by a Kerberoi due to laws they broke. With this power they may be able to set them selves up as a Tier 2-3 organizations doling out orders and demands to Sin Eaters in the mortal world. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T01:56:18-08:00","id":776489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With this power they may be able to set them selves up as a Tier 2-3 organizations doling out orders and demands to Sin Eaters in the mortal world. </div> </div> </div>What sort of orders/demands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T06:15:27-08:00","id":776536,"title":"","content":"Kill these specific mortals (and bring me their ghosts)? End these walking crimes-against-death (vampires, mummies, etc.)? Bring me a coke with real sugar in it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T13:50:20-08:00","id":776780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=776489#post776489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of orders/demands?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well we know that anything's vice is more enjoyable in the underworld. So a Domain controlled by powerful sin eaters is going to likely be dedicated in many ways feeding their vices. This doesn't need to be a hell/inferno situation. They still have Geists and their own morals, so they may find ways to sublimate their vices into less anti-social and self destructive forms. <br /> <br /> As an example Wrath/Violence oriented Sin Eater who is old and powerful in the underworld may command less experience sin eaters in increasingly dangerous &quot;missions&quot; across the world that exist for the sake of his own urges. Another example could be a sin eater driven by lust needs you to escort prostitutes (he doesn't need to be an out and out rapist) into the underworld and won't let your Krewe do what it needs to until you do that. A Sin Eater could want to recover a set of artifacts stolen from the underworld. <br /> <br /> The next set of motivation is that of the Geists. I think we will need to see what they do with 2e to figure out what that could be. I bet the geist will have an aspiration though, so if a powerful sin eater wants to achieve that aspiration that can be a story in itself.<br /> <br /> A third motivation for the underworld nobility would be concerns of politics and ideology. Defending the underworld and its realms from interlopers, and expanding their power in the mortal world in order to do so. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T16:06:07-08:00","id":776861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another example could be a sin eater driven by lust needs you to escort prostitutes (he doesn't need to be an out and out rapist) into the underworld and won't let your Krewe do what it needs to until you do that. </div> </div> </div>Something like that sounds like nearly no Sin-Eater would ever do it and just get stuck not able to do anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T21:18:00-08:00","id":776982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=775034#post775034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> nWoD Wraith wouldn't work very well. It works in oWoD because each gameline was very much entirely self contained - it could easily get away with keeping the play area predominately to its Underworld. nWoD games all use a common framework (mortal baseline, before adding supernatural template; uses the &quot;World of Darkness&quot; primarily, with additional &quot;worlds&quot; being optional add-ins), and ghost mechanics have already been established. To accurately replicate Wraith, it would basically be ignoring the rest of the world and need to build up the Underworld far more. And if you start using a mortal baseline... you pretty much have more Geist than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the differences between oWoD Changeling and nWoD Changeling, I very much doubt that Wraith couldn't be incorporated into the larger universe alongside Geist. The underworld is very much left open for GMs to create new domains and kereboi, meaning there are a lot of places that Wraiths and their domains could be established, if far and away. That's also discounting the fact that nothing is known on what is under the oceans in the underworld - Wraith could easily be settled there.<br /> <br /> Thats said, I agree with Baroness Nerak on this - Geist and Wraith are two different entities. Just because you like one or the other doesn't mean neither of them deserve a second edition. Tonally they're completely different as well - while they both involve the underworld, Wraith is dark, depressing and pretty much all about existing in a world that would sooner see you subsumed than get closer to actually living. Geist is about bringing balance to the dead and the living however you like and simply getting to <i>live</i> again after dying - that's not to say there aren't dark or depressing moments, but the game is open for being a struggle or being about helping however one can.<br /> <br /> Heck, if you really wanted to make Wraith its own thing without disrupting Geist, then why not make it a realm <i>outside</i> death? The place where ghosts go when they are destroyed instead of being allowed to pass on? Perhaps the remnants of what is lost over time ends up in their dominion, where they reconstitute into a new being? I don't know. At least one group has tried (and is still trying) to make a nWoD Wraith fangame, so there's appeal in it, but it doesn't gather my attention given how dark the game is. If it does get made, great. If not, at least the classic game exists. I'm all for a second edition of Geist to emerge though, or discounting that a new source book. As extensive as Geists' powers are, a new manifestation or key that isn't quite as damning as the Pit or the Stygian Key would be cool (I'm all for them having a cost to get, but I love getting new powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T12:34:59-08:00","id":777300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=776982#post776982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, if you really wanted to make Wraith its own thing without disrupting Geist, then why not make it a realm <i>outside</i> death? The place where ghosts go when they are destroyed instead of being allowed to pass on? Perhaps the remnants of what is lost over time ends up in their dominion, where they reconstitute into a new being? I don't know. At least one group has tried (and is still trying) to make a nWoD Wraith fangame, so there's appeal in it, but it doesn't gather my attention given how dark the game is. If it does get made, great. If not, at least the classic game exists. I'm all for a second edition of Geist to emerge though, or discounting that a new source book. As extensive as Geists' powers are, a new manifestation or key that isn't quite as damning as the Pit or the Stygian Key would be cool (I'm all for them having a cost to get, but I love getting new powers).</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought for Wraith is that they are undead &quot;ghosts&quot; that exist in the physical world much like Strix. They exist because they refuse to accept that they died. Like Werewolves they have an integrity stat that runs the gamut between mostly human and mostly ghost. Like Prometheans they have some passive negative effect on their surroundings. Sorta like mummies they struggle with their memories (unlike mummies they don't try to remember, they try to keep from forgetting). The primary theme of the game is similar to the main theme of oWoD Wraith, accepting that you've died. As long as you can maintain your being you can avoid that acceptance and linger on (indefinitely). But there are prices.<br /> <br /> I believe that's sufficiently different from Geist.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T20:33:59-08:00","id":778081,"title":"","content":"The Wraith that I've been working on has it so they're not-quite-ghosts, not-quite-Astral. The Shadowlands are sort of a sub-realm in the Temenos with link to the Underworld, and Wraiths are people who died, but for some mysterious reason (supernatural powers, force of will, dumb luck), didn't come back quite as ghosts, but as something like a ghost, but still in full possession of their soul, personality, and capacity for growth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T02:08:53-08:00","id":790760,"title":"","content":"What kind of mechanical changes could you guys see being made to the system, specifically its powers, to fit the 2e system? Could some of the Passion powers relate to Doors rather than a bonus to a single roll (Phantasmal Oracle, I'm looking at you)? I know that Baroness Nerak considered houseruling that the Shroud, rather than giving 1/2/3/4/5 armor, instead gave 1/1/2/2/3 armor per level, as 5 armor is apparently quite a beast to fight against.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T21:47:09-08:00","id":791316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=790760#post790760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of mechanical changes could you guys see being made to the system, specifically its powers, to fit the 2e system? Could some of the Passion powers relate to Doors rather than a bonus to a single roll (Phantasmal Oracle, I'm looking at you)? I know that Baroness Nerak considered houseruling that the Shroud, rather than giving 1/2/3/4/5 armor, instead gave 1/1/2/2/3 armor per level, as 5 armor is apparently quite a beast to fight against.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, something non-controversial and constructive! In answer to your questions, yeas I'd imagine any abilities they end up deciding to keep and port over would be adapted to the various subsystems. Certainly would expect to see the Passion Key interact with the Door system, and the Oracle Manifestation interact with the Clue system to a degree.<br /> Likewise I'd expect the combat powers to be massively retweaked...<br /> <br /> At this point I'm mostly hoping that A) 2nd/Chronicle edition does happen, B) that it retains it's more distinctive elements (Krewes, Keys &amp; Manifestations*, etc) and C) that the writers/Devs are able to work comfortably and not forced to rush something unfinished out like last time.<br /> <br /> I love Geist...but it has issues, which contributed to it not doing so well from a sale point of view and it does skew the scales a tad. It is nothing against it's authors; honestly I blame the people who pushed it's production so fast. So when OP (&amp; Paradox now), gets around to it (seriously I think there is 3 games in Chronicles being released before production is set to begin, really early days here) I hope they don't just shrug and go &quot;it is not worth it&quot; because it is...if you are willing to do it right. The high quality &amp; evocative writing that is riddled throughout the corebook, despite it's flaws and premature release is proof enough of that.<br /> <br /> *Kinda paranoid that they plan on ditching the whole Key/Manifestation dynamic of the Bound's powerset. It is a cool little gimmick and I am worried that it is one of the 'too much effort' things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-22T23:35:23-08:00","id":791377,"title":"","content":"I really hope we get a 2nd Edition Geist. It was such a pity how little material we got for it in 1st Edition, but I really loved what we did get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=774941#post774941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The power of Geist's branding <i>is</i> its' dissonance in correlation to its' evocation. The title does leave a question, but it is one that I haven ever seen anyone fail to seek answers for.<br /> <br /> It's not about telling you what you're doing, it's about hooking you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately it didn't really work for me. I spent years just thinking it was probably the new world edition of Wraith and not finding anything to attract my attention. When I finally got a chance to play it, I suddenly discovered it's one of my favourite World of Darkness games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T00:22:20-08:00","id":791396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=791316#post791316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, something non-controversial and constructive! In answer to your questions, yeas I'd imagine any abilities they end up deciding to keep and port over would be adapted to the various subsystems. Certainly would expect to see the Passion Key interact with the Door system, and the Oracle Manifestation interact with the Clue system to a degree.<br /> Likewise I'd expect the combat powers to be massively retweaked...<br /> <br /> At this point I'm mostly hoping that A) 2nd/Chronicle edition does happen, B) that it retains it's more distinctive elements (Krewes, Keys &amp; Manifestations*, etc) and C) that the writers/Devs are able to work comfortably and not forced to rush something unfinished out like last time.<br /> <br /> I love Geist...but it has issues, which contributed to it not doing so well from a sale point of view and it does skew the scales a tad. It is nothing against it's authors; honestly I blame the people who pushed it's production so fast. So when OP (&amp; Paradox now), gets around to it (seriously I think there is 3 games in Chronicles being released before production is set to begin, really early days here) I hope they don't just shrug and go &quot;it is not worth it&quot; because it is...if you are willing to do it right. The high quality &amp; evocative writing that is riddled throughout the corebook, despite it's flaws and premature release is proof enough of that.<br /> <br /> *Kinda paranoid that they plan on ditching the whole Key/Manifestation dynamic of the Bound's powerset. It is a cool little gimmick and I am worried that it is one of the 'too much effort' things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if the Curse manifestation would have the &quot;take a Beat&quot; rule if the person fails to overcome it . . . or does overcome it? Unlike most manifestations, it actually has/could have legitimate conditions that could be broken if the user manages, something that you can't really lighten if you're doing it on friends. However, if you're regularly cursing your friends to make them stronger, what does that say about you from a story perspective, or them if they're inviting it?<br /> <br /> While part of me hopes we get an official 2e sometime soon/within the next two years, I'm also hoping we get something that takes its time to prove its merit rather than just to meet a demand early. Good stuff takes time and effort.<br /> <br /> That . . . is a legitimate worry. As someone who has been working on making their own custom manifestation (and a couple of keys as well), I can attest to how much work goes into making those powers both fit the key and make them stand out from one another. A variant on the 2e Mage system <i>may</i> work, though, where each manifestation did a particular thing and each key simply added their own quirks on top. However, that sounds rather more work than it'd be worth though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T00:27:45-08:00","id":791399,"title":"","content":"On Curses: I don't think they would let you spam beats/experience to your allies...if only in a sidebar &quot;Don't do this, it's stupid&quot; kind of way.<br /> <br /> <br /> On Key/Manifestations: I know...but it is something I'm hoping they will keep, against my reason. Because I feel it is too awesome to jettison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T01:39:17-08:00","id":791426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=791316#post791316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Kinda paranoid that they plan on ditching the whole Key/Manifestation dynamic of the Bound's powerset. It is a cool little gimmick and I am worried that it is one of the 'too much effort' things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they will. The first edition authors did the best job possible explaining it as a brand new concept but to manage all that while writing a new book is tough. They just can't dedicate that much time to thinking how to explain it. I think if they make a 2nd Edition, now the concept is much more familiar and I'm sure the writers will find much easier ways of getting the same information across.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T08:28:08-08:00","id":794839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=790760#post790760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that Baroness Nerak considered houseruling that the Shroud, rather than giving 1/2/3/4/5 armor, instead gave 1/1/2/2/3 armor per level, as 5 armor is apparently quite a beast to fight against.</div> </div> </div> </div>I play a vampire Hunter that became a Sin-Eater, so the ST and I had to houserule some things for sake of compatibility with 2E. This was along the lines of what I worked out. I also got a look at a draft of Mage 2E at GenCon this year and picked out something neat for protective abilities like the Shroud. In that draft's rules on Mage Armor, Arcana that could generate a physical barrier granted 1/2-Arcanum dots as armor, while those that made you a more difficult target to strike granted +Arcanum dots to Defense. <br /> <br /> So for Geist, Keys that actually generate a protective barrier, (like the Elemental Keys), you get a 1/1/2/2/3 armor rating. For Keys that make you harder to hit (Passion, Phantasmal), you get +1/+2/+3/+4/+5 to Defense (even against firearms).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T17:43:23-08:00","id":795232,"title":"","content":"Question: Has any homebrew, official, or semi-official stopgap rules been posted for easing compatibility with other 2 Edition splats on these forums or elsewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T19:55:30-08:00","id":795325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=795232#post795232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Has any homebrew, official, or semi-official stopgap rules been posted for easing compatibility with other 2 Edition splats on these forums or elsewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast's kickstarter release has some info and a rough conversion kit for players to convert 1E to 2E, but for Geist specifically I've not found one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-29T23:56:42-08:00","id":795428,"title":"","content":"I'm probably doing a conversion sometime soon in my current game. I am probably going to ignore the Integrity change, since I homebrewed geist, but I should be able to give the mechanics a pass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T22:41:22-08:00","id":810497,"title":"","content":"I wonder if they would give a more established method of making new Keys for Krewes in 2E, or if they'd expand the keys available for players? As it stands, there really isn't a set method, and given how quadratic the Keys are in regards to Manifestations it can get quite daunting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:14:43-08:00","id":813060,"title":"","content":"I think if I was developing Geist 2E, I'd mostly just refine what was there. The core premise of the game seems great, and the presentation works well for most things. Bring the Underworld into the core book as much as possible. It's been a while since I read the core book, so I don't remember how often the Sin-Eaters go therein, but I'd make the transition about as integral as the Shadow Realm is to werewolves. Kingdoms of bone and ash, rivers of blood and grave-water, etc. Whole realms lost to the Underworld, histories etched in gravestones and black towers. The Underworld is a really fantastic place (in the classical sense of the word), and I'd want to capitalize on its use as much as possible. Sin-Eaters are both at home and foreign there, one part living mortal and one part deathly spirit from the Underworld. Walk in both worlds, the duality of life and death, of forgotten remnants that linger on.<br /> <br /> Maybe have them go further at times, into the Lower Depths? That could be cool.<br /> <br /> Oh, and in the same way that packmembers can be Wolf-Blooded and even mortal now, fully playable, I'd have ghosts be part of the extended Sin-Eater &quot;family.&quot; Including being playable. They have some advantages and disadvantages over full Sin-Eaters, but it makes them unique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:25:52-08:00","id":813063,"title":"","content":"My apologies for being rather contrarian, but I'd personally love to have the Underworld be done in a proper supplement for Geist (basically like Book of the Dead, but more Geist-oriented), and leave it merely mentioned in the corebook (basically as much space as it took in 1e). Not every Geist game deals with the Underworld, and IIRC the general opinion is that it's a neat place to visit every so often but not really an irreplaceable part of the gameline. In fact, in my own Geist version, I went through the mechanics to remove the Underworld completely and I was able to do so with surprising ease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:31:12-08:00","id":813066,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's not going to happen. Sorry you feel that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:38:57-08:00","id":813074,"title":"","content":"No worries, I already did the grunt work. When 2e rolls along, we'll just convert mechanically and fix whatever breaks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:02:40-08:00","id":813118,"title":"","content":"Depends on word count, I'd guess. There are so many good points in Geist that could use expansion, picking just one is hard. There's more info on ghosts and ghost development, the Great Below, Krewe dynamics, Abmortals could use some more elaboration to really bring them out as an antagonist, and of course the standard craziness you get in Player's Guides and Storyteller's Guides.<br /> <br /> As for the Underworld, specifically, maybe focus on the Autocthonous Depth in Core, and really explore the Lower Reaches and the Dead Dominions in a supplement? Gives greater focus to the Underworld, but still leaves some mysteries for later elaboration (and page count).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:53:52-08:00","id":813340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813060#post813060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if I was developing Geist 2E, I'd mostly just refine what was there. The core premise of the game seems great, and the presentation works well for most things. Bring the Underworld into the core book as much as possible. It's been a while since I read the core book, so I don't remember how often the Sin-Eaters go therein, but I'd make the transition about as integral as the Shadow Realm is to werewolves. Kingdoms of bone and ash, rivers of blood and grave-water, etc. Whole realms lost to the Underworld, histories etched in gravestones and black towers. The Underworld is a really fantastic place (in the classical sense of the word), and I'd want to capitalize on its use as much as possible. Sin-Eaters are both at home and foreign there, one part living mortal and one part deathly spirit from the Underworld. Walk in both worlds, the duality of life and death, of forgotten remnants that linger on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think the underworld is tricky with Geist, I mean... you have to keep it disturbing and chthonic, despite the games positive attitude and themes of living life to it's fullest and moving on, and give the different domains strange esoteric rules, without making it just seem like the hedge with less plants and more skulls.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and in the same way that packmembers can be Wolf-Blooded and even mortal now, fully playable, I'd have ghosts be part of the extended Sin-Eater &quot;family.&quot; Including being playable. They have some advantages and disadvantages over full Sin-Eaters, but it makes them unique. </div> </div> </div>Well, ghosts were made playable in the last breaths of 1e.... but those don't exactly work with 2e's ghost mechanics, so having them as Weaker-Version of Splat would be cool.<br /> <br /> Personally, I hope they use influences in some way, I mean. Ghosts can be so varied, but the normal keys are rather limited to just elemental stuff and blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:41:22-08:00","id":813519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813340#post813340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the underworld is tricky with Geist, I mean... you have to keep it disturbing and chthonic, despite the games positive attitude and themes of living life to it's fullest and moving on, and give the different domains strange esoteric rules, without making it just seem like the hedge with less plants and more skulls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Well, ghosts were made playable in the last breaths of 1e.... but those don't exactly work with 2e's ghost mechanics, so having them as Weaker-Version of Splat would be cool.<br /> <br /> Personally, I hope they use influences in some way, I mean. Ghosts can be so varied, but the normal keys are rather limited to just elemental stuff and blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusingly enough, I've started planning out a dead dominion where it's mostly covered with plants that can serve as mementos (including fruit trees containing the spirits of those who broke the rules, the fruit from which can act as fetters), though the plants tend to look more like glass than normal green-matter. The rules are mostly themed around Don't Step On The Grass and Be Quiet But Not Sneaky.<br /> <br /> On track though, I think the underworld is kind of required for a game like this. Aside from Sin Eaters inherently having powers to open avernian gates, how do you have a game which deals with humans who can see and interact with ghosts as much as they do and <i>not</i> have a way to access the underworld detailed in the core book? It just fits thematically. Furthermore, I never really saw the Underworld as a different version of the Hedge. Both are threatening, dangerous and so huge one could easily get lost in them and never re-emerge, but you could say that about any shady neighborhood or subway. That doesn't make them the same. Even if not all games enter the underworld, I could probably bet that not every game of Changeling has them ever entering the Hedge again, or any supernatural going into their own inherent otherworld. Just because one group doesn't use it doesn't mean others won't, and get interesting ideas from it.<br /> <br /> As for keys, I've found them to be varied enough (in spite of my eagerness to make others). We have four elementals, a couple that deal with the human mind (passion and phantasmal), one for animals, one for manmade objects, one for ghosts or blood, and one for the darkness (stillness). Honestly, I see that as variance enough for the basics. I would like a few guidelines for making ones own keys though, or even manifestations - it's a lot of work to try and make manifestations for keys that aren't &quot;X but with a different theme&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T18:35:29-08:00","id":813805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813060#post813060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe have them go further at times, into the Lower Depths? That could be cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, the Underworld <i>is</i> a Lower Depth. That said, I would be interested to see Sin-Eaters roam the more esoteric dead places in the cosmos, not to mention a nod to the Inferno's ability to corrupt ghosts into demons. What might a Sin-Eater think if he realized how similar these demons really were to the ghost he carried?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, and in the same way that packmembers can be Wolf-Blooded and even mortal now, fully playable, I'd have ghosts be part of the extended Sin-Eater &quot;family.&quot; Including being playable. They have some advantages and disadvantages over full Sin-Eaters, but it makes them unique. </div> </div> </div>Mummy had something like this with the Lucid Dead Numen, but I don't know if that fits into G:tSE. I feel like if there was to be a minor template, it'd be some kind of Medium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:15:50-08:00","id":813826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813805#post813805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy had something like this with the Lucid Dead Numen, but I don't know if that fits into G:tSE. I feel like if there was to be a minor template, it'd be some kind of Medium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:23:26-08:00","id":813837,"title":"","content":"Lucid Dead as a Manifestation? Maybe?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:56:33-08:00","id":813855,"title":"","content":"If I were to have fully sentient undead in Geist, I'd probably go with revenants over ghosts. Something even more powerful than a ghost's Anchor, stronger even than the bond between Geist and Bound, tore them out of the Underworld and back into their bodies. They don't seem like zombies, at first glance, and some are even friendly. Can they be sent off like ghosts? Is that even a good idea? And what do they want?<br /> <br /> ...Excuse me, I have to go write something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T19:59:10-08:00","id":813858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813805#post813805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strictly speaking, the Underworld <i>is</i> a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>No more than the Shadow is. Summoning ghosts isn't accomplished by banishing any particular phenomenon from the area.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T20:21:28-08:00","id":813873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813855#post813855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to have fully sentient undead in Geist, I'd probably go with revenants over ghosts. Something even more powerful than a ghost's Anchor, stronger even than the bond between Geist and Bound, tore them out of the Underworld and back into their bodies. They don't seem like zombies, at first glance, and some are even friendly. Can they be sent off like ghosts? Is that even a good idea? And what do they want?<br /> <br /> ...Excuse me, I have to go write something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be interested in knowing if they are in any way related to the Revenants of Vampire. I've been house ruling it that they are effectively the same, but the only difference is the introduction of Vitae","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T21:08:28-08:00","id":813893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813873#post813873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be interested in knowing if they are in any way related to the Revenants of Vampire. I've been house ruling it that they are effectively the same, but the only difference is the introduction of Vitae</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, totally separate. Think &quot;The Crow&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:04:28-08:00","id":814343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=813873#post813873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be interested in knowing if they are in any way related to the Revenants of Vampire. I've been house ruling it that they are effectively the same, but the only difference is the introduction of Vitae</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond Beast all of the gamelines for Chronicles of Darkness are independent of one another. So reused terminology isn't strange at all. It's one of the reasons why I don't see a problem with rebranding &quot;Geist: the Sin-Eaters&quot; into the more easily understood &quot;Revenant: the Risen.&quot; <br /> <br /> Since my own chronicle setting is massively crossed-over I simply renamed Vampire's &quot;Revenants&quot; to &quot;Ghasts&quot; (which is totally a word that the D&amp;D monster manual writers totally invented from the word ghastly).<br /> <br /> And yeah, malonkey1's Crow analogy totally works for this game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T12:13:12-08:00","id":814353,"title":"","content":"Oh, no I totally understand that they're separate for the purposes of canon, but in my own headcanon I've had it that the same drive and passion that creates a ghostly Revenant is basically the same that induces the 'spontaneous Embrace' the only difference being the introduction of Vitae into one and not the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:45:57-08:00","id":815046,"title":"","content":"I really hope they update it for the god machine. I really love Geist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T14:01:11-08:00","id":815673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=815046#post815046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope they update it for the god machine. I really love Geist</div> </div> </div> </div>Ditto. I really want to run a game with a Beast character (even one made with the pre-kickstarter version of the game) but I can't because the two systems are mutual in their respective editions. Geist isn't available in 2E, and Beast has various powers that aren't established in 1E. Keeping Geist in its 1E state in a 2E game is just imbalanced, since it doesn't have any powers respecting doors, but the Shroud armor count make them practically walking in power armor. It's annoying. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T15:36:55-08:00","id":815725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=815673#post815673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ditto. I really want to run a game with a Beast character (even one made with the pre-kickstarter version of the game) but I can't because the two systems are mutual in their respective editions. Geist isn't available in 2E, and Beast has various powers that aren't established in 1E. Keeping Geist in its 1E state in a 2E game is just imbalanced, since it doesn't have any powers respecting doors, but the Shroud armor count make them practically walking in power armor. It's annoying. :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly, the section in beast that converts 1e games to 2e does lower how much protection armour powers gives iirc, and Sin-Eaters aren't exactly known for their social manoeuvring prowess (though I would personally add in a power for all sin-eaters that they start with a better impression than they would were they not a sin-eater).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T16:38:34-08:00","id":815754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=815725#post815725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, the section in beast that converts 1e games to 2e does lower how much protection armour powers gives iirc, and Sin-Eaters aren't exactly known for their social manoeuvring prowess (though I would personally add in a power for all sin-eaters that they start with a better impression than they would were they not a sin-eater).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is more at how Sin Eaters have certain powers that do pertain to social environments, particularly with many of the oracles (particularly Passion and Phantasmal). These give static bonuses of around 1 bonus dice per situation, which, while nice in theory, doesn't work quite as well when instead of one roll for a suggestion you make several such rolls to convince someone (unlocking a door each time). If one keeps to the &quot;one roll to convince&quot; rule of 1E, then Beasts' powers of knocking down doors doesn't have a basis. I have heard suggestions for the Shroud to make its armor count easier on the battle system, though.<br /> <br /> That said, the rule of Sin Eaters gaining a bonus with other Sin Eaters by having a complicated/large collection of mementos stands up a bit better with the doors system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T10:41:57-07:00","id":853563,"title":"","content":"Can anyone think of any kinds of merits that would be implemented in Geist 2e? It's something I've noticed about most gamelines that Geist simply doesn't have - Merits specific for Sin Eaters. I mean, there are ceremonies and mementos to pick up, but how is that different compared to, say, Tokens for Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T15:19:10-07:00","id":853705,"title":"","content":"It really depends on where the devs go with 2e. For instance, if the made the Geist/Sin-eaters relation resemble the cWoD Wraith/Shadow relationship (adjusted for Geist's completely different mood of course) that opens up all kinds of possibilities. <br /> <br /> Ghost retainers are another kinda obvious merit idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T18:58:27-07:00","id":853800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=853563#post853563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone think of any kinds of merits that would be implemented in Geist 2e? It's something I've noticed about most gamelines that Geist simply doesn't have - Merits specific for Sin Eaters. I mean, there are ceremonies and mementos to pick up, but how is that different compared to, say, Tokens for Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>From my 2e geist: revised Haunt, twilight network merits, Mentor (geist), mementos, ceremony merits, krewe merits, sin-eater fighting merits, getting influences for things relating to your threshold, threshold merits, archetype merits (like being able to spend plasm to unlock non-avernain portals if you're a bonepicker), advanced merits like the type from beast, ghost retainers, better at eating ghosts, better at Not seeing ghosts, better at opening avernian gates, better on social maneuvering ghosts, touchstone merit, heal bodies damage when you come back to life, living keystone (since anchors can be people now/must be taken at character creation), location keytone (since anchors can be locations now/must be taken at character creation).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For instance, if the made the Geist/Sin-eaters relation resemble the cWoD Wraith/Shadow relationship (adjusted for Geist's completely different mood of course) that opens up all kinds of possibilities. </div> </div> </div>What sorta possibilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-26-2016, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:15:12-07:00","id":853840,"title":"","content":"In WoD Wraith the old ideal was to have other players play your Shadow about 20% of the time. Embracing that kind of gameplay (polar opposite of Beast where you almost have two characters) would be an interesting direction. One can imagine that the Geists have there own selection of merits, etc. to choose from.<br /> <br /> Since Geist already stole the dualistic character theme from Wraith, why not embrace it. (I'd go as far as to flip the script and have the Geists be the player characters with Sin-eaters being the &quot;mortal&quot; passengers that coach the Geists through the motions of humanity.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T20:31:00-07:00","id":853847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=853840#post853840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WoD Wraith the old ideal was to have other players play your Shadow about 20% of the time. Embracing that kind of gameplay (polar opposite of Beast where you almost have two characters) would be an interesting direction. One can imagine that the Geists have there own selection of merits, etc. to choose from.<br /> <br /> Since Geist already stole the dualistic character theme from Wraith, why not embrace it. (I'd go as far as to flip the script and have the Geists be the player characters with Sin-eaters being the &amp;quot;mortal&amp;quot; passengers that coach the Geists through the motions of humanity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it wasn't hard coded into Geist 2e, Vampire 2e did have an optional rule where other players would play the vamp's Beast. I'm sure that there will at least be an optional rule for playing each other's Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:30:17-07:00","id":853880,"title":"","content":"Would you all prefer Geist 2e to be a system update that left the existing flavor largely intact and was largely the same game but cleaner, or a more drastic revision with a different feel and tone (up to and including renaming things/changing core concepts)?<br /> <br /> I'm in the latter camp, if it matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-26T21:50:27-07:00","id":853890,"title":"","content":"I don't want a drastic tonal shift, but I'd definitely want to see some concepts overhauled so they serve the intended themes better. For example, the fact that the players know the Bargain has no real muscle impacts the game's feel, even if nominally the characters don't know that. The Synergy rule changes can be a chance to give the Geist and the Bargain a bit more psychological impact on the Bound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T01:13:29-07:00","id":853936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=853840#post853840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WoD Wraith the old ideal was to have other players play your Shadow about 20% of the time. Embracing that kind of gameplay (polar opposite of Beast where you almost have two characters) would be an interesting direction. One can imagine that the Geists have there own selection of merits, etc. to choose from.<br /> <br /> Since Geist already stole the dualistic character theme from Wraith, why not embrace it. (I'd go as far as to flip the script and have the Geists be the player characters with Sin-eaters being the &quot;mortal&quot; passengers that coach the Geists through the motions of humanity.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be annoyed if that was a rule. Optional rule maybe, but as a full blown thing with merits and stuff, I'd be annoyed. I want to play my character, let other people play theirs. I'm fine with merits that are flavoured as the geist being the one who is actually getting the merit, but beyond that doesn't sound fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Would you all prefer Geist 2e to be a system update that left the existing flavor largely intact and was largely the same game but cleaner, or a more drastic revision with a different feel and tone (up to and including renaming things/changing core concepts)?</span> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I'm in the latter camp, if it matters.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Definitely first camp. If it changed from being the sort of flavour it was too much I wouldn't see much point purchasing it since IMO it'd end up just touching on the most cliche boring aspects of death. I want the themes to be transition, uncertainty and the value of life. I'm fine with renaming stuff (definitely rename manifestation to something else considering manifestations are part of the </span>ephemeral<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> rules now), tweaking flavour and shifting mechanics so they fit the themes better and just so mechanics work better in general, but the flavour is Why I want to play Geist. It is a look at death that isn't just &quot;Doom and gloom. Why are we playing this rather than the character's just </span>committing<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> suicide? This is boring.&quot;, and it's mythology and uncertainty means it can fit globally so well.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">It doesn't help that most &quot;dramatic revisions&quot; I've heard of have basically just been things that make it more Wraith, or the fact that if it is such a drastic revision why are you even calling it geist rather than making a different gameline? Doing that basically means people who don't like 1e geist are less likely to look at the game since they aren't interested in geist, and you alienate the people who like 1e geist.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want a drastic tonal shift, but I'd definitely want to see some concepts overhauled so they serve the intended themes better. For example, the fact that the players know the Bargain has no real muscle impacts the game's feel, even if nominally the characters don't know that. The Synergy rule changes can be a chance to give the Geist and the Bargain a bit more psychological impact on the Bound. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I do think synergy needs to tie much more into the geist getting another chance at experiencing it's desires, the geist needs to get more out of the </span>bargain<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">. One idea I have is that geists get three aspirations as if they were characters (rated by severity of the action), and actively going against them is a breaking point (with drastic ones giving a bonus on the breaking point, while ones that you could do easily like eat a burger from a specific place down the street or buy a cigarette lighter would have a penalty). Maybe make it so the beats you get from these aspirations can only be spent on a specific type of thing or that you can only buy new manifestations with geist beats or something.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-27-2016, 04:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T06:06:23-07:00","id":853993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=853880#post853880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you all prefer Geist 2e to be a system update that left the existing flavor largely intact and was largely the same game but cleaner, or a more drastic revision with a different feel and tone (up to and including renaming things/changing core concepts)?<br /> <br /> I'm in the latter camp, if it matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already done a full-scale rework of Geist as a homebrew thing, where I've kept most of the mechanics as-is but completely overhauled the fluff and default setting assumptions. I'd either want to see something close to what I did (for obvious reasons) or something that I can at least fully rework in a similar way to what I did.<br /> <br /> One thing I am not looking forward to when it comes to the 2e conversion is redoing the Morality analogue. I replaced Synergy with Anamnesis, and it did wonders to reinforce the fluff I was going for. Not sure how I'll convert the &quot;scale of actions that risk losing Anamnesis&quot; mechanic to the way the new Integrity analogues are being done. It's going to require quite a bit of brainstorming, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-27T08:23:51-07:00","id":854052,"title":"","content":"I think it would be wise to expect much more than a simple overhaul for Geist 2e. Just look at the differences between the 1e and 2e versions of V:tR, W:tF, M:tAw, P:tC, and C:tL (and likely H:tV too). Geist 2e is going to be a different but closely related creature to Geist 1e. Among other things, I'd expect a feature chronicle that changes everything we think we know about Sin-eaters and the world they inhabit. <br /> <br /> <b>Change. </b>I'd get used to it. It's the whole idea behind making a 2e. IMO, that's a good thing. Without change it'd just be the same old same old, in which case why not just stick to 1.1e?<br /> <br /> @milov3 I'm sorry you find that annoying but it would be a novel mechanic and would bring an all-new cooperative aspect to RPG's (or at least to CofD RPG's). You don't have to like all of a game's rules to like the game. As for optionality, all CofD games are sandbox games. <i>All</i> of the rules are optional ones. You don't like Disciplines? Use Dread Powers or Numena or even homebrewed Merits. Don't like Harmony? Don't use it. Don't like Gnosis? Don't use it. Etc., etc. The rules in the book are designed to help you get the game onto your table. But like plans they don't have to survive contact with the &quot;enemy&quot; (i.e., the troupe). Always, always, use the tools that you want to use to tell the stories that you want to tell. Doing anything else would just be a glorified live action video game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T00:20:19-07:00","id":854378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=854052#post854052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@milov3 I'm sorry you find that annoying but it would be a novel mechanic and would bring an all-new cooperative aspect to RPG's (or at least to CofD RPG's). You don't have to like all of a game's rules to like the game. As for optionality, all CofD games are sandbox games. <i>All</i> of the rules are optional ones. You don't like Disciplines? Use Dread Powers or Numena or even homebrewed Merits. Don't like Harmony? Don't use it. Don't like Gnosis? Don't use it. Etc., etc. The rules in the book are designed to help you get the game onto your table. But like plans they don't have to survive contact with the &quot;enemy&quot; (i.e., the troupe). Always, always, use the tools that you want to use to tell the stories that you want to tell. Doing anything else would just be a glorified live action video game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware, I mean I'm a homebrewer. If I didn't know tabletop games are easy to change and warp to my groups preferences after spending years altering the rules of games so they fit my groups preferences, that'd be rather strange. :P<br /> <br /> I was simply stating my view on your suggestion. Simply disliking someone elses suggestion doesn't mean I am not aware of the basics of tabletop gaming. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Among other things, I'd expect a feature chronicle that changes everything we think we know about Sin-eaters and the world they inhabit. </div> </div> </div>Is there even a thing we know in Geist? The whole thing is 80% contradictory :P<br /> hmm.... maybe that's the thing. Something tied to the laws of the Underworld that enforces a sort of law and &quot;This is the correct way&quot; directly opposed to the sin-eater method of &quot;Everything is true, yes even that stuff that cannot be truth if this other thing is true&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T09:52:12-07:00","id":854522,"title":"","content":"I'm in the first camp too. I'd expect some change, especially to deal with Sin-Eaters and cultural appropriation, but ultimately I'd like to see the game remain much the same, just tightened up and more internally consistent. We shall see though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:21:09-07:00","id":854537,"title":"","content":"I'm in the second camp as the first camp's needs could simply be addressed via a Mortal Remains kind of book. But I've been in camp 2 all along so...no surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T10:36:24-07:00","id":854545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=854522#post854522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in the first camp too. I'd expect some change, especially to deal with Sin-Eaters and cultural appropriation</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the thing that I'd like to see most is a proportionately lower emphasis on the cultural tendencies of the modern Bound as a general phenomenon, because that's demonstrably warped the perception a distressing number of people have of how Sin-Eaters work, and seeing examples of the older specimens kills two birds with one stone by possibly providing example conspiracy-level characters and showing that ritual pragmatism is not mutually exclusive with a coherent metaphysical perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T16:31:04-07:00","id":854726,"title":"","content":"For individuals who are in the second camp, what themes would they change? I mean, saying &quot;I want change&quot; is fine, but what do you hope the dev's change it towards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:16:55-07:00","id":854811,"title":"","content":"IIRC, Synergy is being handled like Harmony, where you try to balance your human side with the Geist. I think that'd give the Bargain and Geister more teeth and in game meaning. It also seems to fit the definition of Synergy better than the 1e version. I'd think Touchstones would fit also, with the Geists side as the Keystone, while the human side would be Anchor-like, a human, place, or thing that was important in life and helps provide unfinished business. I'm not sure if I'd like Virtue and Vice, or a mechanic describing the human personality and the geist's personality. I completely agree Archetype and especially Threshold based Merits like in Vampire and Werewolf. Those add so much flavor. Merits can dial up or down the ghostiness or the humanity. Thresholds need more crunch, more presence in the game. Also, I hope they're less shy about how hard to kill Sin-eaters. Having been storytelling Mummy for a bit, sin-eater resurrection seems like a reeeeeeeally bad deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:39:39-07:00","id":855327,"title":"","content":"I personally don't like the way Geists are depicted currently. I generally don't enjoy roleplaying things that are too amoral, alien or inhuman. It's hard for me to find them relatable, so I just don't deal with them. If I were to play a Sin-Eater as-is, I'd probably make my Geist either more like a normal ghost, so that my character has a relatable foil to interact with, or just make them very bland and never mention them again.<br /> <br /> I'd also personally want Sin-Eaters to be properly undead, instead of this &quot;death-touched living&quot; state (I'd use that for a minor template instead). It'd be good to play an undead character that has such different themes from Mummy, Vampire or Promethean.<br /> <br /> I'd also want Sin-Eaters to have more things to do that don't relate to the dead. I'd like to see more appeal for dealing with mortals and their issues, balancing them with the matters of the dead.<br /> <br /> I don't expect this to happen at all, but for my own take on Geist, I just deleted Mementos entirely. They honestly feel like clutter, both metaphorically and literally. None of my players felt the impact in the slightest, and even the Crafts-oriented character is much happier using the equipment creation rules instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:42:11-07:00","id":855329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855327#post855327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also personally want Sin-Eaters to be properly undead, instead of this &quot;death-touched living&quot; state (I'd use that for a minor template instead). It'd be good to play an undead character that has such different themes from Mummy, Vampire or Promethean.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I understand, difference does this make aside from just being even harder to kill?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I don't expect this to happen at all, but for my own take on Geist, I just deleted Mementos entirely. They honestly feel like clutter, both metaphorically and literally. None of my players felt the impact in the slightest, and even the Crafts-oriented character is much happier using the equipment creation rules instead.</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been trying to think about how to make mementos more important but they do seem rather like they were just randomly chucked in. I mean, I like keystones and things like the tattoo momentos, but all they do is minor buffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-29-2016, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T17:33:32-07:00","id":855378,"title":"","content":"Well, I feel like the Sin-Eater take on &quot;the sanctity of death&quot; is a bit hypocritical considering their circumstances (and the existence of the Revenance merit for high-tier krewes). IMO Geist should do away with that and embrace the fact that Sin-Eaters are not going to be a natural part of the life-death cycle. Being undead means Sin-Eaters are immortal by default (instead of requiring Revenance), are considered undead by supernatural effects that care about such things (such as the Death arcanum, wards against undead, anti-undead Endowments, etc.) and serve as a better reminder of their second chance than an alien voice in their heads.<br /> <br /> As for Mementos, the problem is that they are purely a fluff-inspired mechanic, and the fluff itself is very superficial. The idea of the Sin-Eater as a collector of &quot;cool stuff&quot; fits with the hedonistic fluff about second chances. The problem is that Geist takes that fluff and just doesn't do anything with it. There's no <i>purpose</i> to the second chance, because Geists are inhuman and mysterious, so their reasons are basically &quot;whatever works for the plot.&quot; If you put all the flavour together, it just gives the idea that Sin-Eaters are just random people who won the death lottery and now get cool powers, cool stuff, cool mythology and symbols, and cool places to visit. The Underworld also feels like an accessory, and that's because Sin-Eaters as a whole just don't have motivations beyond whatever the player assigns to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:30:02-07:00","id":855435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=854811#post854811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, Synergy is being handled like Harmony, where you try to balance your human side with the Geist. I think that'd give the Bargain and Geister more teeth and in game meaning. It also seems to fit the definition of Synergy better than the 1e version. I'd think Touchstones would fit also, with the Geists side as the Keystone, while the human side would be Anchor-like, a human, place, or thing that was important in life and helps provide unfinished business. I'm not sure if I'd like Virtue and Vice, or a mechanic describing the human personality and the geist's personality. I completely agree Archetype and especially Threshold based Merits like in Vampire and Werewolf. Those add so much flavor. Merits can dial up or down the ghostiness or the humanity. Thresholds need more crunch, more presence in the game. Also, I hope they're less shy about how hard to kill Sin-eaters. Having been storytelling Mummy for a bit, sin-eater resurrection seems like a reeeeeeeally bad deal.</div> </div> </div> </div> Some really good ideas here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T19:36:17-07:00","id":855437,"title":"","content":"well Giest didn't get the 2e treatment in dark eras, which is awkard because the Three Kingdoms of Darkness Chapter is a crossover between Changeling and Geist, but the Changeling parts are 2e and the Geist Parts are 1e. How is that even usable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:06:19-07:00","id":855453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855437#post855437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">well Giest didn't get the 2e treatment in dark eras, which is awkard because the Three Kingdoms of Darkness Chapter is a crossover between Changeling and Geist, but the Changeling parts are 2e and the Geist Parts are 1e. How is that even usable?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not like the divide between 1E and 2E are even that deep, and there are tools aplenty all around for those who don't want to have to balance the matter. But the two are easily playable together, in some form or fashion.<br /> <br /> Also, I would like to note that this news was made clear at the introduction of Dark Eras last year.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:16:58-07:00","id":855457,"title":"","content":"Plus, wasn't Geist one of the more potent game lines, powers wise? I remember they left 1e vampire and werewolf in the dust. They might be toe to toe with some 2e games, almost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T20:53:17-07:00","id":855472,"title":"","content":"Oh, certainly. It might not be fair to say they were overpowered, but if any splat was inproportionately overpowered in relation to their mythos, it was Sin-Eaters, and the those mof's could easily stand with 2E's jump.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Worth noting is that The Wolf and The Raven, the Viking Werewolf/Sin-eater setting, also has this 'problem'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-29-2016, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T23:42:36-07:00","id":855518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855378#post855378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I feel like the Sin-Eater take on &quot;the sanctity of death&quot; is a bit hypocritical considering their circumstances (and the existence of the Revenance merit for high-tier krewes). IMO Geist should do away with that and embrace the fact that Sin-Eaters are not going to be a natural part of the life-death cycle. Being undead means Sin-Eaters are immortal by default (instead of requiring Revenance), are considered undead by supernatural effects that care about such things (such as the Death arcanum, wards against undead, anti-undead Endowments, etc.) and serve as a better reminder of their second chance than an alien voice in their heads.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it'd be abit strange if Sin-Eaters couldn't grow old with the person they love... Chronicles of Darkness Immortality sounds too bleak for a game about Second Chances. Also, I'm not sure how it'd be a reminder of their second chance since you're now a zombie... You can't digest things, have kids, take drugs, etc. etc. How is it a second chance at life, when your not alive?<br /> <br /> Though I do definitely agree that the world should (at least in general) should view Sin-Eaters as something that shouldn't exist and are not part of the proper cycle of life and death. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Mementos, the problem is that they are purely a fluff-inspired mechanic, and the fluff itself is very superficial. The idea of the Sin-Eater as a collector of &quot;cool stuff&quot; fits with the hedonistic fluff about second chances. </div> </div> </div>What if.... Mementos actually did something like, be anchors of ghosts that you tie to yourself basically turning all mementos (outside of keystones) into an easy method of summoning that ghost? Simplifies the mechanics rather than having five different types of memento, gives them a reason to exist (since ghosts can be useful), actually fits the name rather than just calling them mementos because of memento mori.... hmm... could theoretically even allow people to do this to someones anchor before they die, making sure that they leave a ghost since not everyone does. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that Geist takes that fluff and just doesn't do anything with it. There's no <i>purpose</i> to the second chance, because Geists are inhuman and mysterious, so their reasons are basically &quot;whatever works for the plot.&quot; If you put all the flavour together, it just gives the idea that Sin-Eaters are just random people who won the death lottery and now get cool powers, cool stuff, cool mythology and symbols, and cool places to visit. The Underworld also feels like an accessory, and that's because Sin-Eaters as a whole just don't have motivations beyond whatever the player assigns to them. </div> </div> </div>I think I may have interpreted Geists as more human than you are. I think geists should be a ghost who has had bits and pieces of themselves replaced by the concepts of their two Keys. If they are completely inhuman and mysterious, then I'd agree their would be no purpose to the second chance which does sound rather dull.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T04:01:28-07:00","id":855607,"title":"","content":"I'd second keeping Sin-Eaters in that weird state of &quot;alive, but touched by death&quot; giving them really strange interactions with anti-undead things. Being alive is an important part of the whole Bargain and Second Chances package.<br /> <br /> As for RPing the Geist, I think the best bet is to keep in mind that Geists are ghost <i>and</i> something more/else. STs can use that to throw curveballs - when characters/Players think they have a handle on their Geist, you can always use the &quot;inhuman motivation&quot; reason to shake things up. Or the opposite. You can also take human motivations to inhuman degrees, or take inhuman features and give them human quirks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T07:08:25-07:00","id":855674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855378#post855378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I feel like the Sin-Eater take on &quot;the sanctity of death&quot; is a bit hypocritical considering their circumstances (and the existence of the Revenance merit for high-tier krewes). IMO Geist should do away with that and embrace the fact that Sin-Eaters are not going to be a natural part of the life-death cycle. Being undead means Sin-Eaters are immortal by default (instead of requiring Revenance), are considered undead by supernatural effects that care about such things (such as the Death arcanum, wards against undead, anti-undead Endowments, etc.) and serve as a better reminder of their second chance than an alien voice in their heads.<br /> <br /> As for Mementos, the problem is that they are purely a fluff-inspired mechanic, and the fluff itself is very superficial. The idea of the Sin-Eater as a collector of &quot;cool stuff&quot; fits with the hedonistic fluff about second chances. The problem is that Geist takes that fluff and just doesn't do anything with it. There's no <i>purpose</i> to the second chance, because Geists are inhuman and mysterious, so their reasons are basically &quot;whatever works for the plot.&quot; If you put all the flavour together, it just gives the idea that Sin-Eaters are just random people who won the death lottery and now get cool powers, cool stuff, cool mythology and symbols, and cool places to visit. The Underworld also feels like an accessory, and that's because Sin-Eaters as a whole just don't have motivations beyond whatever the player assigns to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are among the reasons I've been a proponent of rebranding Geist into something like Revenant: the Risen. IMO the whole second chances thing is a bit overwrought.<br /> <br /> What might actually be helpful is if the big 2e version of Geist wait until we get a proper CofD Wraith game. In fact I wouldn't be sad if Wraith and Geist were paired up and shared some antagonists. A &quot;cool&quot; idea (people's mileage will vary here) is if they shared a rulebook a la one of those old double sided SF/Fantasy paperbacks you sometimes saw back in the '70s. On one side is Wraith on the other is Geist (or Revenant), it'd have to be as thick the M20 rulebook but hey, almost everyone gets what they want (obviously they'd be separate PDFs).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T10:44:17-07:00","id":855783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855518#post855518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it'd be abit strange if Sin-Eaters couldn't grow old with the person they love... Chronicles of Darkness Immortality sounds too bleak for a game about Second Chances. Also, I'm not sure how it'd be a reminder of their second chance since you're now a zombie... You can't digest things, have kids, take drugs, etc. etc. How is it a second chance at life, when your not alive?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO it'd emphasise the entire point of second chances even more. It shouldn't be a second chance to have fun and not do anything of consequence with your new life, that's the entire problem with Geist as-is. It's got this huge &quot;THIS IS YOUR SECOND CHANCE, NOW TAKE IT!&quot; motif, but it doesn't give the player any sense of urgency or motivation. Geist is not the story of a revenant that comes back to avenge her own murder, or single dad that comes back to keep his child safe until adulthood, or any of the classic second chance stories.<br /> <br /> Geist's overall theme is more about winning the lottery than defying death because something just matters that much to you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855518#post855518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I do definitely agree that the world should (at least in general) should view Sin-Eaters as something that shouldn't exist and are not part of the proper cycle of life and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. IMO the fact that they should not exist gives even more weight to the second chance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855518#post855518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if.... Mementos actually did something like, be anchors of ghosts that you tie to yourself basically turning all mementos (outside of keystones) into an easy method of summoning that ghost? Simplifies the mechanics rather than having five different types of memento, gives them a reason to exist (since ghosts can be useful), actually fits the name rather than just calling them mementos because of memento mori.... hmm... could theoretically even allow people to do this to someones anchor before they die, making sure that they leave a ghost since not everyone does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, maybe this is me, because I default to crossovers unless I just don't play the gameline at all, but I am rather bored of &quot;magical item&quot; mechanics. Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Hunter and the blue book series all have different rules for magical items of different types. I just do not want to bother with yet another class. Besides, even if they were super useful, there's no reason I couldn't just borrow the mechanics from another gameline, or use the blue books that deal with that (1e had Reliquary and the core book, 2e has item creation rules in the core book).<br /> <br /> Unless the entire point of a gameline revolves around items, they end up as clutter mechanics more often than not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855518#post855518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I may have interpreted Geists as more human than you are. I think geists should be a ghost who has had bits and pieces of themselves replaced by the concepts of their two Keys. If they are completely inhuman and mysterious, then I'd agree their would be no purpose to the second chance which does sound rather dull.</div> </div> </div> </div>The feel I got from the fluff was that Geists were alien entities with incomprehensible personalities and motives because they themselves don't remember who they are anymore. It's like an amnesiac who has based their identity on a title/archetype.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be more powerful for Geist (and it would fit their lighter mood) if Sin-Eaters brought themselves back from the dead somehow, instead of just tickling some alien entity's fancy. It'd make the second chances theme really stand out and take center stage. This is, not coincidentally, exactly what I did for my own rework of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855674#post855674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are among the reasons I've been a proponent of rebranding Geist into something like Revenant: the Risen. IMO the whole second chances thing is a bit overwrought.<br /> <br /> What might actually be helpful is if the big 2e version of Geist wait until we get a proper CofD Wraith game. In fact I wouldn't be sad if Wraith and Geist were paired up and shared some antagonists. A &quot;cool&quot; idea (people's mileage will vary here) is if they shared a rulebook a la one of those old double sided SF/Fantasy paperbacks you sometimes saw back in the '70s. On one side is Wraith on the other is Geist (or Revenant), it'd have to be as thick the M20 rulebook but hey, almost everyone gets what they want (obviously they'd be separate PDFs).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would support this sort of thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T12:12:50-07:00","id":855873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855783#post855783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The feel I got from the fluff was that Geists were alien entities with incomprehensible personalities and motives because they themselves don't remember who they are anymore. It's like an amnesiac who has based their identity on a title/archetype.<br /> <br /> I think it'd be more powerful for Geist (and it would fit their lighter mood) if Sin-Eaters brought themselves back from the dead somehow, instead of just tickling some alien entity's fancy. It'd make the second chances theme really stand out and take center stage. This is, not coincidentally, exactly what I did for my own rework of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about a hybrid of this and the old? The Sin-Eater fought their way (back) to the gates of the Underworld on their own merit, and such a fight prompted the Geist to offer their Bargain? It isn't because Geists need to make them, or they were bored, the character <i>earned</i> it. But the Geist component still explains the power-set, and why you didn't simply end up as a ghost (I'd relegate Rank 2, or even 3, Ghosts as those who made the same fight, but didn't get a Bargain).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T14:44:31-07:00","id":856022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855873#post855873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about a hybrid of this and the old? The Sin-Eater fought their way (back) to the gates of the Underworld on their own merit, and such a fight prompted the Geist to offer their Bargain? It isn't because Geists need to make them, or they were bored, the character <i>earned</i> it. But the Geist component still explains the power-set, and why you didn't simply end up as a ghost (I'd relegate Rank 2, or even 3, Ghosts as those who made the same fight, but didn't get a Bargain).</div> </div> </div> </div>When I did my rework, I was expecting to have to do A LOT of work to replace all the mentions of Geists, but it was way easier than I thought. Geists just don't have that much of an impact in the game. You could easily get rid of them with minimal effort, as I did, and end up with a way more powerful narrative. Besides, the foreboding devil over your shoulder has IMO been done better by gamelines like Vampire, Beast, Werewolf and arguably Mage (if you choose to take &quot;the Supernal&quot; as the supernatural force pervading your perceptions and taking up much of your thought).<br /> <br /> Though your proposal is leagues better than what we have in the game currently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:12:39-07:00","id":856035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=855783#post855783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IMO it'd emphasise the entire point of second chances even more. It shouldn't be a second chance to have fun and not do anything of consequence with your new life, that's the entire problem with Geist as-is. It's got this huge &quot;THIS IS YOUR SECOND CHANCE, NOW TAKE IT!&quot; motif, but it doesn't give the player any sense of urgency or motivation. Geist is not the story of a revenant that comes back to avenge her own murder, or single dad that comes back to keep his child safe until adulthood, or any of the classic second chance stories.<br /> <br /> Geist's overall theme is more about winning the lottery than defying death because something just matters that much to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except you're not meant to be a revenant. You're a psychopomp.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, maybe this is me, because I default to crossovers unless I just don't play the gameline at all, but I am rather bored of &quot;magical item&quot; mechanics. Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Hunter and the blue book series all have different rules for magical items of different types. I just do not want to bother with yet another class. Besides, even if they were super useful, there's no reason I couldn't just borrow the mechanics from another gameline, or use the blue books that deal with that (1e had Reliquary and the core book, 2e has item creation rules in the core book). </div> </div> </div>I sorta like the magic item mechanics as long as they are different enough. These should be rather different (at least IMO, it might not be enough for you) since it's not as much a magic item as much as simply a really strong anchor that you can use. I mean, you could have a memento sword, but it wouldn't do anything special that a memento coin couldn't do. The item isn't something being enchanted, the anchor's just getting a stronger tie with the ghost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The feel I got from the fluff was that Geists were alien entities with incomprehensible personalities and motives because they themselves don't remember who they are anymore. It's like an amnesiac who has based their identity on a title/archetype. </div> </div> </div>Since it's effectively ghost + spirit in 1e, I got a more half-way impression rather than 100% alien.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it'd be more powerful for Geist (and it would fit their lighter mood) if Sin-Eaters brought themselves back from the dead somehow, instead of just tickling some alien entity's fancy. It'd make the second chances theme really stand out and take center stage. This is, not coincidentally, exactly what I did for my own rework of the game. </div> </div> </div>Well, sin-eaters can only be made from specific people, so I could see something like that tied in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T15:46:54-07:00","id":856044,"title":"","content":"Being a psychopomp might be the intention for what Sin-eaters do after they come back. Functionally though, their origins are much closer to revenants. These being the Chronicles of Darkness and personal horror being an aspect of each of the games, I find the revenant part of their nature way more engaging than weird carnival thing that much of the game focuses on. I also personally think that psychopomps kinda work better as a minor template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 03-30-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T16:13:15-07:00","id":856060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856035#post856035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except you're not meant to be a revenant. You're a psychopomp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except there's not really a reason to do that. The Archetypes are so varied that being a psychopomp is only a minority of what different Sin-Eaters do. Furthermore, it doesn't tie in with the Geist origin at all. Why would Geists want the person they hitched a ride with dedicate their limited time to being a psychopomp? I can sorta get the whole &quot;party like it's Dia de los Muertos&quot; vibe for Geists that want to experience what it's like to be alive again, but even that motivation is very weak.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856035#post856035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sorta like the magic item mechanics as long as they are different enough. These should be rather different (at least IMO, it might not be enough for you) since it's not as much a magic item as much as simply a really strong anchor that you can use. I mean, you could have a memento sword, but it wouldn't do anything special that a memento coin couldn't do. The item isn't something being enchanted, the anchor's just getting a stronger tie with the ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I vastly prefer the anchor rules to be the way they are (that is, People/Places/Objects), rather than being reduced to special items with yet another system. I agree that expanding upon the qualities and characteristics of Anchors is an interesting thing to do, but IMO mementos are just purposeless. If you want a system for history-infused objects, you already have better things in other gamelines (I think Mummy deals with that sort of thing as well?).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856035#post856035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since it's effectively ghost + spirit in 1e, I got a more half-way impression rather than 100% alien.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think spirits are less alien than Geists. At least spirits have understandable, sometimes even predictable, motivations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856035#post856035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sin-eaters can only be made from specific people, so I could see something like that tied in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually prefer that the &quot;specific people&quot; are people who are strong-willed or motivated enough, rather than &quot;they possessed something that appealed to some alien entity.&quot; It lessens the &quot;winning the lottery&quot; aspect I dislike about Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T18:30:20-07:00","id":856134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856044#post856044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a psychopomp might be the intention for what Sin-eaters do after they come back. Functionally though, their origins are much closer to revenants. These being the Chronicles of Darkness and personal horror being an aspect of each of the games, I find the revenant part of their nature way more engaging than weird carnival thing that much of the game focuses on. I also personally think that psychopomps kinda work better as a minor template.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sincere question, not intended to sound rude but I'm 100% it will sound rude but I cannot think of a different way to ask. What do you like about 1e Geist? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856060#post856060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except there's not really a reason to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that needs to be fixed. Since it's the Intent, but mechanics don't give you any incentive to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Archetypes are so varied that being a psychopomp is only a minority of what different Sin-Eaters do. </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I think archetypes are too varied. I mean, one is &quot;I should be dead&quot;.... why would they make the bargain in the first place? Removing archetypes that are bloat, and go against the themes would be a good change for 2e IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, it doesn't tie in with the Geist origin at all. Why would Geists want the person they hitched a ride with dedicate their limited time to being a psychopomp? I can sorta get the whole &quot;party like it's Dia de los Muertos&quot; vibe for Geists that want to experience what it's like to be alive again, but even that motivation is very weak. </div> </div> </div>Geists wanting to exist seems to be the primary reason for their origin considering them seem to want to do anything to stay out of the underworld (though I do think it's weird they made a plane of existence for geist and then went &quot;If you go there, your geist will dislike it to the extent you might lose synergy&quot;).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I vastly prefer the anchor rules to be the way they are (that is, People/Places/Objects), rather than being reduced to special items with yet another system. I agree that expanding upon the qualities and characteristics of Anchors is an interesting thing to do, but IMO mementos are just purposeless. If you want a system for history-infused objects, you already have better things in other gamelines (I think Mummy deals with that sort of thing as well?). </div> </div> </div>I think you've misunderstood my intent. This wouldn't be change to the anchor rules, it would be a sin-eater is able to take an anchor infuse it with your psyche, strengthening it so that you can summon the ghost to that anchor when put a bit of plasm into it. Simple, quick, doesn't clutter things, just a merit or two of space in the book, and &quot;should&quot; fit with the themes of the game better than 1e mementos (YMMV).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually think spirits are less alien than Geists. At least spirits have understandable, sometimes even predictable, motivations. </div> </div> </div>I think we'll have to agree to disagree on the topic of how alien Geists are since this is just going around in circles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I actually prefer that the &quot;specific people&quot; are people who are strong-willed or motivated enough, rather than &quot;they possessed something that appealed to some alien entity.&quot; It lessens the &quot;winning the lottery&quot; aspect I dislike about Geist. </div> </div> </div>The issue with that is that it means to play a Sin-Eater you must have x attribute at y level, meaning less character options. Especially since it means you cannot play a weak-willed sin-eater who basically does whatever there geist demands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:24:54-07:00","id":856202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I think archetypes are too varied. I mean, one is &quot;I should be dead&quot;.... why would they make the bargain in the first place? Removing archetypes that are bloat, and go against the themes would be a good change for 2e IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, when I was working out Archetype Tilts, a take on Mourners that I find... acceptable, if not desirable is less &quot;I should be dead&quot; and more &quot;I recognize that I died, and nothing will be the same again&quot;. Still kinda hollow for a motivation, but there you have it. They'd be more likely to hang around ghosts than the living. Not like Advocates who want to help ghosts. No, ghosts are the Mourner's &quot;people&quot;. And other undead, I suppose (nevermind that the Mourner themself is not actually undead. Kinda).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists wanting to exist seems to be the primary reason for their origin considering them seem to want to do anything to stay out of the underworld (though I do think it's weird they made a plane of existence for geist and then went &quot;If you go there, your geist will dislike it to the extent you might lose synergy&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it more as &quot;the Geist wants to experience <i>life</i>, and doesn't like the reminder of the Great Below.&quot; Is it weirdly contradictory, considering the requirements of high Psyche? Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with that is that it means to play a Sin-Eater you must have x attribute at y level, meaning less character options. Especially since it means you cannot play a weak-willed sin-eater who basically does whatever there geist demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>A drive to fight for life need not require strong Willpower (the stat), merely a compelling enough reason. The character could be a complete doormat, normally, but whatever offed them that first time hit just the right buttons to trigger their drive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T20:29:55-07:00","id":856205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think that needs to be fixed. Since it's the Intent, but mechanics don't give you any incentive to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, it doesn't fit the &quot;second chance&quot; flavour either. When I think &quot;psychopomp&quot;, I think &quot;medium&quot; or a religious type (either a priest figure or an angel-type).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I think archetypes are too varied. I mean, one is &quot;I should be dead&quot;.... why would they make the bargain in the first place? Removing archetypes that are bloat, and go against the themes would be a good change for 2e IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of Geist's main problems was a lot of cool ideas that sorta vaguely fit the same general fluff and were thrown in, so we ended up with a very unfocused product. The disparate Archetypes really eroded any sense of meaning or purpose in the &quot;second chance&quot;. So yes, that would be a good change.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists wanting to exist seems to be the primary reason for their origin considering them seem to want to do anything to stay out of the underworld (though I do think it's weird they made a plane of existence for geist and then went &quot;If you go there, your geist will dislike it to the extent you might lose synergy&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with Geists wanting to exist is that it doesn't explain why they're picky at all with their subjects. Even if things don't work out, they can always just abandon them or go full Wretched and not give a fuck. Clearly Geists have other goals, which is why they can afford to be selective about the way they do things.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I've literally never used the Underworld and I've deleted it from my take on Geist with surprisingly minimal effort. Again, the Underworld just does not interact with Geist as much as you'd think. As a place to visit, I just can't see the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you've misunderstood my intent. This wouldn't be change to the anchor rules, it would be a sin-eater is able to take an anchor infuse it with your psyche, strengthening it so that you can summon the ghost to that anchor when put a bit of plasm into it. Simple, quick, doesn't clutter things, just a merit or two of space in the book, and &quot;should&quot; fit with the themes of the game better than 1e mementos (YMMV).</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are magic item rules I could live with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856134#post856134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with that is that it means to play a Sin-Eater you must have x attribute at y level, meaning less character options. Especially since it means you cannot play a weak-willed sin-eater who basically does whatever there geist demands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said anything about attributes, and I mentioned &quot;motivated&quot; as a potential requisite. A weak-willed sin-eater can easily be motivated by that one thing that they can't allow. Even the meekest person has their touchy issue. So long as that issue is taken care of (like the single parent that came back to make sure their kid wouldn't be an orphan), they can be as weak-willed and meek as they want, because they already got the sensitive issue out of the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:07:47-07:00","id":856223,"title":"","content":"@milo v3: What makes you think I don't like Geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-30T21:50:39-07:00","id":856252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856223#post856223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@milo v3: What makes you think I don't like Geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't technically think you don't like Geist. More I'm not sure what you do like in Geist since you seem to want nearly every major aspect of it flavor-wise changed from your posts, but you must have at least an interest in the game otherwise you wouldn't be posting in this thread, so I'm wondering about the common ground between our perspectives on the game so I can discuss ideas easier as I would rather not just be going &quot;No, I don't like your ideas&quot; over and over again in this thread... Makes me feel rather rude when I do that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:15:03-07:00","id":856396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856252#post856252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't technically think you don't like Geist. More I'm not sure what you do like in Geist since you seem to want nearly every major aspect of it flavor-wise changed from your posts, but you must have at least an interest in the game otherwise you wouldn't be posting in this thread, so I'm wondering about the common ground between our perspectives on the game so I can discuss ideas easier as I would rather not just be going &amp;quot;No, I don't like your ideas&amp;quot; over and over again in this thread... Makes me feel rather rude when I do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fair but permit me to ask a counter-question. What do you not like about Geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T05:50:04-07:00","id":856412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856396#post856396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's fair but permit me to ask a counter-question. What do you not like about Geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head; archetype bloat/going against themes, no merits, mementos not fitting the themes and being rather bland mechanically, ceremonies costing extra to make unique, that your geist is meant to be getting a second chance to experience things but there is no incentive to actually do things your geist wants, synergy being pretty bland, archetypes doing nothing, underworld being pointless, basically no merits, the krewe system is rather lacking both in the number of positions and how... well everything like group merits works, the antagonists being pretty bleh, and lack of things to actually do in the game, the name manifestations, and the fact that you can make new keys but it doesn't say how that works with the threshold system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 03-31-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T06:48:14-07:00","id":856434,"title":"","content":"Seems like we have the same problems with the game. The titular Geist really isn't a factor in the game. The primary problem is the tonal dissonance that comes from the celebratory feel of Krewes and Sin-Eaters when compared to the unfinished business and brooding death themes that Geists and the Underworld bring to the game. Much like Werewolf 2e brought all new focus on The Pack and The Hunt, I think a Geist 2e should focus on the last two things--Geists and the Underworld--and not the first two things. Now YMMV and there's no issues about that but I'll be blunt, I don't actually care that you don't like my (or anyone else's ideas). I wouldn't be posting my ideas if I agreed with yours.<br /> <br /> Now let me get to answering your initial question. First a little background: Wraith: the Oblivion is (and always has been) my favorite World of Darkness game. So when a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; came out for it in the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness, I was excited. And it is my second favorite 1e game (right after Mummy). That doesn't mean I think its a good game though. It isn't. Quality wise Geist 1.0 was barely better than the Changing Breeds blue book. Geist 1.1 really didn't make it much better, it merely made it playable. So depsite the fact that I like Geist more than most of the other 1e's, it's simply not a well put together game. It's best parts are the things it inherited from Wraith--the Underworld, Keys, Mementos, dualistic characters. All the things that sit on the Revenant rather than the Psychopomp side of its DNA.<br /> <br /> As I see it if 2e doesn't focus on the titular Geists then it should be rebranded into something like Sin-Eater: the Illuminated. A title that captures the Psychopomp aspect of Sin-Eaters. But that's also a game that doesn't need Geists or any of the baggage they bring with them. However, that might also be a boring game because psychopomps lead the dead to their rest. They're people who know things. They have answers. And that doesn't actually mesh very well with the overarching mood of the Chronicles of Darkness which is one of interwoven and nesting mysteries. Better is a game that doubles down on Geists. However, that's a game that doesn't really need Sin-Eaters except as a possible minor template or unless it wants to inherit the Psyche/Shade duality from Wraith. In the first case, it's a game that should be rebranded to something like Revenant: the Risen. In the second case we might not need to rebrand it but it becomes a game that needs some very strong mechanical teeth to fully develop the dualistic aspect of Sin-Eaters and Geists sharing one body. A mechanic that has players share characters is the best way to accomplish this.<br /> <br /> So it isn't like I have any one idea of what the 2e game should look like. I have multiple ideas based on which of the book's themes will become the focal point of 2e. You might not like any of them but the nature of 1e isn't such that it can survive as is if it goes through the 2e treatment. I put it to you, the game's title is Geist and it would be best if 2e focused on them and not Sin-Eaters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:06:24-07:00","id":856482,"title":"","content":"Hmm. One way to conceptually reconcile the more grim focus of Geists/Sin-Eaters and the celebratory Sin-Eater themes, is a similar divide with vampires. By the nature of their Beast, they are driven to selfish, predatory existence, which the Kindred counter with their &quot;veneer of humanity&quot; Covenants (in that Covenants are how vampires cope and keep from descending into Draugr). Something similar might happen with Sin-Eater society - it's a party, because otherwise there would be nothing but tears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:14:39-07:00","id":856486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856482#post856482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. One way to conceptually reconcile the more grim focus of Geists/Sin-Eaters and the celebratory Sin-Eater themes, is a similar divide with vampires. By the nature of their Beast, they are driven to selfish, predatory existence, which the Kindred counter with their &quot;veneer of humanity&quot; Covenants (in that Covenants are how vampires cope and keep from descending into Draugr). Something similar might happen with Sin-Eater society - it's a party, because otherwise there would be nothing but tears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is not an explanation for Covenants that I ascribe to. Covenants are a social (political/spiritual) divide among the Undead. They don't have anything to do with the Humanity/Touchstone mechanics (which is what prevent the slide into Draugr-hood) at all. They're more of a political or magical mini-game within the larger Vampire game.<br /> <br /> I'll be blunt and say that you can't actually reconcile death with mardi gras. Geists are entities with unfinished business. That really doesn't jive too well with &quot;let's get our hedonism on&quot;. Also, I don't really see how &quot;let's get our hedonism on&quot; relates to being a psychopomp (which is what sin-eaters supposedly are).<br /> <br /> I realize this position isn't popular with some but the game's title is &quot;Geist&quot; therefore the game should be about Geists and the thing players play should be Geists. Any other solution should be an automatic rebranding to better describe what it is you're really playing. Because it's not the case the Geist 1e was ever a game about Geists (and this has been pointed out by others).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T08:56:53-07:00","id":856508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856486#post856486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is not an explanation for Covenants that I ascribe to. Covenants are a social (political/spiritual) divide among the Undead. They don't have anything to do with the Humanity/Touchstone mechanics (which is what prevent the slide into Draugr-hood) at all. They're more of a political or magical mini-game within the larger Vampire game.<br /> <br /> I'll be blunt and say that you can't actually reconcile death with mardi gras. Geists are entities with unfinished business. That really doesn't jive too well with &quot;let's get our hedonism on&quot;. Also, I don't really see how &quot;let's get our hedonism on&quot; relates to being a psychopomp (which is what sin-eaters supposedly are).<br /> <br /> I realize this position isn't popular with some but the game's title is &quot;Geist&quot; therefore the game should be about Geists and the thing players play should be Geists. Any other solution should be an automatic rebranding to better describe what it is you're really playing. Because it's not the case the Geist 1e was ever a game about Geists (and this has been pointed out by others).</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh. I have no hold-ups regarding the name. Rebranding at this point would be bad for 2E continuity. I'd rather they just made the Geist more relevant (which it seems like everyone here wants, more or less).<br /> <br /> As to &quot;Mardi Gras&quot;: You can very well <i>distract</i> morbidity with celebration, and perhaps even silence, momentarily, the incessant drive of the Geist with the thrills of life (this is assuming Geists have such drive, which I'd hope gets made clear). As for the Sin-Eater benefit of celebration: As stated, it is choosing laughter over tears.<br /> <hr /><br /> On the topic of the Geist's drive and purpose, I'd be very happy with a similar system like with Demon's Cypher. Initially, the Geist is an archetype/Threshold driven thing, pursuing action without really understanding why. As you work with the Geist to uncover <i>its</i> history and identity, its goals (and behavior) get more personalized and focused, until at last it understands <i>why</i> it is a ghost/Geist, and has a chance to &quot;finish things&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 03-31-2016, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:39:16-07:00","id":856695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856434#post856434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like we have the same problems with the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The titular Geist really isn't a factor in the game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that should be fixed... But IMO, fixed not removed. I mean, it's not even hard to fix.... Adding geist aspirations, mentor merit, make touchstones bits of the geists life, and fixing synergy seemed to do it pretty easily<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The primary problem is the tonal dissonance that comes from the celebratory feel of Krewes and Sin-Eaters when compared to the unfinished business and brooding death themes that Geists and the Underworld bring to the game. </div> </div> </div>And here is where I mainly disagree with the problems about the game. Since I love the celebratory feel of Krewes and Sin-Eaters and definitely prefer it over the doom and gloom brood hour. I mean, IMO, Geists should be part of the celebratory of life feel rather than bringing it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now YMMV and there's no issues about that but I'll be blunt, I don't actually care that you don't like my (or anyone else's ideas). I wouldn't be posting my ideas if I agreed with yours. </div> </div> </div>I simply find that constructive discussion is better than a pointless discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now let me get to answering your initial question. First a little background: Wraith: the Oblivion is (and always has been) my favorite World of Darkness game. So when a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; came out for it in the &quot;new&quot; World of Darkness, I was excited. And it is my second favorite 1e game (right after Mummy). That doesn't mean I think its a good game though. It isn't. Quality wise Geist 1.0 was barely better than the Changing Breeds blue book. Geist 1.1 really didn't make it much better, it merely made it playable. So depsite the fact that I like Geist more than most of the other 1e's, it's simply not a well put together game. It's best parts are the things it inherited from Wraith--the Underworld, Keys, Mementos, dualistic characters. All the things that sit on the Revenant rather than the Psychopomp side of its DNA. </div> </div> </div>I'm surprised you consider the Underworld and Mementos some of the best parts of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So it isn't like I have any one idea of what the 2e game should look like. I have multiple ideas based on which of the book's themes will become the focal point of 2e. You might not like any of them but the nature of 1e isn't such that it can survive as is if it goes through the 2e treatment. I put it to you, the game's title is Geist and it would be best if 2e focused on them and not Sin-Eaters. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I do think the game should focus on geists, but sin-eater is also in the name. It should focus on both. As the morality stat suggests, synergy between the two is key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T13:55:32-07:00","id":856704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856695#post856695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised you consider the Underworld and Mementos some of the best parts of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Recall the Wraith is my favorite WoD game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856695#post856695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I do think the game should focus on geists, but sin-eater is also in the name. It should focus on both. As the morality stat suggests, synergy between the two is key.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that Synergy is the key. It's inspired by a similar mechanic from W:tO. But I disagree that sin-eater should be very important unless a much more novel 2-player or shared play mechanic is adopted. Synergy by itself isn't getting it done. And again Geist is the name. The players should be playing Geists and, at best, Sin-Eaters should be their co-pilots. It shouldn't be the other way around like it is now. YMMV<br /> <br /> Regarding celebrating death and celebratory atmosphere, it's really a personality quirk that should be left to the individual players because really, few things are as personal to us, as how we react to death. None of the people I know are ever in a celebratory mood when people they pass away. I think there are good reasons why Mark Rein*Hagen made W:tO the way he did. Geist could stand to be more somber in mood. You made a deal with a literal devil to come back from the dead. You didn't win the lottery. It is a Chronicles of <b><i>Darkness</i></b> game afterall. (IMO, another problem Geist has is that it spends all of its energy trying to be <b><i>not Wraith</i></b> and has nothing left to assert its own voice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T03:04:50-07:00","id":857602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856704#post856704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding celebrating death and celebratory atmosphere, it's really a personality quirk that should be left to the individual players because really, few things are as personal to us, as how we react to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of the issue with this is the fact that it isn't about celebrating death. It's celebrating Life. If your character doesn't have appreciation towards life... they probably shouldn't be a sin-eater....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> None of the people I know are ever in a celebratory mood when people they pass away. </div> </div> </div>So? I'm not really sure how that's relevant. This isn't a game about the people left when someone dies. This is a game more about when someone has a near death experience and has a new appreciation of life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Geist could stand to be more somber in mood. </div> </div> </div>Just what we need, a Chronicles of Darkness game with a somber mood with a focus on characters life after death. Could rebrand it to match the new theme, Vampire: The Requiem maybe -.-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You made a deal with a literal devil to come back from the dead. </div> </div> </div>This always makes me wonder... Does that change when that &quot;devil&quot; is an angel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-02-2016, 09:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T09:19:19-07:00","id":857742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857602#post857602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of the issue with this is the fact that it isn't about celebrating death. It's celebrating Life. If your character doesn't have appreciation towards life... they probably shouldn't be a sin-eater....</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no. That doesn't work for me (and I suspect others). As was already pointed out Sin-Eaters don't actually celebrate life in as much as they celebrate winning the lottery. The game should be about way more than that. They made a deal with something not alive to come back to the land of the living. A big problem with the game is 100% too much focus on the 'back to the land of the living' bit and 100% not enough focus on the 'made a deal with something not alive' part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857602#post857602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So? I'm not really sure how that's relevant. This isn't a game about the people left when someone dies. This is a game more about when someone has a near death experience and has a new appreciation of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>But didn't you say Sin-Eaters were psychopomps? See where I'm going with this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857602#post857602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just what we need, a Chronicles of Darkness game with a somber mood with a focus on characters life after death. Could rebrand it to match the new theme, Vampire: The Requiem maybe -.-</div> </div> </div> </div>That is just what we need. Because I reject the notion that Vampire is a game primarily about characters life after death. It's a game of politics and magic and faith and addiction and your inner monster, none of which are about death per se. Whereas Geist is a game about passing beyond, the underworld, ghosts, and cheating death (at a price -- which it needs more of that whole price part because right now it's free-ride city).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857602#post857602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This always makes me wonder... Does that change when that &quot;devil&quot; is an angel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Devil, angel, what's the difference? A deal was struck with something not human. The Chronicles of Darkness being what they are, the underlying intentions of that not human thing should be not good. People who come back from the dead shouldn't be partying it up like it was some asinine kegger. I don't want to play Frat-boy: the Party-Crasher any more than I want to play Care Bears: the Happy.<br /> <br /> Like I said before. Geist spends too much time trying to be <b><i>not Wraith</i></b> and not enough time thinking about what it means to come back to life with an undead monkey on your back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T15:01:23-07:00","id":857950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857742#post857742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah no. That doesn't work for me (and I suspect others). As was already pointed out Sin-Eaters don't actually celebrate life in as much as they celebrate winning the lottery. The game should be about way more than that. They made a deal with something not alive to come back to the land of the living. A big problem with the game is 100% too much focus on the 'back to the land of the living' bit and 100% not enough focus on the 'made a deal with something not alive' part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But didn't you say Sin-Eaters were psychopomps? </div> </div> </div>Yep. Turns out psychopomps deal with the dead... not the moping people who are left behind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> See where I'm going with this... </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is just what we need. Because I reject the notion that Vampire is a game primarily about characters life after death. It's a game of politics and magic and faith and addiction and your inner monster, none of which are about death per se. Whereas Geist is a game about passing beyond, the underworld, ghosts, and cheating death (at a price -- which it needs more of that whole price part because right now it's free-ride city). </div> </div> </div>You want a game about undead who have to deal with the moody depression ramifications about having being brought back from the dead with an evil alien presence inside their head that can take control of you and you can never be rid of unless you truly finally die... That's vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Chronicles of Darkness being what they are, the underlying intentions of that not human thing should be not good. </div> </div> </div>This is what I fundamentally disagree with. Why? Chronicles of Darkness is a game where everything is in shades of grey, so why can't it be good? You can play a good beast... but no you can't have a geist that isn't horrible?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People who come back from the dead shouldn't be partying it up like it was some asinine kegger. I don't want to play Frat-boy: the Party-Crasher any more than I want to play Care Bears: the Happy. </div> </div> </div>Yes... because acting like a frat boy is the only method to enjoy life or allow your geist to re-experience the joys of life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Like I said before. Geist spends too much time trying to be </span><b><i>not Wraith</i></b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> and not enough time thinking about what it means to come back to life with an undead monkey on your back</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can't say what it's like in relation to Wraith since I never played it or read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-02-2016, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T20:29:02-07:00","id":858108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=856486#post856486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is not an explanation for Covenants that I ascribe to. Covenants are a social (political/spiritual) divide among the Undead. They don't have anything to do with the Humanity/Touchstone mechanics (which is what prevent the slide into Draugr-hood) at all. They're more of a political or magical mini-game within the larger Vampire game.<br /> <br /> I'll be blunt and say that you can't actually reconcile death with mardi gras. Geists are entities with unfinished business. That really doesn't jive too well with &quot;let's get our hedonism on&quot;. Also, I don't really see how &quot;let's get our hedonism on&quot; relates to being a psychopomp (which is what sin-eaters supposedly are).<br /> <br /> I realize this position isn't popular with some but the game's title is &quot;Geist&quot; therefore the game should be about Geists and the thing players play should be Geists. Any other solution should be an automatic rebranding to better describe what it is you're really playing. Because it's not the case the Geist 1e was ever a game about Geists (and this has been pointed out by others).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to beat a point to death (pun not intended), but I think there very is something akin to reconciling death with mardi gras - it's called a Day Of The Dead celebration, where, once a year, people go and enjoy themselves in a macabre celebration. Sugar skulls, people decorated as skeletons or with bones as part of their garb, appealing to the lost and enjoying life while one has it. That is Geist in a nutshell to me; you take aspects of the dead, remember what is past and, rather than dwell on how we're all going to die, you enjoy the life you have, celebrate it, and extend those celebrations to the dead as well, because they <i>were</i> alive once. Why not spread some of that joy to those who do not have it?<br /> <br /> Also note, you don't have to go the hedonism route, and really I don't see how hedonism really factors in outside of the underworld, where the desires of someone naturally come up to the surface and keep coming up. Even the underworld doesn't really work in line with Sin Eaters, because it has that influence on literally everyone. Heck, it's why Angels and Demons naturally don't enjoy the underworld.<br /> <br /> Yes, you took a bargain with a creature that is not alive. However, you took it because you both <i>want to be alive</i>, so why mope when you both get what you want and with a bit extra? People in real life can find life either depressing or enriched when they come back from a near-death experience, so why can't fictional characters get a version of that from an actual death experience? Besides that, the game is broad enough that you can play your characters however you want. You want to be someone who believes themselves to be dead after coming back? You've got Mourners. You want to make sure the dead and the living stay seperate? Gatekeepers. You want to introduce the living to the dead, or campaign to help the dead whenever you can, or exploit the dead for whatever mystical and physical goods they have? Pilgrims, Advocates, Necromancers and Bonepickers.<br /> <br /> The game isn't about hedonism as it is about enjoying what life has to offer. What I love about Geist is just that - there's no angst demanded from the players for our characters having died, nor does it say they have to be at odds with the voice in their heads 24/7. If we want to be, go for it, but if we want voices that are benign, if odd, then go for it. Just because something is crazy or divorced from reality doesn't mean it's malicious, and even if they annoy our characters with their antics and we can't get rid of them that's fine too, <i>because that is life</i>. You're always going to have people you can't divorce yourself from that will annoy you, tempt you to do dark things or just scream in your ears that others can't or won't help you with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857742#post857742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah no. That doesn't work for me (and I suspect others). As was already pointed out Sin-Eaters don't actually celebrate life in as much as they celebrate winning the lottery. The game should be about way more than that. They made a deal with something not alive to come back to the land of the living. A big problem with the game is 100% too much focus on the 'back to the land of the living' bit and 100% not enough focus on the 'made a deal with something not alive' part.<br /> <br /> That is just what we need. Because I reject the notion that Vampire is a game primarily about characters life after death. It's a game of politics and magic and faith and addiction and your inner monster, none of which are about death per se. Whereas Geist is a game about passing beyond, the underworld, ghosts, and cheating death (at a price -- which it needs more of that whole price part because right now it's free-ride city).<br /> <br /> Devil, angel, what's the difference? A deal was struck with something not human. The Chronicles of Darkness being what they are, the underlying intentions of that not human thing should be not good. People who come back from the dead shouldn't be partying it up like it was some asinine kegger. I don't want to play Frat-boy: the Party-Crasher any more than I want to play Care Bears: the Happy.<br /> <br /> Like I said before. Geist spends too much time trying to be <b><i>not Wraith</i></b> and not enough time thinking about what it means to come back to life with an undead monkey on your back.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing a bit part about Geists though - they were <i>once human</i> and want to experience that again. The game practically encourages you to figure out what the dead had in life, to decrypt what your Geist wants and to fulfill those wishes. In return, you get powers and perceptions you never had while alive, and you're able to help others you otherwise couldn't. Heck, Sin Eaters are one of the only gamelines where you can properly <i>resolve</i> your supernatural condition, and the only other ones I can think of off the top of my head is Promethean and Changeling 2e. Just because you make a deal with something that isn't human doesn't mean the game automatically becomes a horror story. Don't get my wrong, it can be if you and the GM want it to be, but it doesn't automatically have to be it.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't know what definition of &quot;Vampire&quot; you have, but a game where you come back to life after death and you need to drink blood to survive sounds awfully like a vampire game to me. Just because it's about &quot;politics and magic and faith and addiction and your inner monster&quot; doesn't make it any less a game about being a vampire.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it just feels like you want to take levity out of the game because it's trying to make death less of a depressing thing to work with in a game. Why does it need to be dark and dour? If you don't like the mood, play it differently. If that still isn't enough, to the point you feel the game should be completely and innately changed, then why are you playing something that doesn't offer what you want?<br /> <br /> Also, I think you're confusing a game &quot;trying to be not Wraith&quot; with a game simply being its own thing. That statement can apply to literally any other gameline in World/Chronicles of Darkness with something vaguely similar to an old World of Darkness gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T03:11:32-07:00","id":858251,"title":"","content":"Every culture views death in a different way. When my great Aunt Ruth died it was on the eve of her grandson's wedding. We celebrated the wedding on Saturday and Sunday we put on our mourning clothes and sat in solemn silence. No one thought twice that her grandson went on his honeymoon no one said he was mourning wrong. Geist is a complex game and can be used to explore every facet of death not just the grimdark of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T14:54:06-07:00","id":859897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to beat a point to death (pun not intended), but I think there very is something akin to reconciling death with mardi gras - it's called a Day Of The Dead celebration, where, once a year, people go and enjoy themselves in a macabre celebration. Sugar skulls, people decorated as skeletons or with bones as part of their garb, appealing to the lost and enjoying life while one has it. That is Geist in a nutshell to me; you take aspects of the dead, remember what is past and, rather than dwell on how we're all going to die, you enjoy the life you have, celebrate it, and extend those celebrations to the dead as well, because they <i>were</i> alive once. Why not spread some of that joy to those who do not have it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not seeing what that has to do with a CofD game. Honestly, it sometimes feels like someone was going for the creepy feel of Ron Moore's Carnivale but added to much party and not enough creepy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, you took a bargain with a creature that is not alive. However, you took it because you both <i>want to be alive</i>, so why mope when you both get what you want and with a bit extra? People in real life can find life either depressing or enriched when they come back from a near-death experience, so why can't fictional characters get a version of that from an actual death experience? Besides that, the game is broad enough that you can play your characters however you want. You want to be someone who believes themselves to be dead after coming back? You've got Mourners. You want to make sure the dead and the living stay seperate? Gatekeepers. You want to introduce the living to the dead, or campaign to help the dead whenever you can, or exploit the dead for whatever mystical and physical goods they have? Pilgrims, Advocates, Necromancers and Bonepickers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, not convinced that the Geist is riding around with you because it <i>wants to be alive</i>. Also not sure how not partying it up is the same as moping. ~A =/= B All I'm arguing for is ~A.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the game shouldn't be about winning the lottery because they didn't. They might have come back from death but the didn't come back alone and the thing they brought with them has wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game isn't about hedonism as it is about enjoying what life has to offer. What I love about Geist is just that - there's no angst demanded from the players for our characters having died, nor does it say they have to be at odds with the voice in their heads 24/7. If we want to be, go for it, but if we want voices that are benign, if odd, then go for it. Just because something is crazy or divorced from reality doesn't mean it's malicious, and even if they annoy our characters with their antics and we can't get rid of them that's fine too, <i>because that is life</i>. You're always going to have people you can't divorce yourself from that will annoy you, tempt you to do dark things or just scream in your ears that others can't or won't help you with.</div> </div> </div> </div>We agree to disagree. I'm not seeing what your idea of the game offers that can't be done with the vanilla rule book. Just anchor a ghost to your character. More to the point though, if this is all you want then a Mortal Remains-style update book is all you need (purely a mechanical facelift to 2e rules). Some of us want the full 2e treatment though. We <i>can</i> actually both get what we want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing a bit part about Geists though - they were <i>once human</i> and want to experience that again. The game practically encourages you to figure out what the dead had in life, to decrypt what your Geist wants and to fulfill those wishes. In return, you get powers and perceptions you never had while alive, and you're able to help others you otherwise couldn't. Heck, Sin Eaters are one of the only gamelines where you can properly <i>resolve</i> your supernatural condition, and the only other ones I can think of off the top of my head is Promethean and Changeling 2e. Just because you make a deal with something that isn't human doesn't mean the game automatically becomes a horror story. Don't get my wrong, it can be if you and the GM want it to be, but it doesn't automatically have to be it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the book is more than a little unclear on whether or not they actually were <i>once human</i>. Also all of the game lines have ways of resolving the &quot;supernatural condition&quot; it's just some of those don't involve being human anymore. Not sure what this has to do with anything though. You can resolve your Geist's wants. So what? Now what? Mystery solved...permanently. The problem is that unlike Promethean and Changeling 2e, Geist doesn't actually have any incentives for story progression. It's just resurrect as much as you want, life is a ball, you won the lottery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't know what definition of &quot;Vampire&quot; you have, but a game where you come back to life after death and you need to drink blood to survive sounds awfully like a vampire game to me. Just because it's about &quot;politics and magic and faith and addiction and your inner monster&quot; doesn't make it any less a game about being a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah no, Vampire is about a lot of things. Coming back from death isn't really one of them. Living forever by paying a price on the other hand...<br /> <br /> Geist is fundamentally different (in theory) because unlike some animalistic beast doing everything it can to survive from night to night, Geists have (or are supposed to have) some alien entity driving them to accomplish mysterious ends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, it just feels like you want to take levity out of the game because it's trying to make death less of a depressing thing to work with in a game. Why does it need to be dark and dour? If you don't like the mood, play it differently. If that still isn't enough, to the point you feel the game should be completely and innately changed, then why are you playing something that doesn't offer what you want?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want the levity in the game left to the individual players and storytellers, where it belongs. I want its mandate removed from the game. Also, don't know if you've been paying attention but the 2e-ification process has involved complete and innate changes to every game that's undergone the process. I'm looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=858108#post858108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I think you're confusing a game &quot;trying to be not Wraith&quot; with a game simply being its own thing. That statement can apply to literally any other gameline in World/Chronicles of Darkness with something vaguely similar to an old World of Darkness gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference in moods is 180 degrees. This is not the case with any of the other WoD v CofD games. IMO this is <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i>. It <i>is</i> okay for the game to be darker than it is.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:10:37-07:00","id":859915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857950#post857950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857950#post857950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep. Turns out psychopomps deal with the dead... not the moping people who are left behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for necromancers. Not sure where you were going with this. Not being happy isn't the same as moping. Major error on your part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857950#post857950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You want a game about undead who have to deal with the moody depression ramifications about having being brought back from the dead with an evil alien presence inside their head that can take control of you and you can never be rid of unless you truly finally die... That's vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not what I said at all but you're free to make up my part of this &quot;conversation&quot; as you go along. Not winning the lottery isn't the same thing as moping. Ramifications and lack of levity are also not the same as moping. Actions have consequences. Consequences are serious things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857950#post857950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is what I fundamentally disagree with. Why? Chronicles of Darkness is a game where everything is in shades of grey, so why can't it be good? You can play a good beast... but no you can't have a geist that isn't horrible?</div> </div> </div> </div>As usual twisting things around to make them as bad as possible. I didn't say you couldn't have a good Geist or that you couldn't do good. I just think that levity or lack of it should be left to the discretion of individual players and troupes and not be part of the game's core identity. The Geist should take center-stage, &quot;sin-eater&quot; afterall, is merely a sub-title.<br /> <br /> I'd also note that you typically only need to add a single drop of white to black to make it grey but the converse isn't really true. Adding a single drop of black to white usually gets you some eggshell or other &quot;off-white&quot; color and not grey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857950#post857950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes... because acting like a frat boy is the only method to enjoy life or allow your geist to re-experience the joys of life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you probably meant to be faceitous but humor doesn't actually translate into text that easily. Ultimately though, I just calls them likes I sees them. <br /> <br /> Geist is so focused on levity that it has nothing left for the sense of mystery, urban fantasy, and gothic lit that are central to both CofD and good ghost stories.<br /> <br /> You really don't want a Geist 2e you just want Geist 1e with 2e compatible rules. I think a Mortal Remains book will suffice for your wants. Others of us want the full 2e treatment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=857950#post857950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't say what it's like in relation to Wraith since I never played it or read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, do yourself a favor and pick up a copy of Wraith 20th when it comes out. You won't be sorry. Best WoD game of them all (and I rather liked all of them). CofD could definitely go for a game like it.<br /> <br /> At any rate. I think this discussion has petered out. You're not changing your position and I'm not changing mine. The beauty is that there are ways we can both get what we want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T18:45:07-07:00","id":860030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You really don't want a Geist 2e you just want Geist 1e with 2e compatible rules. I think a Mortal Remains book will suffice for your wants. Others of us want the full 2e treatment </div> </div> </div>Nah, I want change. Just not change that removes the primary concept. As far as I'm aware, the 2e games alter mechanics and themes so they better fit the desired themes of the game and removing things that harm player experience. Werewolf is still a game of half-spirit shapechanging hunters, but there are changes that make it fit it's themes of being hunters and being part of a pack properly.<br /> <br /> Synergy for example would Have to be changed in 2e. Not just because integrity has replaced morality, but because synergy doesn't fit right with what the themes suggest. It's meant to be synergy between the geist and sin-eater, but geists have basically no agency in 1e so that doesn't make sense and then on top of that the geist's personality doesn't even alter how synergy works, you can act directly opposite to your geists interests and yet still have high synergy. Synergy also doesn't make sense with the idea that many sin-eaters end up with a geist inside their head that they dislike or is psycho or something. People have made some good suggestions for this; making it more like harmony, making synergy tied to your geists aspirations, or replacing it with something else entirely.<br /> <br /> Momentos was another thing I think should be severely changed to give a reason for players to get them, since right now they are just random minor buffs. Archetypes maybe changed to reflect what the bargain between geist and mortal was, rather than randomly coming out of nowhere, and remove redundant archetypes. Make the underworld actually important. Give actual reason or sin-eaters to deal with ghosts, since right now a lot of the time it's just &quot;Because that's what you're meant to do in geist&quot;. Make the krewes fit the themes or remove them, since right now they don't properly fit outside of a method to give geists a mythology tie, but that could just be an initial thing with geists rather than having to jump through hoops to get it. Give geists more agency since they're the title, etc.<br /> <br /> I want change, I just want it to be 2e Geist rather than an unrelated gameline that happens to use the word geist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, do yourself a favor and pick up a copy of Wraith 20th when it comes out. You won't be sorry. Best WoD game of them all (and I rather liked all of them). CofD could definitely go for a game like it. </div> </div> </div>Nah, fundamental differences in perspective on mechanics and death wouldn't go down well. Plus too angsty (and I'm saying that as a guy who dates emos and goths) :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T22:20:36-07:00","id":860797,"title":"","content":"I feel like an item being a Memento should do something to alter it mechanically somehow; there are a few examples which <i>seem</i> to imply that, such as the bus ticket in the core book which works like any ticket but is immediately handed back to you, but the actual rules never elaborated on that. Heck, the idea of vehicles being mementos is something I have a lot of interest in, and yet in gameplay terms they're just kind of...there. The only mementos that really do interesting things are deathmasks since they allow a numen to manifest when worn. I dunno, do you guys have any ideas regarding that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T02:43:08-07:00","id":860895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=860797#post860797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like an item being a Memento should do something to alter it mechanically somehow; there are a few examples which <i>seem</i> to imply that, such as the bus ticket in the core book which works like any ticket but is immediately handed back to you, but the actual rules never elaborated on that. Heck, the idea of vehicles being mementos is something I have a lot of interest in, and yet in gameplay terms they're just kind of...there. The only mementos that really do interesting things are deathmasks since they allow a numen to manifest when worn. I dunno, do you guys have any ideas regarding that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... well earlier I talked about the idea of having mementos be anchors that you have invested some of your psyche into, allowing you to call/summon that anchors ghost to you with some plasm. But I'm not sure how to handle more freeform effects for mementos since they're always rather wishy-washy mechanically and basically just say &quot;make up whatever&quot; (one of the reasons I never liked tokens in changeling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-07-2016, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T04:38:16-07:00","id":860943,"title":"","content":"Could always model them off of both Fetters and 2E Fetishes. By that I mean, take a Numina from the Ghost tied to the Memento, they mold it until it fits a thematic modification for the item in question (Like how Fetishes replicate and/or alter Gifts).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:45:21-07:00","id":861182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=860895#post860895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... well earlier I talked about the idea of having mementos be anchors that you have invested some of your psyche into, allowing you to call/summon that anchors ghost to you with some plasm. But I'm not sure how to handle more freeform effects for mementos since they're always rather wishy-washy mechanically and basically just say &quot;make up whatever&quot; (one of the reasons I never liked tokens in changeling).</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea I had for a memento vehicle (which eventually spawned into its own Horror) was that they could use plasm as fuel instead of conventional gasoline or diesel...but only if you left it in a low spot, or the underworld, which may or may not give it some unusual quirks. Giving it plasm from yourself while it's running could improve its performance for a scene...while the next scene it has a detriment to its function (say, only able to go up to safe speeds, if not lower). I don't know how balanced that is, but I feel like the larger the memento, the more odd it should be when death energies are involved. Again, the core book gave errata to that effect, but the mechanics of it never gave any indication that these could happen.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of investing psyche into mementos though, given that &quot;psyche&quot; literally means soul.<br /> <br /> Hmmm...what if mementos that anyone handled only gave minor effects, whereas mementos that are &quot;bound&quot; to a player (aka paid for with experiences) offered a much more profound effect (such as the aforementioned vehicle boost)...or vice versa, even, if you want mementos to be creepy gear that still provides some benefit to non-Sin Eaters using them. A bit like tokens in that regard, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T08:05:06-07:00","id":880981,"title":"","content":"If archetypes were changed to represent the bargain you make with your geist, what would bonepicking represent? What could the geist get from their host living comfortably?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T08:25:36-07:00","id":880995,"title":"","content":"A comfortable life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T09:00:56-07:00","id":881023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=880981#post880981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If archetypes were changed to represent the bargain you make with your geist, what would bonepicking represent? What could the geist get from their host living comfortably?</div> </div> </div> </div>Living it up, but differently than the thrill/sensation-seeking Celebrants. Bonepickers live <i><b>decadently</b></i> (yes, bolded <i>and</i> italicized).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:04:49-07:00","id":881249,"title":"","content":"One thing I wanna bring up, since it seems relevant, is that the whole of the Chronicles of Darkness is written from a very humanist perspective-some games more than others, but all of them have that thread in there. Humanity is a tough thing to be, but it's uniquely celebrated through the adversity.<br /> <br /> You want a game where it sucks to be human, go play World of Darkness. But as much as Chronicles is a game about monsters, that monstrosity is a giant toast to humanity, a bittersweet party mix played at the graduation wake. In this world, there is something to humanity, and if you remember it long enough, you just might get it back.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are monsters, as every gameline is, and there is much wrong with them and their niche of the corner. But fuck it, they ain't getting any deader, and there's Mexican Coke and Jack Daniels just waiting to have rough sex in their mouth. Eat, drink and be merry-you've been to the bottom of the world, you'll be back some day, and the only thing to do is to keep going up. You might even find what you lost along the way.<br /> <br /> Not to say that there couldn't be more in the book to support the Mourner's, Reapers, and Pilgrim's arguments. But humanity is pretty cool, and if it takes making a deal with a fucked-up has-been god to get close to it again-well, eat, drink and be merry-how much more fucked can you get?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:21:24-07:00","id":881263,"title":"","content":"Isn't it abit.... narratively mundane though? &quot;I will bring you back to life.. and in return you must live a good life....&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 05-03-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:42:50-07:00","id":881271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=881263#post881263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it abit.... narratively mundane though? &quot;I will bring you back to life.. and in return you must live a good life....&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you know how hard it is to live a good life? Especially when you factor in a deranged death god that has largely forgotten what human <i>is</i>, let alone what constitute the &quot;good life&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 05-03-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T14:43:32-07:00","id":881272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=881263#post881263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that abit.... narratively mundane though? &quot;I will bring you back to life.. and in return you must live a good life....?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If that was what the has-been god was saying, it might be. Does that musty old masquerade mannequin know what it wants? It forgot the taste of it's lovers skin when its tongue took on the thousandth layer of dust, what the shotgun spray of sunny celluloid color illuminates in the dark place of the head when it's eyes fell from their skull, what the thrill of the car crash is on ear when they clawed it out to keep from the screams ages ago. No, it doesn't ask for life. It doesn't remember. It asks for comprehension, it asks for sense, a dream it forgot when the world became dark.<br /> <br /> But it comes from the corpse that remembers, the bitter joke that's got legs again. It comes from the ghost who knows, the flatline that remembers. It comes from a human who knows things now, the one who has heard the raining rebar and echoed could-have-beens of the World Below. It comes from someone who has been to the bottom of the barrel, but remembers what sex and movies and hot dogs and never-ending red lights are. It comes from the person who had nothing and has come to realize that every pain, every pleasure, every frustration, every stupid, mind-numbing cry of hounds and telemarketers, every stupid, cringe-wringing pun from drunken slobs tripping on their own shit, every mosquito bite, every brain freeze, every gross fart-all of that is <i>not</i> the loss, the oblivion, the scouring of being. It is not that ocean, quiet and placid, that one slowly drowns in until there is nothing left.<br /> <br /> No, from the Geist, such a cry is meaningless-they don't even have a clue what they're talking about anymore.<br /> <br /> But from the Sin-Eater? The one who still has perspective?<br /> <br /> Life is it's own reward. Every fucking stupid, dumbass, exasperating bit of it. Eat it up. Drink it up. Live this entire fractured, fractal cesspool of delusions and every sensation and emotion you can wring from it to the hilt. These asinine, mundane things are the only holy and real things that matter. Life, in all it's god damned shades, is the only thing that matter.<br /> <br /> Eat it, drink it, and live it-because you've been as fucked as you can get, and you will be as fucked as you can get again in future, but neither is this day. And that makes today a good day.<br /> <br /> And one day, maybe even Death itself will remember what Life was like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-03-2016, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-03T21:45:19-07:00","id":881488,"title":"","content":"I still think the game could play up how the Geists are supposed to embody different forms of death, and those forms directly impact the impulses/requirements placed on the Bound. If they are just &quot;you live life and I'll sit back and enjoy&quot; with no muscle/dark-side behind the Bargain, the whole idea that they embody different forms of death end up ringing kind of hollow.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm saying their desire to taste-life shouldn't be part of the mix at all! It should. But I think a flaw in 1E is the lack of muscle behind the Bargain encourages players to ignore it, unless they're specifically playing a Reaper, or something else where &quot;well that's what I wanted to do anyway&quot;. I think that should be a major part of the &quot;personal horror&quot; of this particular game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T00:28:56-07:00","id":881572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=881272#post881272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, from the Geist, such a cry is meaningless-they don't even have a clue what they're talking about anymore.<br /> <br /> But from the Sin-Eater? The one who still has perspective?</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm specifically talking about from the Geist. For the sin-eater it makes perfect sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, it doesn't ask for life. It doesn't remember. It asks for comprehension, it asks for sense, a dream it forgot when the world became dark. </div> </div> </div>I can see this working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=881488#post881488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still think the game could play up how the Geists are supposed to embody different forms of death, and those forms directly impact the impulses/requirements placed on the Bound. If they are just &quot;you live life and I'll sit back and enjoy&quot; with no muscle/dark-side behind the Bargain, the whole idea that they embody different forms of death end up ringing kind of hollow.<br /> <br /> Not that I'm saying their desire to taste-life shouldn't be part of the mix at all! It should. But I think a flaw in 1E is the lack of muscle behind the Bargain encourages players to ignore it, unless they're specifically playing a Reaper, or something else where &quot;well that's what I wanted to do anyway&quot;. I think that should be a major part of the &quot;personal horror&quot; of this particular game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's my primary issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T21:14:02-07:00","id":888820,"title":"","content":"Mage 2e has a section on the underworld which is of some use to people wanting to do 2e geist. It gives some basic rules for the underworld and chthonians, and stuff (they're sorta like ghosts now), and gives some information on how geists and kerberoi work in the new edition + expanded definition of plasm.... there is also the implication that Sin-Eaters aren't the only type of bound that geists can create.<br /> <br /> edit: and there is nothing stopping chthonian geists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"