 Hills approach to open Dev. Just shower is with stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more of a masochist, and hope for the Dave-like slow trickling of stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T16:28:10-07:00","id":961968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=961967#post961967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm more of a masochist, and hope for the Dave-like slow trickling of stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly the best model is the CAS &quot;say literally nothing ever and then one day the book is out.&quot;<br /> <br /> I kid, I kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T02:12:18-07:00","id":962164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=961944#post961944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm,imma try and guess what teh REDACTED are. Are they by any chance some kind of undead being who have some kind of relationship with their own names? maybe their names are thier Anchors? so if you say bloody mary three times,she will listen.<br /> are the REDACTED anything like that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope! But that's a really cool idea. Maybe if Geist gets a Night Horrors book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=961968#post961968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Clearly the best model is the CAS &quot;say literally nothing ever and then one day the book is out.&quot;<br /> <br /> I kid, I kid.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to be a little more communicative than that. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T02:37:34-07:00","id":962167,"title":"","content":"A question I've been mulling over since word of Geist 2E got confirmed is: will The Sin-Eaters have a minor template, either a supporting 'human' template (like ghouls, wolf-blooded, sleepwalker/proximi, fae-touched, sadiq, &amp; depending how one plays or views them the Redeemed) or an antagonist 'human' template (Alchemists, Heroes)? given the feel of the game thus far, my hope is for a supporting minor template","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:44:19-07:00","id":962230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962167#post962167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question I've been mulling over since word of Geist 2E got confirmed is: will The Sin-Eaters have a minor template, either a supporting 'human' template (like ghouls, wolf-blooded, sleepwalker/proximi, fae-touched, sadiq, &amp; depending how one plays or views them the Redeemed) or an antagonist 'human' template (Alchemists, Heroes)? given the feel of the game thus far, my hope is for a supporting minor template</div> </div> </div> </div>There's an Appendix in the vein of the ones in Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage yes. Not going to spoil who it's about just yet, but I will say it's written by the brilliant Filamena Young, who also wrote Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, and Proximi, so if you liked those sections, I think you'll like what we've got planned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:47:30-07:00","id":962233,"title":"","content":"I hope it's a mini-template of tier 2 ghosts who have been made more into actual people than a ghost via large plasm infusion (since that used to make them lucid in 1e), but it's not likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-02-2016, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:14:23-07:00","id":962251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962233#post962233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope it's a mini-template of tier 2 ghosts who have been made more into actual people than a ghost via large plasm infusion (since that used to make them lucid in 1e), but it's not likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I've been thinking about that for a Ghost Chronicle project. Open a thread to discuss it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:22:09-07:00","id":962262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962230#post962230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's an Appendix in the vein of the ones in Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage yes. Not going to spoil who it's about just yet, but I will say it's written by the brilliant Filamena Young, who also wrote Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, and Proximi, so if you liked those sections, I think you'll like what we've got planned.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved those sections! Filamena Young is a fantastic writer. I eagerly await her and all team's work <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:22:31-07:00","id":962264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962233#post962233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope it's a mini-template of tier 2 ghosts who have been made more into actual people than a ghost via large plasm infusion (since that used to make them lucid in 1e), but it's not likely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rank 2 ghosts <i>are</i> actual people. They don't need an infusion of Plasm to make them moreso. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:48:46-07:00","id":962278,"title":"","content":"Mortals without souls are still people. Ghosts are not human, but neither is a vampire or a werewolf, and some might say a mage. All those are still considered people. Ghosts are NPCs and now they need a rules expansion to be PCs which honestly could wait until Geist 2e. <br /> <br /> Travis Stout,<br /> <br /> Geist originally had a bipolar theme and mood. Technically, I guess it was conflicted but presented as bipolar due to a rushed development. Could I get a brief on the theme and mood of Geist 2e so I can properly digest any released info? I want to know what the game is about, but I don't need rules and antagonists spoiled if you don't want. Hence, I ask about the theme and mood instead of the introduction of the game's bible. Hope that it is clear what I'm after.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:18:02-07:00","id":962492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962264#post962264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rank 2 ghosts <i>are</i> actual people. They don't need an infusion of Plasm to make them moreso. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting the impression Rank has very little to do with a ghost's sapience and much more to do with a gohost's power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T15:51:18-07:00","id":962542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962264#post962264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rank 2 ghosts <i>are</i> actual people. They don't need an infusion of Plasm to make them moreso. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry let me rephrase: &quot;I hope it's a mini-template of tier 2 ghosts who bring them closer to life than their ghostselves, making them properly playable via large plasm infusion (since that used to make them lucid in 1e), but it's not likely.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T19:06:58-07:00","id":962633,"title":"","content":"Not sure what you mean. I think ghosts are playable now. They can't properly use experience to power up, but that would be a simple rules expansion. Probably right about it being unlikely if more than that is desired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:17:42-07:00","id":962661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962633#post962633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what you mean. I think ghosts are playable now. They can't properly use experience to power up, but that would be a simple rules expansion. Probably right about it being unlikely if more than that is desired.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Based on that, the loch ness monster and T-rex are playable since horror rules exist.<br /> 2. They can't change their integrity after creation &quot;unless something happens to push them back to the level of cognizance and self-awareness they had in life.&quot;... like say... a plasm infusion...<br /> 3. Attributes would cost a giant amount of xp to increase.<br /> 4. Attributes have no clear amount a player should start with.<br /> 5. Should players be able to go past 14 attribute dots?<br /> 6. Should players be able to have attributes up to 7 at character creation?<br /> 7. Skills being replaced by &quot;wishy-washy&quot;-ness is fine for NPC's but annoying when it comes to running a PC for a whole campaign.<br /> 8. Attribute + Attribute can easily be higher than Attribute + Rank, meaning they might be worse at doing stuff that they are thematically tied to than them doing actions that have nothing to do with their concept.<br /> 9. Lack of merits means you have much less customization than you'd really want for PC's.<br /> 10. Need XP costs for numina/influence/manifestations<br /> 11. Can you take more than 5 numina?<br /> 12. How are you going to stop the player from getting bored after a few sessions when they cease to be able to spend XP without having to turn themselves into geists?<br /> 13. Needs some way to deal with the fact that they are harder to include in the group's adventurers than vampires in that they have to linger around their anchors so often and that if they lose all their anchors they get stuck in the undeworld requiring the other players to repeatedly summon them over and over.<br /> 14. Is the ghost still considered playable if it claims someone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T04:24:48-07:00","id":962762,"title":"","content":"I'm reading over the Geist crossover section in the Demon Storyteller's Guide. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> your name isn't on it, but did you have any hand in it? Is anything in it a potential hint of what's to come? Specifically this bit about the difference between modern sin-eaters and the &quot;old guard&quot;.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Death is Optional</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Sin-Eaters present unique challenges to the Unchained. Unlike other supernatural entities, Sin-Eaters\u2019 paranormal concerns rest squarely with the dead. Unless a demon is willing to brave the Underworld, the Bound must be dealt with in human terms. That has its own challenges. With two minds in one body, \u201ctroublesome\u201d doesn\u2019t come close to defining how hard it is to pull one over on a Sin-Eater. Their only common goal, as a people, seems to be helping ghosts move on.<br /> <br /> The ethos of modern Sin-Eaters revolves around unpredictability and celebrating life. Older-generation Bound are generally more serious. Their grim outlook is not simply a matter of age, however. Something runs deep in the bones and plasm of the old guard, something that the Unchained don\u2019t yet understand. The current generation, meanwhile, uses their second chance at life to celebrate it, resulting commonly in a carefree attitude and an irreverent take on the supernatural. The one time all Sin-Eaters are in lockstep is when someone or something interferes with ghosts, or the Underworld they\u2019ve been charged to protect. In those cases, the full extent of a Sin-Eater\u2019s powers are on display; the only recourse is to run or redirect blame onto someone else, ideally a mutual enemy. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T04:46:30-07:00","id":962768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962661#post962661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Based on that, the loch ness monster and T-rex are playable since horror rules exist.<br /> 2. They can't change their integrity after creation &quot;unless something happens to push them back to the level of cognizance and self-awareness they had in life.&quot;... like say... a plasm infusion...<br /> 3. Attributes would cost a giant amount of xp to increase.<br /> 4. Attributes have no clear amount a player should start with.<br /> 5. Should players be able to go past 14 attribute dots?<br /> 6. Should players be able to have attributes up to 7 at character creation?<br /> 7. Skills being replaced by &quot;wishy-washy&quot;-ness is fine for NPC's but annoying when it comes to running a PC for a whole campaign.<br /> 8. Attribute + Attribute can easily be higher than Attribute + Rank, meaning they might be worse at doing stuff that they are thematically tied to than them doing actions that have nothing to do with their concept.<br /> 9. Lack of merits means you have much less customization than you'd really want for PC's.<br /> 10. Need XP costs for numina/influence/manifestations<br /> 11. Can you take more than 5 numina?<br /> 12. How are you going to stop the player from getting bored after a few sessions when they cease to be able to spend XP without having to turn themselves into geists?<br /> 13. Needs some way to deal with the fact that they are harder to include in the group's adventurers than vampires in that they have to linger around their anchors so often and that if they lose all their anchors they get stuck in the undeworld requiring the other players to repeatedly summon them over and over.<br /> 14. Is the ghost still considered playable if it claims someone?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, would a simple template layered on top of a Rank 2 Ghost:<ul><li>Unlock the standard 9 Attributes? Highest Attribute in a category determines the simplified rating (So Str 2, Int 3, Pre 2 would equal Power 3) when needed?</li> <li>Open up Skills again? But the Ghost can use Rank instead, if for some reason it is higher and thematic?</li> <li>Attributes are capped at 5, as normal for mortals or Rank 2.</li> <li>Merits are selectable again (this seems more like a simplified NPC restriction than an inherent Ephemeral one).</li> <li>Use the XP Costs in The Pack?</li> <li>Remember that Essence Bleed only occurs every hour, so short excursions are possible (though lacking the required Manifestation Conditions makes doing anything material tricky).</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T04:59:38-07:00","id":962773,"title":"","content":"Travis, what is the plan for the power set of a Sin-Eater for Geist 2e? Would it be more of a rebalance of the pre-existing set of powers or a new slew of powers all together? Perhaps half and half? I know it's been said that Manifestations will be renamed but how about Keys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T07:32:51-07:00","id":962818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962762#post962762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading over the Geist crossover section in the Demon Storyteller's Guide. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> your name isn't on it, but did you have any hand in it? Is anything in it a potential hint of what's to come? Specifically this bit about the difference between modern sin-eaters and the &amp;quot;old guard&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I offered some feedback on it, but that was written before there was officially a Geist 2e and before I was officially the developer on it. So it's... close-ish in some respects, but it's also very much an outsider's view.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962773#post962773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Travis, what is the plan for the power set of a Sin-Eater for Geist 2e? Would it be more of a rebalance of the pre-existing set of powers or a new slew of powers all together? Perhaps half and half? I know it's been said that Manifestations will be renamed but how about Keys?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keys are still in, but the powers are getting a major overhaul. It's still too early for me to want to talk about mechanics, but it's not going to be the same system as 1e. For one thing, trying to design and balance a full set of powers for every Key/Haunt* combo is an incredibly difficult task, and leads to a lot of weird, athematic powers. For another, space is a concern for PoD books. Geist 1e spent 37,000 words in Manifestations and Keys; we have about 25k for the topic. And finally, I'd like Geist to get some actual supplements this time around, and the logistics of trying to add new powers to a grid like that is a nightmare.<br /> <br /> So expect a tighter, more thematic power set this time around. We're experimenting with some pretty cool stuff, though comma that I think will make them feel pretty mechanically distinct from the other spots.<br /> <br /> * Spoiler. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T10:15:15-07:00","id":962874,"title":"","content":"Sounds promising, especially with supplement books for the gameline. I suppose more powers could be added in like the Pit Manifestations and Stygian Key? I can understand tightening up the powers especially for the print space, I think some people probably felt some powers were redundant with other powers present, though I think most of the concerns I've seen with that were on the curse key.<br /> <br /> I imagine since Tilts and Conditions were made into full fledged things in 2e, that Sin-Eaters/Geists being a manipulator/causes would be their shining field, especially with Boneyard. Seems like sudden environmental control would be the thing that a Sin-Eater could do better than other splats, probably only rivaled by Mages and Beasts in their own lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T11:39:01-07:00","id":962918,"title":"","content":"So how do Haunts work if there isn't a full thing? I hate to keep harping on &quot;well what <i>I</i> was doing&quot;, but my main ideas were to either use a system like Werewolf's Renown/Gifts system. Are Keys likely to be as limiting (and yet so very random) as they were in 1e? In thinking of how to unofficially redo Geist, I realized that a lot of the Manifestations tended to do things that were, as you said, athematic (and that barely had supporting mechanics to begin with). Another one was to do something similar to the Princess: The Hopeful homebrew and have generic Manifestations--Haunts, in this case--that could then have Keys applied to them for additional effect. Come to think of it, that's sort of how Seeming Contracts work in Changeling. I had to essentially redefine half the keys to make them more reasonable. The overlap between Stygian/Silent and how Stigmatic makes any interactions with ghosts double-easy were of concern, as well as the fact that half the Elemental Keys are &quot;that, but with Water/Air/Fire/Earth instead!&quot; Not to mention the overlap between Caul and Shroud, and the way that so many of both grant Armour and/or Defense, making Sin-eaters impossible to actually hit, even in 1e where Defense is generally meaningless.<br /> I love Geist conceptually, but I think half my posts on the OPP forums are criticizing its actual mechanics... And the themes of things like Krewes. Or the way Krewe merits don't even work with how krewes work. Seriously how do you become a Tier 2 krewe, there is no actual explanation for what happens when you join an existing Krewe despite &quot;your Geist changes and you all have a revelation&quot; being a major aspect of krewes.<br /> <br /> Moving on, will we be likely to see anything about the Church of the Black Gate? They're a Claimed/Geist obsessed cult that sees the merger of flesh and ephemera as a state of godliness, and the focus of an SAS (<i>Through The Ebon Gate</i>) and one of the aspects of Geist I've always felt would be good as a major antagonist. Actually, I've always felt in general that with the way Geister can often take on mythic forms that giving Sin-eaters some mythical history would be completely reasonable (and that it's absence is frustrating). I had actually written up some stuff comparing Aztlan with the Underworld, and creating a mythic history where Geister were tied to several aspects of Mayaztec culture, with many of the Gods being Sin-eaters or at least their Geister, and some stuff with Cortez' arrival.<br /> But really now I'm just rambling about my homebrew ideas, which isn't that useful to the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962874#post962874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think some people probably felt some powers were redundant with other powers present, though I think most of the concerns I've seen with that were on the curse key.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not really on board with Boneyard area control shenanigans (boneyard is a dumb power and should either be restricted and limited for more haunted housey applications or ditched); <i>Man</i>, The Curse... That Manifestation is so pointless. Almost every Curse effect is so asinine and petty that in any case it would be easier to shoot someone. All the effects of the Curse are just ways to pester and gaslight without the actual need to do anything, which considering the vast majority of Sin-eater powers already work to that end seems pointless. Shout-out to the Stygian Curse for giving you sexual dysfunction so bad you kill yourself. There's also the fact that the mechanics are vague to the point of uselessness, though I'm too lazy to download the 1.1 pdf to double check whether that was fixed, and doubly too lazy to crack open my book, so I can't elaborate on what specifically was my problem with it.<br /> Shout out to the Pit Manifestation for essentially being the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T12:00:34-07:00","id":962931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962768#post962768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, would a simple template layered on top of a Rank 2 Ghost:<ul><li>Unlock the standard 9 Attributes? Highest Attribute in a category determines the simplified rating (So Str 2, Int 3, Pre 2 would equal Power 3) when needed?</li> <li>Open up Skills again? But the Ghost can use Rank instead, if for some reason it is higher and thematic?</li> <li>Attributes are capped at 5, as normal for mortals or Rank 2.</li> <li>Merits are selectable again (this seems more like a simplified NPC restriction than an inherent Ephemeral one).</li> <li>Use the XP Costs in The Pack?</li> <li>Remember that Essence Bleed only occurs every hour, so short excursions are possible (though lacking the required Manifestation Conditions makes doing anything material tricky).</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say that &quot;ghosts don't have skills or Merits&quot; is more of a &quot;this system is designed for STCs&quot; quality than &quot;ghosts use three Attributes&quot;. Given that astrally-projecting characters use three Attributes but keep their Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-03-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T04:10:00-07:00","id":963158,"title":"","content":"If I was trying to make a ghost player, I would start by creating the mortal character that the ghost is made from then convert that over to a ghost. I would not use the skill rules for ephemerals as I believe that to be strictly based on them being NPCs. Start at rank 2 with 3 numina and guess some experience costs for rank and numina. I would stick to the limits imposed by rank.<br /> <br /> I imagine an official write-up for ghosts or spirits would be more thought out, but that is the quick and dirty version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:24:25-07:00","id":963188,"title":"","content":"Numina would <i>probably</i> sit at around 2 to 4 experiences a piece (pretty sure there's precedent for those numbers or thereabouts). Rank... would be complicated, in part because it &quot;scales&quot; quicker than other power stats. Seems like something the character would need to meet requirements of some kind for before investing experience in at all.<br /> Some concrete rules might need to be laid out for Influences too: can a PC ghost have more dots of Influence than an NPC ghost? What would they cost to increase? Does buying more cost Numina &quot;slots&quot; like it does when creating an NPC ghost? Can the player <i>even buy them at all</i>, or do they just acquire new levels with Rank? And how do <i>Manifestations</i> work in player hands? How do Bans and Banes scale with increasing rank aside from the general and open-ended &quot;gets more complicated for more powerful ephemerals&quot; rule? Are there special rules for the Integrity they in particular track?<br /> <br /> Ghost PCs would be fantastic to see, and I'm still holding out hope for them (<i>especially</i> for Geist 2e; playable ghosts alongside Sin-Eaters and living mortals with or without ghost-related supernatural merits - and perhaps the new mystery minor template if it doesn't cover anything already mentioned - would <i>really</i> emphasize the game's &quot;mediator between the living and the dead&quot; theme), but there are a number of questions that need answering first that giving experience costs won't cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":".  Minor typo correction. 09-04-2016, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T06:48:29-07:00","id":963198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963188#post963188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost PCs would be fantastic to see, and I'm still holding out hope for them (<i>especially</i> for Geist 2e; playable ghosts alongside Sin-Eaters and living mortals with or without ghost-related supernatural merits - and perhaps the new mystery minor template if it doesn't cover anything already mentioned - would <i>really</i> emphasize the game's &quot;mediator between the living and the dead&quot; theme), but there are a number of questions that need answering first that giving experience costs won't cover.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly would, and I recall a story in the <i>The Primordial Feast</i> (the Beast anthology),Territory I think it was called, where there was a Sin-Eater who had the ghost of their former boyfriend (who died in the crash that led to her Bargain) as a companion, even to the point that they interacted like they were normal people, bar the only-I-can-see-you thing. I'm hoping that this is an omen for Geist 2e, as the sin-eater in question also used a power which I don't recall from Geist 1e to turn herself into a living, moving metal statue. The closest I can remember to that in 1e is the 5-dot Grave-Dirt Caul, which lets the sin-eater turn into an inanimate stone statue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T10:29:42-07:00","id":963264,"title":"","content":"Unless they couldn't come up with any other good ideas for a side splat, I assume player ghosts won't make the core but a supplement will cover ghosts and they would drop full player rules then. I would imagine some people would buy a ghost book even if they won't play Geist. Depending on what a Krewe looks like in the end, ghosts might be able to join. I can't see ghosts not getting as much in Geist as spirits got in Werewolf. Ghosts are easier to write than spirits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T10:52:59-07:00","id":963272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963264#post963264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless they couldn't come up with any other good ideas for a side splat, I assume player ghosts won't make the core but a supplement will cover ghosts and they would drop full player rules then. I would imagine some people would buy a ghost book even if they won't play Geist. Depending on what a Krewe looks like in the end, ghosts might be able to join. I can't see ghosts not getting as much in Geist as spirits got in Werewolf. Ghosts are easier to write than spirits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost-Krewe members would be something awesome, in my opinion. I'm not sure exactly how that would work, but after all that's not my job <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:56:09-07:00","id":963316,"title":"","content":"Haunts is very thematic, better then Manifestatioms for Giest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:07:45-07:00","id":963319,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if Haunts and Keys interact at all now or are they seperate abilities altogether?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:09:44-07:00","id":963321,"title":"","content":"I'm curious if the minor template are some kind of sentient plasm infused zombies, that don't rot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:20:47-07:00","id":963324,"title":"","content":"Or maybe they're Revenants (a la WoD:Antagonists, not VtR2e). While MtC's ghost Numina was an admitted patch job in terms of implementation, the concepts that were covered by it are sound, and include walking dead as well as ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:45:55-07:00","id":963336,"title":"","content":"My idea for a Geist specific minor splat was effectively an Abmortal; they were close to dying, but just when they hit the cusp, something stopped, almost as though death rejected them...or felt it just wasn't a good day to take that particular person. Maybe they were tied to another person who experienced death, and in doing so gained a new lease on life in turn. They aren't Abmortals, but they're not quite Sin Eaters eithr. They can see ghosts, but the image is fuzzy, their voices not as distinct; they can hold plasm, but not use it nearly so well; they have access to a Key and a Manifestation/Haunt, but only the one initially, and they may also use Ceremonies. I call them Death Hallowed, but I've not made much progress with them. :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:48:24-07:00","id":963340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963324#post963324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe they're Revenants (a la WoD:Antagonists, not VtR2e). While MtC's ghost Numina was an admitted patch job in terms of implementation, the concepts that were covered by it are sound, and include walking dead as well as ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A Revenant's just a ghost Claiming its own corpse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T13:51:26-07:00","id":963368,"title":"","content":"Complete with the increased attributes? You're not merging two separate people into one, so the mechanics might not be exactly the same.<br /> <br /> That little nitpick aside, the Claimed in WtF are the result of a spirit Claiming a human; but they're still considered to be a distinct character type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T16:33:03-07:00","id":963439,"title":"","content":"I think Ghosts, Spirits, Goetics (with a Mages help), and even Godmachine Angels can use the Claimed Manifestation on either a living person or a dead body. <br /> <br /> Once they become Claimed they're only real difference is in personality and Influences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-04-2016, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T00:22:46-07:00","id":963586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963319#post963319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious if Haunts and Keys interact at all now or are they seperate abilities altogether?</div> </div> </div> </div>They interact, just not in the same way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963439#post963439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Ghosts, Spirits, Goetics (with a Mages help), and even Godmachine Angels can use the Claimed Manifestation on either a living person or a dead body</div> </div> </div> </div>For that matter, so can geists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T04:56:14-07:00","id":963630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963586#post963586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They interact, just not in the same way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For that matter, so can geists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Great to hear the names of the Sin-Eater power facets. I look forward to hearing how Haunts &amp; Keys interact. As Haunts are now an ability, are the Safe Place location with an Underworld connection for Sin-Eaters remaining Cenotes (I seem to recall that they used to be called Haunts)?<br /> <br /> And if I understand you correctly, as a Geist is a Rank 3+ ghost, they can Claim just like a Rank 3+ of any other form of ephemeral entity, but also have the option to make the Bargain instead of Claiming right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T05:04:20-07:00","id":963632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963630#post963630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great to hear the names of the Sin-Eater power facets. I look forward to hearing how Haunts &amp; Keys interact. As Haunts are now an ability, are the Safe Place location with an Underworld connection for Sin-Eaters remaining Cenotes (I seem to recall that they used to be called Haunts)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that Merit is called Cenote unless/until I come up with something better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963630#post963630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if I understand you correctly, as a Geist is a Rank 3+ ghost, they can Claim just like a Rank 3+ of any other form of ephemeral entity, but also have the option to make the Bargain instead of Claiming right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct; both Claim and the Bargain are treated as Manifestations, so assuming a geist has Claim as one of its Manifestations (remember, ephemeral entities have Twilight Form and a number of additional Manifestations equal to Rank), it can Claim people, objects, or corpses. Not all geists have Claim, though.<br /> <br /> And yes, geist-Claimed are different than Bound. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T05:06:56-07:00","id":963634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963586#post963586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They interact, just not in the same way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling that Haunts will be template powers that Keys will fill the blanks in for, having key words that change the outcomes while saving on space. For example, Cold-Wind now gives cetain Haunts the Blizzard tilt if the Haunt exceptionally succeeds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T05:41:30-07:00","id":963646,"title":"","content":"Disappointed that manifestations are renamed to haunts (especially when they could be called Locks or Seals or Gates or Crypts or something). Haunt's noun definition was a perfect name for the safe place merit....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T06:42:07-07:00","id":963667,"title":"","content":"I'm curious, can Geists who are already bound and have the claim manifestation use claim on a person/corpse/object? I recall a power from 1e's manifestations were it was possible for a person's geist to claim a corpse for a couples days that sort of rapid deteriorated.<br /> <br /> I suppose Geists having the possibility for that from the get go does make for incentive to not piss them off when it can always claim your toaster or best friend until you appease it, or on the plus side, be beneficial to supernaturally assist you by possessing that car or forklift in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:26:42-07:00","id":963703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963667#post963667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm curious, can Geists who are already bound and have the claim manifestation use claim on a person/corpse/object? I recall a power from 1e's manifestations were it was possible for a person's geist to claim a corpse for a couples days that sort of rapid deteriorated.<br /> <br /> I suppose Geists having the possibility for that from the get go does make for incentive to not piss them off when it can always claim your toaster or best friend until you appease it, or on the plus side, be beneficial to supernaturally assist you by possessing that car or forklift in combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Claimed Manifestation is permanent unless the ephemeral entity wishes to leave. My guess is that the Bound Manifestation for Geists is permanent until the living partner/host is destroyed (Psyche is reduced to 0) or perhaps there's some rituals or prices required to separate the living from the dead. Otherwise there'd be an 'easy out' of being a Sin-Eater and even with GtSE being a hopeful CoD game, even the games that have an &quot;out&quot; endgame of being what they are (Promethean's Great Work, Mummy's Apotheosis, The Changeling playtest material's option of trying to remove Wyrd, etc.) require a lot of sacrifice &amp; work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T11:29:23-07:00","id":963807,"title":"","content":"If Synergy is how well the two entities have integrated, then I'd expect Synergy 0 to be a requirement for cutting the geist loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:01:00-07:00","id":963827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963807#post963807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Synergy is how well the two entities have integrated, then I'd expect Synergy 0 to be a requirement for cutting the geist loose.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fair point! I wonder if either a Synergy 0 or a Synergy 10 would do the trick...Beast the Primordial suggests that Synergy is like Harmony, since neither breaking point can be used to expand a Lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T12:23:05-07:00","id":963839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963827#post963827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A fair point! I wonder if either a Synergy 0 or a Synergy 10 would do the trick...Beast the Primordial suggests that Synergy is like Harmony, since neither breaking point can be used to expand a Lair.</div> </div> </div> </div>The clues start coming together... *gets out magnifying glass*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T13:03:14-07:00","id":963863,"title":"","content":"The existing points of comparison for 2e:<br /> <br /> Humanity costs experience to raise; it exist as a trait largely for the purposes of losing it.<br /> <br /> Harmony is costless and can break up or down, though the extreme ends of the scale are harder to get out of than the midpoint; the nature of Harmony 0 in particular makes it very difficult to rebalance without external aid.<br /> <br /> Wisdom, like Humanity, costs experience to raise and exists as a trait primarily to make &quot;high-Integrity monster&quot; something you have to work at; it also uses special experience and has a specific prerequisite.<br /> <br /> Pilgrimage, like Wisdom, can only be raised in certain circumstances with a particular type of experience; furthermore, it's actually impossible to lose your last dot in it.<br /> <br /> Clarity is a little closer to Harmony, in that it costs no experience to raise and can vacillate wildly across a chronicle; unlike Harmony, you can't get back from a rating of zero at all and you have to put time into getting a higher rating (though the window for doing so gets smaller as your Clarity drops and larger as it gets higher) or else engage with a limited-use shortcut that almost inevitably complicates your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-05-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:18:13-07:00","id":964364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=963863#post963863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existing points of comparison for 2e:<br /> <br /> Humanity costs experience to raise; it exist as a trait largely for the purposes of losing it.<br /> <br /> Harmony is costless and can break up or down, though the extreme ends of the scale are harder to get out of than the midpoint; the nature of Harmony 0 in particular makes it very difficult to rebalance without external aid.<br /> <br /> Wisdom, like Humanity, costs experience to raise and exists as a trait primarily to make &quot;high-Integrity monster&quot; something you have to work at; it also uses special experience and has a specific prerequisite.<br /> <br /> Pilgrimage, like Wisdom, can only be raised in certain circumstances with a particular type of experience; furthermore, it's actually impossible to lose your last dot in it.<br /> <br /> Clarity is a little closer to Harmony, in that it costs no experience to raise and can vacillate wildly across a chronicle; unlike Harmony, you can't get back from a rating of zero at all and you have to put time into getting a higher rating (though the window for doing so gets smaller as your Clarity drops and larger as it gets higher) or else engage with a limited-use shortcut that almost inevitably complicates your life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Awesome Sum up! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And Satiety is a lot like Clarity but with a downside to being full, and as much a fuel as an Integrity source. Cover is pretty unique - you want a lot of it to stay safe, and can do a lot with it story wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:19:07-07:00","id":964366,"title":"","content":"And I know this is a silly question given the 2nd Edition books after DtD, but can we expect a Sin-Eater perspective of Tokyo?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:44:20-07:00","id":964390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964366#post964366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I know this is a silly question given the 2nd Edition books after DtD, but can we expect a Sin-Eater perspective of Tokyo?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can. David Hill is already after me to let him share the draft, but I want more time to blog about the underlying changes first. But it's awesome as usual. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:03:40-07:00","id":964401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964390#post964390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can. David Hill is already after me to let him share the draft, but I want more time to blog about the underlying changes first. But it's awesome as usual. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Very excited for those blogs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:17:47-07:00","id":964412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964401#post964401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Very excited for those blogs! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Same here!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:12:10-07:00","id":964510,"title":"","content":"To preface this, I routinely get the &quot;x-splat&quot; &amp; the &quot;y-splat&quot; definitions mixed up. Having said that, what are folks thoughts on whether or not Thresholds will remain the x-splat and Archetypes the y-splat or if new names/concepts will replace them? With the heads up earlier in the thread that Geist will have changes in mechanics compared to the original, It seems like the sky's the limit and anything could happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ! I rather liked the Thresholds and their links to the four horsemen (+1 that is). Archetypes felt a bit nebulous and I wondered if 2E might use them for the virtue/vice analog for Sin-Eaters instead...SO many thoughts running around in my noggin' about this game! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:35:04-07:00","id":964535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964390#post964390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can. David Hill is already after me to let him share the draft, but I want more time to blog about the underlying changes first. But it's awesome as usual. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div> We got a small taste from his posting of the Changeling Toyko.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T18:02:55-07:00","id":964685,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I was going to call them Unlocks.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12074\" data-vbnamecard=\"12074\">Robert D</a> I'm super hoping Synergy is like Harmony (and Satiety), and that 10 and 0 are both unwanted states. I had the idea of 10 being Vacant and 0 being Wretched.<br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Worth noting that you also can't go below <i>Integrity</i> 1 either.<br /> <br /> And it looks like I need to go read the Japanese Freehold spoilers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T20:26:58-07:00","id":964747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964685#post964685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> I was going to call them Unlocks.</div> </div> </div> </div> In my 2e conversion I called them Seals because of the key thing + seven seals of the horsemen.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T00:56:16-07:00","id":964836,"title":"","content":"I was thinking seals myself, maybe gates. Hard to say without knowing what will come to be. Threshold was x and Archetype was y by default. Sin-eaters didn't have the kind of organizations that would make for a proper y-splat. Also, x and y can be interchangeable which makes it confusing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> After reading the Changeling bit, I'm starting to think the creation of a Sin-Eater might have changed significantly.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sin-Eaters in Honshu almost all become what they are through a pilgrimage to the<br /> <br /> Watarase River in Tochigi Prefecture. They take this pilgrimage with help of a human<br /> <br /> group of priestesses called the Azusa Miko. These Miko are quite versed in yokai<br /> <br /> legendry, and make fast friends with the Yosei in most scenarios. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-07-2016, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T02:26:20-07:00","id":964862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964836#post964836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the Changeling bit, I'm starting to think the creation of a Sin-Eater might have changed significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation doesn't have to change for that to happen. Sin-Eaters tell geists looking for potential bound to go to the river, and have the final part of the pilgrimage involve the pilgrim's death. That way as soon as someone finishes their pilgrimage a geist can put forth the bargain to the pilgrim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:29:59-07:00","id":965044,"title":"","content":"I imagine Sin-Eater Japan stuff might include Aokigahara Forest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T10:42:10-07:00","id":965056,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8331_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8331\" data-vbnamecard=\"8331\">milo v3</a> Ooh, that's good. Seals is good. Or, Manifestations=Seals and the individual powers as Unlocks. You'd use a Key on the Seal and Unlock the ability.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1526\" data-vbnamecard=\"1526\">Diggs</a> The Threshold/Archetype situation always bothered me. Thresholds did nothing for you besides give your starting Keys. After that, there was no benefit. No curse, no blessing, no cost reductions. At best if you extrapolate you could regain Plasm by invoking your Threshold, but there were no rules for it [to bring up my homebrew, skirting Death allowed you to roll to regain Plasm; doing it related to your Threshold added Psyche to the roll]. Archetypes were worse. Ostensibly they let you regain plasm and in <i>very</i> narrow situations they let you use a Manifestation for free, but in practice they're nothing but fluff and have no actual purpose [Again with my homebrew: I replaced them with Wake and Epitaph, Anchors based on how you relate to the dead and how you use your second chance at life, which were mechanically the same as Mask/Dirge].<br /> <br /> Really I keep bringing it up, I might as well just link the <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1WkkF0qlmJ-_vFnzvvQ6qR4WFAleQnHef-Gt53a5m7Eo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">damned</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ctjKIkgbhgTNqASvQhA2zYRfNwwmmf4YGfRSoaLeU9U/edit\" target=\"_blank\">thing</a> I kind of wish I had actually kept working on it, even as the real 2e kept getting pushed away. Sure, there were already two or three other projects to 'fix' Geist and make it 2e, but you can never have too many mods. At least, not until all your ENBs crash your computer every time you load Skyrim.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5557_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5557\" data-vbnamecard=\"5557\">Runcible</a> Suicide Forest is some spooky shit. Also, Battleship Island.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 09-07-2016, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:06:28-07:00","id":965163,"title":"","content":"Thresholds actually do affect other things, primarily Ceremonies - if you use your keystone as a ritual tool in a ceremony in a way that matches your threshold, you get a +3 bonus to it (so if your keystone was of the Forgotten Threshold and it was a necklace, you could use it in the Finding Ceremony to find someone who was forgotten, or died to an accident).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-07-2016, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:06:38-07:00","id":965257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964862#post964862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Creation doesn't have to change for that to happen. Sin-Eaters tell geists looking for potential bound to go to the river, and have the final part of the pilgrimage involve the pilgrim's death. That way as soon as someone finishes their pilgrimage a geist can put forth the bargain to the pilgrim.</div> </div> </div> </div>An addition is a change. I recall the person dies briefly, wants to continue living, geist comes along, and a bargain is struck. Sounds like in Honshu there is more to it than that. Not a problem for me. It was a bit boring. In this instance, I'm actually fine with gutting the game and rebuilding it. I liked the concepts but the execution seemed rushed without even needing to be told that it was. I think by current standards the details are actually pretty dated. Geist is the reason why I never complain about games coming out late. Literally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:30:53-07:00","id":965357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965257#post965257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I recall the person dies briefly, wants to continue living, geist comes along, and a bargain is struck.</div> </div> </div> </div>The same things happeing in Honshu, it just happens that there is a place that geists know will have people that will accept the bargain, so they go there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T23:52:49-07:00","id":965525,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> That's essentially fluff only. What specific thing you do for a ceremony doesn't really matter, and every ceremony can accept any Threshold or Keystone as part of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T00:37:44-07:00","id":965541,"title":"","content":"I do hope ceremonies wont cost extra for reflavouring them in 2e... that was odd and annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T01:04:31-07:00","id":965548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965541#post965541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do hope ceremonies wont cost extra for reflavouring them in 2e... that was odd and annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely will not. Ceremonies look a lot more like Forsaken 2e rites now--some suggestions for symbolism/ritual actions to provide a guideline, but you can and should decide for yourself what that specific ceremomy looks like for your krewe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:25:03-07:00","id":965592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965548#post965548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They absolutely will not. Ceremonies look a lot more like Forsaken 2e rites now--some suggestions for symbolism/ritual actions to provide a guideline, but you can and should decide for yourself what that specific ceremomy looks like for your krewe.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Delightful! I enjoyed the suggested symbols/rituals in WtF 2e's rites. I imagine Geist 2e's will be ghost-based, with wardings, summonings, and banishments as needed, and i wonder what sort of effects Ceremonies will have on mortals or on Sin-Eater template abilities (which i can only speculate on what 2e's template will look like lol).<br /> <br /> On a different note, I recall lots of nicknames given to Sin-Eaters in various other lines' books (Hunter, Dark Eras, Changeling Tokyo preview in the Changeling Lost forum): Fogmen, Risen Dead, etc.) Do Sin-Eaters refer to themselves by any other names besides the Bound or Sin-Eaters? Or has anyone come across other names other creatures or characters call them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:52:28-07:00","id":965601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965592#post965592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a different note, I recall lots of nicknames given to Sin-Eaters in various other lines' books (Hunter, Dark Eras, Changeling Tokyo preview in the Changeling Lost forum): Fogmen, Risen Dead, etc.) Do Sin-Eaters refer to themselves by any other names besides the Bound or Sin-Eaters? Or has anyone come across other names other creatures or characters call them?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Bound&quot; is the general term for &quot;people who accepted the Bargain and returned from death mystically bonded to a geist.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is a specific term for those Bound who fall into the player character-suitable splats.<br /> <br /> To continue using the Werewolf analogy, it's like how &quot;Uratha&quot; means all werewolves and &quot;Forsaken&quot; means &quot;this specific group the game is built around playing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those are the only names in general use in the core book--though, as you say, sometimes in particular places or Dark Eras the locals might have different terminology. &quot;Krewe,&quot; for example, only became associated with the Bound and their religion in the 1920s, during a major resurgence of Sin-Eater culture around New Orleans, and it wasn't particularly widely used outside the Americas until decades later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":12259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","user":"GimpInBlack","date":". 09-08-2016, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T05:46:38-07:00","id":965619,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Dark Eras, might this core book dig into the whole underworld was an ocean once before lowering into the ocean of fragments? Or the current Sin-Eater/Cthnonian relationship being different than how it was far back in the past?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T06:57:07-07:00","id":965645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965601#post965601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Bound&quot; is the general term for &quot;people who accepted the Bargain and returned from death mystically bonded to a geist.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is a specific term for those Bound who fall into the player character-suitable splats.<br /> <br /> To continue using the Werewolf analogy, it's like how &quot;Uratha&quot; means all werewolves and &quot;Forsaken&quot; means &quot;this specific group the game is built around playing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those are the only names in general use in the core book--though, as you say, sometimes in particular places or Dark Eras the locals might have different terminology. &quot;Krewe,&quot; for example, only became associated with the Bound and their religion in the 1920s, during a major resurgence of Sin-Eater culture around New Orleans, and it wasn't particularly widely used outside the Americas until decades later.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always liked the use of the New Orleans 'Krewe' as the grouping for Sin Eaters. Really brings out the celebratory side of the funeral themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:36:21-07:00","id":965663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965357#post965357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same things happeing in Honshu, it just happens that there is a place that geists know will have people that will accept the bargain, so they go there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a singles bar. But for not-really-suicides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:48:37-07:00","id":965675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965601#post965601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Bound&quot; is the general term for &quot;people who accepted the Bargain and returned from death mystically bonded to a geist.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is a specific term for those Bound who fall into the player character-suitable splats.<br /> <br /> To continue using the Werewolf analogy, it's like how &quot;Uratha&quot; means all werewolves and &quot;Forsaken&quot; means &quot;this specific group the game is built around playing.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those are the only names in general use in the core book--though, as you say, sometimes in particular places or Dark Eras the locals might have different terminology. &quot;Krewe,&quot; for example, only became associated with the Bound and their religion in the 1920s, during a major resurgence of Sin-Eater culture around New Orleans, and it wasn't particularly widely used outside the Americas until decades later.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really quite interesting.<br /> <br /> So, what exactly is it that determines whether or not somebody is a Sin-Eater or one of these other groups? Is it because their Bargain was different, or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T07:55:16-07:00","id":965678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965675#post965675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really quite interesting.<br /> <br /> So, what exactly is it that determines whether or not somebody is a Sin-Eater or one of these other groups? Is it because their Bargain was different, or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I'm aware, all of that was true in 1e. So... probably the same as in 1e:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist 1e</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cSin-Eater\u201d is properly used only for the Bound who use their gifts to lay the dead to rest, whether by destroying them, banishing them to the Underworld, or resolving their anchors. Some of the Bound choose a different path: they deny what Sin-Eaters see as their responsibility, whether out of fear, laziness, or greed.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:15:28-07:00","id":965690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965675#post965675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really quite interesting.<br /> <br /> So, what exactly is it that determines whether or not somebody is a Sin-Eater or one of these other groups? Is it because their Bargain was different, or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basically just their approach to the condition. Sin-eaters try (generally speaking) to help the dead and the living coexist, be that by helping a ghost move one, by banishing an insane spectre or by killing off necromancers and Bound-gone-bad. Those who are not sin-eaters tend to be the ones who enslave ghost for their own ends or use their Manifestations (Haunts now) selfishly to gain things for themselves. That's not to say that 'sin-eaters' never use the dead unfairly or abuse their powers, but in general they are the ones that don't. There's no real difference between them other than culture and their personal opinions and self-imposed duties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T08:22:25-07:00","id":965692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965690#post965690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's basically just their approach to the condition. Sin-eaters try (generally speaking) to help the dead and the living coexist, be that by helping a ghost move one, by banishing an insane spectre or by killing off necromancers and Bound-gone-bad. Those who are not sin-eaters tend to be the ones who enslave ghost for their own ends or use their Manifestations (Haunts now) selfishly to gain things for themselves. That's not to say that 'sin-eaters' never use the dead unfairly or abuse their powers, but in general they are the ones that don't. There's no real difference between them other than culture and their personal opinions and self-imposed duties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much this, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T09:44:32-07:00","id":965721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965601#post965601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sin-Eater&quot; is a specific term for those Bound who fall into the player character-suitable splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does this imply there will be more stuff about non-Sin-eater Bound? I mean, that was <i>kind of</i> there in 1e, but of course it never had anyone else, and even the Sacrosanct/Wretched/Vacant were treated as normal Sin-eaters, with no mechanics referencing their ideological differences. Both La Diabla Blanca and Nicholas Burtchael have Archetypes (Reaper/Wretched and Reaper/Vacant respectively, which just highlights one of the many problems with the Archetype system, in that being Wretched of Vacant in the way the book presents means being a specific Archetype; what about a Wretched where the Bound was a sociopathic killer, but the Geist is a saint?)<br /> <br /> Will there be any mechanical difference, like how Pure are mechanically distinct from Forsaken? I mean, Archetypes as they exist in 1e don't work for Bound that <i>aren't </i>Sin-eaters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T10:23:22-07:00","id":965735,"title":"","content":"Is there a possibility of more than one geist trying to strike a bargain with a recently deceased at the same time or even more so actually getting a person to agree to multiple bargains? Wasn't sure if it was possible for a person to have multiple geists attached to one bound. Sort of like how there's the hive-claimed but more of a &quot;hive-bargained&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:11:44-07:00","id":966094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965721#post965721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this imply there will be more stuff about non-Sin-eater Bound? <br /> <br /> Will there be any mechanical difference, like how Pure are mechanically distinct from Forsaken? I mean, Archetypes as they exist in 1e don't work for Bound that <i>aren't </i>Sin-eaters</div> </div> </div> </div>A little bit in the core--maybe as much as the Pure got in Forsaken 2e. It's something I want to explore layer, though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965735#post965735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a possibility of more than one geist trying to strike a bargain with a recently deceased at the same time or even more so actually getting a person to agree to multiple bargains? Wasn't sure if it was possible for a person to have multiple geists attached to one bound. Sort of like how there's the hive-claimed but more of a &amp;quot;hive-bargained&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the cpre, but it's a topic earmarked for the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:27:06-07:00","id":966098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965735#post965735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a possibility of more than one geist trying to strike a bargain with a recently deceased at the same time or even more so actually getting a person to agree to multiple bargains? Wasn't sure if it was possible for a person to have multiple geists attached to one bound. Sort of like how there's the hive-claimed but more of a &quot;hive-bargained&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You just know someone is going to take inspiration from Lind from &quot;Oh My Goddess&quot; with that idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:36:08-07:00","id":966103,"title":"","content":"Forgive me if this gets at something else, but an a Geist sneak out of the Underworld by any means other than the Bargain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T00:37:41-07:00","id":966106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=966094#post966094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in the cpre, but it's a topic earmarked for the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would certainly be interesting, especially with the fact that it might be difficult to tell whether it's one geist with a number of aspects or multiple geister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T06:01:39-07:00","id":966161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=966094#post966094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A little bit in the core--maybe as much as the Pure got in Forsaken 2e. It's something I want to explore layer, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not in the cpre, but it's a topic earmarked for the future.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's great to hear!<br /> <br /> I'm wondering, would you say plasm is easier for a Sin-Eater to get in 2e than it was in 1e, or rather more options to regain it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T13:14:27-07:00","id":966408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=966103#post966103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this gets at something else, but an a Geist sneak out of the Underworld by any means other than the Bargain?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld hasn't really been covered in 2e but I assume Underworld Gate works in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Correction: The Underworld was briefly covered in Mage but not in a way that suggests how ghosts break out. Creating the Open condition on an Avernian Gateway then a Manifestation effect to open the gateway is what seems to be likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 09-09-2016, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:00:32-07:00","id":966527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=966103#post966103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this gets at something else, but an a Geist sneak out of the Underworld by any means other than the Bargain?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was sure geists had to be on the mortal plane when they make the bargain, so they already escaped the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T12:51:09-07:00","id":966869,"title":"","content":"following up on Runcible's question, will Pain Junkies still be a thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T00:33:37-07:00","id":967806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=966103#post966103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me if this gets at something else, but an a Geist sneak out of the Underworld by any means other than the Bargain?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the whole point of becoming a geist is to Anchor yourself to an abstract concept rather than a person, place, or object, and thus be way less vulnerable to being blasted away into the Underworld. They still have to find their way back out via an Avernian Gate or some other means, though, so you'll find plenty of unbound geists lurking both in the Underworld and in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HelmsDerp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=966869#post966869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">following up on Runcible's question, will Pain Junkies still be a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't even know what those are. Like, Bound who get off on pain because they know they can't really die? Sure, they probably exist, but they're not going to warrant proper-noun status or in-depth discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T03:57:08-07:00","id":967853,"title":"","content":"One of the ways to regain plasm in first edition was to cause or be the victim of injury lining up with your Threshold. There was a brief mention of some Bound getting addicted to the plasm rush and deliberately seeking out opportunities to get hurt (or hurt other people) for it. It's a neat mechanic with some interesting cross splat repercussions and I hope it survives the transition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:52:40-07:00","id":967875,"title":"","content":"Any chance there will be a (fill in the blank) Chronicle Anthology for Geist????","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T05:55:20-07:00","id":967877,"title":"","content":"The Geist stories in the Beast &amp; Dark Eras anthologies were awesome and I'd love to see more Sin-Eater fiction &amp; really get a feel for the Chronicles of Darkness from that perspective. If it comes out with the Changeling Anthology &amp; the Hunter Anthology (kinda like the Mage &amp; Promethean ones came out fairly close together with the werewolf one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T14:39:39-07:00","id":968148,"title":"","content":"Realized I left an unfinished sentence. If there is a REDACTED Chronicle Anthology for Geist and if it comes out with the Changeling &amp; Hunter anthologies that are in the works, I will be grinning for days <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:03:51-07:00","id":968405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968148#post968148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realized I left an unfinished sentence. If there is a REDACTED Chronicle Anthology for Geist and if it comes out with the Changeling &amp; Hunter anthologies that are in the works, I will be grinning for days <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>No idea when it will come out relative to the other Anthologies, but there will be one for Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T05:45:02-07:00","id":968466,"title":"","content":"Since Abmortals would be relegated to perhaps a future supplement, what about Deathlords? I'm not sure if they would be thematically relevant, and got hardly anything regarding them in 1e other than the conspiracies of knowing that there are some down in the underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T07:34:59-07:00","id":968509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968466#post968466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Abmortals would be relegated to perhaps a future supplement, what about Deathlords? I'm not sure if they would be thematically relevant, and got hardly anything regarding them in 1e other than the conspiracies of knowing that there are some down in the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh. I have <i>opinions</i> about the term &quot;Deathlords.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those opinions are &quot;It belongs in <i>Exalted</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T09:07:22-07:00","id":968554,"title":"","content":"Getting a new name like Manifestations to Haunts? Or replaced/reworked into something different and more thematic? Or has something to do with those redacted mask bearing ghosts? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T14:43:59-07:00","id":968750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968509#post968509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I have <i>opinions</i> about the term &quot;Deathlords.&quot;<br /> <br /> Those opinions are &quot;It belongs in <i>Exalted</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They were in Geist, but they were more a legend about the underworld - that each Threshold had a Deathlord attached, and that they ruled the underworld in a very distant fashion. Nobody has found a genuine Deathlord and lived to tell the tale, and most found are either Geists or Kerberos with high opinions of themselves. But still, it's pretty much stated they exist in some way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T15:30:15-07:00","id":968786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968750#post968750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were in Geist, but they were more a legend about the underworld - that each Threshold had a Deathlord attached</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't actually show up in the books, and the only place I can think of that it's come up is my own spitballing that Rank 8 ghosts are Threshold-embodying entities akin to the Shadow's greater Celestines. The line itself only really says that they're the mythical old gods that rule the Underworld and that regardless of whether they really exist there's definitely factions that claim to carry out their will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T16:19:47-07:00","id":968815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968509#post968509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heh. I have <i>opinions</i> about the term &amp;quot;Deathlords.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Those opinions are &amp;quot;It belongs in <i>Exalted</i>.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>So does that mean no Death Lords, or that they have a new name?<br /> <br /> also on another note will the 5 Horsemen of the apocalypse play a larger part in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T19:58:56-07:00","id":968948,"title":"","content":"I never found Deathlords to be relevant to the game. They existed supposedly. If their existence has a point then I have no issue with them returning. Otherwise, I can do without them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T00:03:12-07:00","id":969059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968815#post968815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does that mean no Death Lords, or that they have a new name?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Chthonic Gods&quot; just has such a nicer ring to it, don't you think?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=968815#post968815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also on another note will the 5 Horsemen of the apocalypse play a larger part in 2E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. 2e skews much more toward the personal and immediate than the grand, cosmic scope. Even when your krewe is actively pursuing a [REDACTED], it's about the direct impact your actions have on the people around you, not whatever arbitrarily-high Rank Underworld gribblies are doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T01:30:47-07:00","id":969088,"title":"","content":"The Cthonic Gods are in the &quot;Gaia, the Oracles, and the Principle&quot; realm of beings that might be inferred from a Rank chart, but don't functionally exist in the setting beyond other beings believing in them. As opposed to the &quot;Luna, Helios, the Judges, and the Exarchs&quot; realm of setting gods who will up and punch you in the junk if you take their name in vain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:23:08-07:00","id":969180,"title":"","content":"Since Geists might be getting more of a presence mechanically in the, is the synergy system different? Perhaps sorta like Deviant where there is two &quot;integrity&quot; meters, but one for the sin-eater and one for the geist and the ideal would be keeping the meters on both end on a close if not exact match for synergy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:26:45-07:00","id":969183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969180#post969180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Geists might be getting more of a presence mechanically in the, is the synergy system different? Perhaps sorta like Deviant where there is two &quot;integrity&quot; meters, but one for the sin-eater and one for the geist and the ideal would be keeping the meters on both end on a close if not exact match for synergy?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's different. Not like Deviant, but not like 1e Geist either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:29:54-07:00","id":969186,"title":"","content":"It's all been very intriguing stuff so far, looking forward to the open development blogs and most definitely looking forward to the full book!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T06:45:08-07:00","id":969194,"title":"","content":"Most the guesses about what Synergy will be most like in 2e has been assuming it'll be like Werewolf since it's all about balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:45:00-07:00","id":969220,"title":"","content":"I understand this is retreading back a few pages, but I just read this entire thread this morning and I had a lingering question that wasn't touched on: since Geister are ghosts which drank deep from one of the rivers of the Underworld, can we expect the Underworld to keep its traditional five rivers and for each Threshold to be thematically tied to one of the rivers? Maybe even instead of a Horseman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T07:51:48-07:00","id":969227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969220#post969220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand this is retreading back a few pages, but I just read this entire thread this morning and I had a lingering question that wasn't touched on: since Geister are ghosts which drank deep from one of the rivers of the Underworld, can we expect the Underworld to keep its traditional five rivers and for each Threshold to be thematically tied to one of the rivers? Maybe even instead of a Horseman?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot more than five Rivers. No comment on the rest at this time. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":12259,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","user":"GimpInBlack","date":". 09-14-2016, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T08:53:36-07:00","id":969246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969227#post969227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are a lot more than five Rivers. No comment on the rest at this time. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Answers my unspoken question of whether or not the non-Greek rivers were being kept from 1e. <br /> <br /> Speaking of those non-Greek rivers, there's one in particular that I'm wondering about. Specifically in regards to its potential connection to &quot;Appendix One?&quot; How cold am I?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:00:36-07:00","id":969249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969059#post969059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Chthonic Gods&quot; just has such a nicer ring to it, don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know- it sounds a bit clumsy and too similar to Chthonians. Other than that, what I've liked about the term &quot;Deathlords&quot; was that it gave them a majestic outlook- it made you think about Death as a ruler, as collector of wealth, as an eternal power which sits upon a stony throne. Chthonic Gods makes me think about something lowly, twisted and earthly, something dirty and foul which clings to others.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I am a visual thinker and has a certain level of synesthesia, so feel free to ignore everything I've just said :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:01:34-07:00","id":969250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969249#post969249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know- it sounds a bit clumsy and too similar to Chthonians. Other than that, what I've liked about the term &quot;Deathlords&quot; was that it gave them a majestic outlook- it made you think about Death as a ruler, as collector of wealth, as an eternal power which sits upon a stony throne. Chthonic Gods makes me think about something lowly, twisted and earthly, something dirty and foul which clings to others.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I am a visual thinker and has a certain level of synesthesia, so feel free to ignore everything I've just said :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Those connotations are intentional. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:19:23-07:00","id":969263,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna have to make it a thing in one of my campaigns to seek a ghost/geist that has made it its goal to try to drink from all the rivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-14T09:43:36-07:00","id":969282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969250#post969250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those connotations are intentional. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>in that case- I must say I'm looking forward to the new edition even more than before","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T06:22:44-07:00","id":969847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969059#post969059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. 2e skews much more toward the personal and immediate than the grand, cosmic scope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, I liked the Thresholds being based on the Five Horsemen. If there's no more Horsemen, will the Thresholds be any different than before? Certain Thresholds would have had higher numbers anyway (Stricken would have drastically outnumbered everyone, since Cholera alone has probably killed the most human beings ever). When can we see previews and spoilers? I'm so excited for it.<br /> Re: the connotations of Cthonic Gods, the images that kind of thing conjures in my mind would be like Aldrich, Devourer of Gods from <i>Dark Souls III</i>. A hideous black sludge that takes on the form of those it devours or dreams. Complete with a pretty boy's body and a gross mass of bones and dirt for legs.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette1.wikia.nocookie.net/villains/images/a/a6/Aldritch_Dark_Souls_III_1.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20160723162002\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>Although a 'thing' with me for Geister and ghosts is that they should never have eyes... Normal eyes make them to 'human'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T07:38:45-07:00","id":969890,"title":"","content":"Since Synergy is getting a change up, will Psyche also be getting an update for the plus side and downsides of high psyche (IE: Needing to stay in the Underworld for basically half your life at Psyche 10) or would it mostly be the same? That being said, they also had just about the biggest &quot;fuel&quot; pool with plasm and generally out of all the splats were usually the ones to blow through all their fuel reserves the most frequently. Would that be something they are retaining, or is their Plasm pool and expenditure getting a bit of a trim?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:38:38-07:00","id":970025,"title":"","content":"Any chance of a blog post by Halloween? It is the ghostiest day of the Western world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T10:54:40-07:00","id":970042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970025#post970025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance of a blog post by Halloween? It is the ghostiest day of the Western world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> That's a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T12:45:08-07:00","id":970117,"title":"","content":"something I've thought about- does the new Edition going to expand on the &quot;Neolithic Bound&quot; idea of people who get a Chtonian in their body instead of a Geist, or leave it undefined as is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:05:22-07:00","id":970258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970117#post970117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've thought about- does the new Edition going to expand on the &amp;quot;Neolithic Bound&amp;quot; idea of people who get a Chtonian in their body instead of a Geist, or leave it undefined as is?</div> </div> </div> </div> Ooohhhh, that's a good question, could lead up to a creepier breed of Bound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T16:59:04-07:00","id":970314,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a> According to Mage, Ghosts and Cthonians have the same Ranks. So Lares, and by extension Geister, can be Cthonian or Ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:12:20-07:00","id":970321,"title":"","content":"The Cthonian rules might be a weee bit more detailed than &quot;just use ghost rules, yo&quot; in a game line which a) deals with the Underworld all of the time and b) has more than 30 words to spare towards them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:32:01-07:00","id":970333,"title":"","content":"That sounds fun, any chance for the book might mention if/what happens if a Cthonian gets loose in the material world through an Avernian Gate or some other accident?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","user":"Runcible","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T20:31:51-07:00","id":970446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970117#post970117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've thought about- does the new Edition going to expand on the &amp;quot;Neolithic Bound&amp;quot; idea of people who get a Chtonian in their body instead of a Geist, or leave it undefined as is?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be an excellent addition, if not in core, then in Night Horrors or another supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:14:41-07:00","id":970544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969890#post969890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Synergy is getting a change up, will Psyche also be getting an update for the plus side and downsides of high psyche (IE: Needing to stay in the Underworld for basically half your life at Psyche 10) or would it mostly be the same? That being said, they also had just about the biggest &quot;fuel&quot; pool with plasm and generally out of all the splats were usually the ones to blow through all their fuel reserves the most frequently. Would that be something they are retaining, or is their Plasm pool and expenditure getting a bit of a trim?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters will not be forced to spend large chunks of their time in the Underworld, no. The Underworld is where a lot of the story happens; I don't need sticks to get you there when I have all these lovely, lovely carrots.<br /> <br /> Spending lots of Plasm is still part of the design of their powers, because slinging around buckets of ghost snot is cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970117#post970117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">something I've thought about- does the new Edition going to expand on the &quot;Neolithic Bound&quot; idea of people who get a Chtonian in their body instead of a Geist, or leave it undefined as is?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's another one of those topics ideally suited for a supplement, but not really a good fit for the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:46:01-07:00","id":970590,"title":"","content":"hey Travis I got to ask, just how different will mementos be in 2E? the were honestly my favorite part if Geist. so I can wait to see how the turn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T03:07:15-07:00","id":970605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970590#post970590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hey Travis I got to ask, just how different will mementos be in 2E? the were honestly my favorite part if Geist. so I can wait to see how the turn out.</div> </div> </div> </div>They've been cleaned up a lot mechanically, but within the fiction they're largely the same: they're still objects touched by the energies of death, they still have Keys, and they still have weird little side-effects in the vein of Objects in <i>The Lost Room</i>, but there are no longer five wholly different kinds of Memento with different mechanics for each.<br /> <br /> They're also a lot more integral to Sin-Eaters' powers, so you have a lot of incentive to seek them out and carry them around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:23:24-07:00","id":970633,"title":"","content":"&quot;Spending lots of Plasm is still part of the design of their powers, because slinging around buckets of ghost snot is cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> I started laughing so hard I'm convinced my cat Shadow thinks I'd lost my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:24:04-07:00","id":970635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970321#post970321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cthonian rules might be a weee bit more detailed than &amp;quot;just use ghost rules, yo&amp;quot; in a game line which a) deals with the Underworld all of the time and b) has more than 30 words to spare towards them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Excellent point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:35:31-07:00","id":970639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970544#post970544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin-Eaters will not be forced to spend large chunks of their time in the Underworld, no. The Underworld is where a lot of the story happens; I don't need sticks to get you there when I have all these lovely, lovely carrots.<br /> <br /> Spending lots of Plasm is still part of the design of their powers, because slinging around buckets of ghost snot is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd have to agree spending lots of plasm and having high reserves is pretty cool. It does also help set them apart from other splats that have much smaller pools or generally don't have to spend fuel to get an effect unless they want a stronger particular effect.<br /> <br /> Does this mean high psyche now has a new downside since sin-eaters won't necessarily be forced to spend large chunks of time there? :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970605#post970605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They've been cleaned up a lot mechanically, but within the fiction they're largely the same: they're still objects touched by the energies of death, they still have Keys, and they still have weird little side-effects in the vein of Objects in <i>The Lost Room</i>, but there are no longer five wholly different kinds of Memento with different mechanics for each.<br /> <br /> They're also a lot more integral to Sin-Eaters' powers, so you have a lot of incentive to seek them out and carry them around.</div> </div> </div> </div>So mementos are no longer 5 different tiers/categories of varying effect bonuses? Is it more of just kind of a merger amongst most of them for what they are and only split up when it comes to a more significant difference, like Death masks and Memorabilia?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T05:58:18-07:00","id":970643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970639#post970639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So mementos are no longer 5 different tiers/categories of varying effect bonuses? Is it more of just kind of a merger amongst most of them for what they are and only split up when it comes to a more significant difference, like Death masks and Memorabilia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. A Memento is a Memento is a Memento, whether it's a ghost's resolved Anchor, a piece of artwork on the nature of death created by a Sin-Eater directly, or what have you. Deathmasks are sort of a separate thing now that don't quite fit under the Memento umbrella.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:33:53-07:00","id":970651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970643#post970643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. A Memento is a Memento is a Memento, whether it's a ghost's resolved Anchor, a piece of artwork on the nature of death created by a Sin-Eater directly, or what have you. Deathmasks are sort of a separate thing now that don't quite fit under the Memento umbrella.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good. Deathmasks always seemed a little shoehorned into that category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T07:26:17-07:00","id":970676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970643#post970643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct. A Memento is a Memento is a Memento, whether it's a ghost's resolved Anchor, a piece of artwork on the nature of death created by a Sin-Eater directly, or what have you. Deathmasks are sort of a separate thing now that don't quite fit under the Memento umbrella.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds pretty understandable, are Deathmasks getting a change from their original benefits to help distance them mementos, or is it because of a lore update/change on what Deathmasks are? Or both? Perhaps there new category has something to do with these new spooky ghosts that have masks? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:18:19-07:00","id":970825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962164#post962164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope! But that's a really cool idea. Maybe if Geist gets a Night Horrors book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hooray! a compliment<br /> Also,i gotta know. what do a ghost needs to be able to reach rank 5? is going to the underworld strictly necessary?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T04:15:30-07:00","id":971248,"title":"","content":"So deathmasks are still in? Awesome, I always liked them. <br /> <br /> And oh my god, what I'd do for a Geist NH book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:58:51-07:00","id":971477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=969847#post969847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although a 'thing' with me for Geister and ghosts is that they should never have eyes... Normal eyes make them to 'human'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta agree with you there. I want my ghosts so ghostly they forgot what it was like to be human to look it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8509-ketharuil","name":"Ketharuil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:03:37-07:00","id":971484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970544#post970544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't need sticks to get you there when I have all these lovely, lovely carrots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the carrot approach to things. Not enough games use it. Always gotta be beating you over the head with a stick. Either way, I can't wait to see the role Cthonians are gonna play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8509-ketharuil","name":"Ketharuil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:51:28-07:00","id":972240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970633#post970633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Spending lots of Plasm is still part of the design of their powers, because slinging around buckets of ghost snot is cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> I started laughing so hard I'm convinced my cat Shadow thinks I'd lost my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just did the same thing and I think my fuzzies are now in agreement with Shadow.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Mr. Stout,<br /> Thank you very much - these updates have been fantastic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:24:14-07:00","id":973894,"title":"","content":"Since the new Ghost Rider popped up on tv last night I figured I'd ask, would something like the Robbie Reyes Ghost Rider with Eli (the spirit in him) be along the lines of a 2e Geist using a bargain or Geist Claimed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T00:26:19-07:00","id":974275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=973894#post973894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the new Ghost Rider popped up on tv last night I figured I'd ask, would something like the Robbie Reyes Ghost Rider with Eli (the spirit in him) be along the lines of a 2e Geist using a bargain or Geist Claimed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not super familiar with the Robbie incarnation of Ghost Rider, sorry. I did watch Agents of SHIELD last night, though, and it sure looks like he's using a lot of the Caul and the Rage. And, well, the Pyre-Flame Key, obviously. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:23:47-07:00","id":974364,"title":"","content":"Ah, well. In summary Robbie was in a muscle car that got gunned down and while he was bleeding out he heard of a voice and rose up from the dead on fire. They're not quite like all the other Ghost Riders, Eli's a spirit that talks, manipulates and occasionally tries to threaten Robbie, but the best example to sum it up would be the exchange from these three pages. :P<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/PTjrl\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/PTjrl\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://imgur.com/a/PTjrl\" target=\"_blank\"> http://imgur.com/a/PTjrl </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:48:08-07:00","id":974377,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a Bargain, to me, at least. He's asking permission, not &quot;lol, ready or not, Fusion Dance time!&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:03:36-07:00","id":974419,"title":"","content":"I thought so as well, was just curious as to whether a Ghost Rider, or more specifically that one, would fall under either category, or if Ghost Riders in general could fit the templates of the Bound, since there are cases of some agreeing to it and some having it forced onto them. :P<br /> <br /> I figure something like the surrounded by fire would be a pyre-flame caul, penance stare is probably a rage haunt, since the muscle character is essentially Eli's anchor I'd say maybe a weird case of keystone or a level of memorabilia memento from 1e (JFK's assassination car was one), and Robbie's skull helmet as probably a Death mask (It's a kind of weird organic and metallic combination of a helmet and a skull).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:27:26-07:00","id":976509,"title":"","content":"so I got a question Travis, is ectoplasm just ghost essence or is it something else entirely? Because I know both Mage and Vampire referred to it, but sense this is the ghost game I figured you'd got the answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10820,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","user":"Blakemikizuki","date":". 09-26-2016, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T07:37:12-07:00","id":976511,"title":"","content":"You know how the God Machine's angels run on Essence, but produce Aether as a sort of byproduct? Plasm kind of like that with ghosts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T08:10:17-07:00","id":976523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=976511#post976511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how the God Machine's angels run on Essence, but produce Aether as a sort of byproduct? Plasm kind of like that with ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plasm is to ghosts as Aether is to angels, yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T09:03:49-07:00","id":976552,"title":"","content":"So it's a waste product produced by a ghost using his Essence to power Numina? Because from what I remember of GMC, ghosts using Essence <i>also</i> produced Aether. I might be remembering that wrong as I don't have the book in front of me. It happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:27:38-07:00","id":977038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frishman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=976552#post976552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's a waste product produced by a ghost using his Essence to power Numina? Because from what I remember of GMC, ghosts using Essence <i>also</i> produced Aether. I might be remembering that wrong as I don't have the book in front of me. It happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Manifestations, actually, not Numina--and Manifestation Conditions produce it on the regular as long as they last (though that may change if playtesting shows there's still not enough to go around). Haunted houses are very nice sources of Plasm, and Avernian Gateways are downright <i>soupy</i> with the stuff (though having a door to the Underworld in your backyard has its own problems).<br /> <br /> And unless there's a weird ghost-harvesting Merit tucked away in a book somewhere, you're misremembering re: Aether. Only angels spending Essence and the God-Machine directly manipulating reality via Infrastructure generate Aether, ghosts have nothing to do with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T05:29:33-07:00","id":977132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977038#post977038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manifestations, actually, not Numina--and Manifestation Conditions produce it on the regular as long as they last (though that may change if playtesting shows there's still not enough to go around). Haunted houses are very nice sources of Plasm, and Avernian Gateways are downright <i>soupy</i> with the stuff (though having a door to the Underworld in your backyard has its own problems).<br /> <br /> And unless there's a weird ghost-harvesting Merit tucked away in a book somewhere, you're misremembering re: Aether. Only angels spending Essence and the God-Machine directly manipulating reality via Infrastructure generate Aether, ghosts have nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it happens. I've got Demon: the Descent in front of me and I was probably crossing wires from the Essence Thief Numina. I will keep my mouth shut from here on out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T14:58:06-07:00","id":977418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977038#post977038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manifestations, actually, not Numina--and Manifestation Conditions produce it on the regular as long as they last (though that may change if playtesting shows there's still not enough to go around). Haunted houses are very nice sources of Plasm, and Avernian Gateways are downright <i>soupy</i> with the stuff (though having a door to the Underworld in your backyard has its own problems).<br /> <br /> And unless there's a weird ghost-harvesting Merit tucked away in a book somewhere, you're misremembering re: Aether. Only angels spending Essence and the God-Machine directly manipulating reality via Infrastructure generate Aether, ghosts have nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>wait are ectoplasm from ghost and the plasm used by Sin-Eaters the same? I thought they were different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T20:44:10-07:00","id":977575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977418#post977418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> wait are ectoplasm from ghost and the plasm used by Sin-Eaters the same? I thought they were different.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is that ectoplasm is what ghosts are composed of, and plasm is the energy that death creates; ectoplasm is to a ghost what flesh is to a human. Ghosts and Sin Eaters both need plasm to function, but ghosts create it naturally simply by the virtue of being dead, whereas Sin Eaters require it for their powers and can only produce it under certain circumstances that reflect their own averted death. This is partially why Sin Eaters can eat ghosts, as a way to give them a quick and easy method of gaining plasm.<br /> <br /> Bear in mind, though, that's from first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 09-27-2016, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T00:55:19-07:00","id":977653,"title":"","content":"Not quite; you're thinking of &quot;ephemera.&quot; Ghosts are made of <i>ephemera</i> and require <i>Essence</i> to continue existing and to fuel their powers. <i>Plasm</i> is a corporeal side product of ghosts spending Essence on Manifestations, the presence of Manifestation Conditions, and a few other sources (e.g. you can scarf down a Memento for Plasm, assuming you can get it down your neck).<br /> <br /> It's like the scene in the 1984 <i>Ghostbusters</i> where they're exploring the library and they find all that goop on the card catalogues: the Librarian ghost had made the stacks Open, which resulted in Plasm as a residual effect. Had Egon been a Sin-Eater, he could have consumed it (preferably in a manner resonant with his own death); otherwise it would sublimate shortly after being collected.<br /> <br /> The one exception to all this is eating ghosts directly: because of the Bargain, which makes Sin-Eaters partly ghost-like themselves, they can tear hunks out of ghosts and eat them for Plasm even if the ghost isn't Manifesting at the time--the ephemera converts into Plasm as it's being eaten. Other folks who try to eat ghosts for the supernatural power they contain aren't so lucky: they need to rely on occult rituals or weird science or some other means to render ephemera into tangible Plasm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Travis Stout<br /> Geist 2e Developer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack","name":"GimpInBlack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:37:47-07:00","id":977660,"title":"","content":"Plasm also counts as Open for ghosts, so if one ghost possesses something and gets it covered it gunk then leaves, another ghost can have a go without building up the Conditions.<br /> <br /> (The plasm in a Sin Eater is already being used. By their Geist.)<br /> <br /> The two spells in mage that produce &quot;ectoplasm&quot; are, yes, making Plasm as in the Bound fuel trait. Mages are just sufficiently up themselves to not shorten the word.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T05:41:11-07:00","id":977704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=958121#post958121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI'll just say this: It's still fundamentally the same game about people who have died and come back thanks to the intervention of a spooky ghost-thing... but aside from that it's probably going to see the most mechanical differences compared to its first edition of any CofD game so far.<br /> <br /> If I had to pick two inspirational media that really nail the tone we're going for with Geist, it would be <i>Mama</i> and <i>ParaNorman</i>. Make of that what you will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=958128#post958128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say rather that it is <i>hopeful</i>. Every ghost story is, at its core, a tragedy--someone died, and they left something terribly important unfinished. Injustices were done and never righted. Lovers torn from one another, grand dreams thrown into the dark below to be forgotten.<br /> <br /> Geist is a game about looking at that state of affairs and saying &quot;No.&quot; And then being able to back that up with action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice to see that the premise for the game is more or less the same, and it's going to get a lot of streamlining and improvement. I'm looking forward to more updates on this, seeing as me and my sister are fans of this splat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=958197#post958197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, since the 2nd Edition ephemeral entities rules co-opted the term &quot;Manifestation,&quot; bare minimum you can expect them to be called something different. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Something like Locks, perhaps? Arcanist used that term in place of Manifestations for his Sin-Eater conversions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962818#post962818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keys are still in, but the powers are getting a major overhaul. It's still too early for me to want to talk about mechanics, but it's not going to be the same system as 1e. For one thing, trying to design and balance a full set of powers for every Key/Haunt* combo is an incredibly difficult task, and leads to a lot of weird, athematic powers. For another, space is a concern for PoD books. Geist 1e spent 37,000 words in Manifestations and Keys; we have about 25k for the topic. And finally, I'd like Geist to get some actual supplements this time around, and the logistics of trying to add new powers to a grid like that is a nightmare.<br /> <br /> So expect a tighter, more thematic power set this time around. We're experimenting with some pretty cool stuff, though comma that I think will make them feel pretty mechanically distinct from the other spots.<br /> <br /> * Spoiler. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I stand corrected. Not sure if I prefer that term over Lock/Seal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=959701#post959701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neither ghosts nor abmortals are in the Antagonists chapter. Make ofthat what you will. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'm really happy with the antagonists we have, though, and I think you all will be too. [REDACTED] are especially creepy, and [REDACTED] are goddamn <i>terrifying</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, <i>now</i> I want to know who/what [REDACTED] is. On a different note, this does allow for homebrewing a conversion for Abmortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=960327#post960327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Krewes building their own mystery religion is still in. Geists transforming into/revealing mythological aspects is out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that pretty much lines up with what was covered on Sin-Eaters in the Pack. That said, I do hope the mystery religion aspect of a Krewe is streamlined.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=959783#post959783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">Beware of ghosts bearing masks.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Especially</i> when you are teasing us with very small tidbits like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=960427#post960427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably around November/December, if I had to guess.<br /> <br /> Geists are pretty direct beings. Not a whole lot of dissimulation there. If your geist is the King-That-Was, who is the amalgamated ghost of every monarch who was murderously deposed, it's going to factor into your mystery religion as &quot;the amalgamated ghost of every monarch who was murderously deposed.&quot; Of course, that's assuming your krewe is building its religion around geists as deities/mythic figures and not some other foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. Aside from getting hyped that the open developments will start a little after my birthday, the way you describe Geists really makes them similar to spirits in that they embody/reflect concepts. That said, it gives some deeper context into how mixed packs/krewes mesh together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962230#post962230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an Appendix in the vein of the ones in Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage yes. Not going to spoil who it's about just yet, but I will say it's written by the brilliant Filamena Young, who also wrote Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, and Proximi, so if you liked those sections, I think you'll like what we've got planned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=964390#post964390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">David Hill is already after me to let him share the draft, but I want more time to blog about the underlying changes first. But it's awesome as usual. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's Tokyo. I'd be surprised if it wasn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=965548#post965548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ceremonies look a lot more like Forsaken 2e rites now--some suggestions for symbolism/ritual actions to provide a guideline, but you can and should decide for yourself what that specific ceremomy looks like for your krewe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew it would be converted into that format. It does make me wonder if Synergy might be handled in a manner similar to Harmony for 2E.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=967806#post967806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the whole point of becoming a geist is to Anchor yourself to an abstract concept rather than a person, place, or object, and thus be way less vulnerable to being blasted away into the Underworld. They still have to find their way back out via an Avernian Gate or some other means, though, so you'll find plenty of unbound geists lurking both in the Underworld and in Twilight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence, a number of possible story hooks in any Sin-Eater Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970321#post970321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Cthonian rules might be a weee bit more detailed than &quot;just use ghost rules, yo&quot; in a game line which a) deals with the Underworld all of the time and b) has more than 30 words to spare towards them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really do like to see how they will be handled, especially since it was implied(?) that Cthonians were the ones who originally made pacts with Sin-Eaters far back in the past.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=970605#post970605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They've been cleaned up a lot mechanically, but within the fiction they're largely the same: they're still objects touched by the energies of death, they still have Keys, and they still have weird little side-effects in the vein of Objects in <i>The Lost Room</i>, but there are no longer five wholly different kinds of Memento with different mechanics for each.<br /> <br /> They're also a lot more integral to Sin-Eaters' powers, so you have a lot of incentive to seek them out and carry them around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really hope this is one of the first things previewed, come open development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T07:59:06-07:00","id":977766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977653#post977653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one exception to all this is eating ghosts directly: because of the Bargain, which makes Sin-Eaters partly ghost-like themselves, they can tear hunks out of ghosts and eat them for Plasm even if the ghost isn't Manifesting at the time--the ephemera converts into Plasm as it's being eaten. Other folks who try to eat ghosts for the supernatural power they contain aren't so lucky: they need to rely on occult rituals or weird science or some other means to render ephemera into tangible Plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <i>technically</i> Ghosts in Twilight are still using the Twilight Form Manifestation, right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977660#post977660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are just sufficiently up themselves to not shorten the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right for Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:51:22-07:00","id":977813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977660#post977660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. Mages are just sufficiently up themselves to not shorten the word.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or the reverse, Sin-Eaters are sufficiently avant garde to slang it up and shorten it. (Or both really).<br /> <br /> Edit: And now I want to write it as 'plasm. Like a shortened form and 'pataphysics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:36:20-07:00","id":977863,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> You don't need a Manifestation to exist in your normal form. Otherwise every Ghost would have it's first Manifestation locked down by that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:47:49-07:00","id":977868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977863#post977863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> You don't need a Manifestation to exist in your normal form. Otherwise every Ghost would have it's first Manifestation locked down by that.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Ghosts, Spirits, and Angels (but not Goetia) explicitly get Twilight Form for free, and it is called out as a prerequisite to exist in Twilight (and why Goetia normally can't).<br /> <br /> EDIT: You might be able to have Spirits or Ghosts that <i>lack</i> Twilight Form, which would mean they are restricted to the Shadow and Underworld, respectively, much like Goetia are restricted to the Astral (normally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T15:33:27-07:00","id":978004,"title":"","content":"Given how the new antagonists are replacing abmortals, I'm going to assume one type is a variety of necromancer. And given their link to masks, and how fascinated Sin-Eaters are with idiosyncratic identities, I'm going to guess the other is about destroying identity=some kind of anti-Geist (who became part-spirits out of the desire to <i>have </i>an identity).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T19:44:19-07:00","id":978150,"title":"","content":"To be fair, destruction of identity is something the Underworld itself kind of seems to push for, what with the Ocean of Fragments. Which (if they are indeed connected to identity loss) makes one wonder if and <i>how</i> the mask-bearing ghosts might fit into the bigger picture... are they some kind of ghostly &quot;cult&quot; dedicated to the Ocean? Or maybe, somehow, some kind of &quot;mechanism&quot; of the Underworld itself?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T20:21:48-07:00","id":978162,"title":"","content":"Masked ghosts? Makes me think of the Hollows from the anime series <a href=\"http://www.goodmanga.net/4/bleach\" target=\"_blank\">Bleach</a>...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T21:03:14-07:00","id":978176,"title":"","content":"Will Bound still have that death sight thing that lets them see the amount of lifetime a person has remaining over their heads?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T22:15:44-07:00","id":978209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=978176#post978176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Bound still have that death sight thing that lets them see the amount of lifetime a person has remaining over their heads?</div> </div> </div> </div>They didn't have that before. You're thinking of Death Note. The Sin-Eater counterpart was being able to tell how old people were, spot the walking dead, and register people who were on track to die as the relevant Threshold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T00:44:11-07:00","id":978259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=978209#post978209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They didn't have that before. You're thinking of Death Note. The Sin-Eater counterpart was being able to tell how old people were, spot the walking dead, and register people who were on track to die as the relevant Threshold.</div> </div> </div> </div>That last trait I was unaware of. I really hope that the second edition does a better job of relaying this info than first edition did; while it means each new read offers something new, it also means you play with half the game unknown. It is a problem Beast has to a degree, such as in building up your legend. I only learned about it after a friend told me about it, and it was something he only found after a long time with the book.<br /> <br /> Then again, I have missed obvious details before...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:13:34-07:00","id":978913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=978162#post978162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Masked ghosts? Makes me think of the Hollows from the anime series <a href=\"http://www.goodmanga.net/4/bleach\" target=\"_blank\">Bleach</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Bleach may be a convoluted mess, but those early episodes are basically how I ran my Geist game. I even called it Sin-eater Soul Reapers. Just teenagers going around solving GHOST MYSTERIES.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5557_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5557\" data-vbnamecard=\"5557\">Runcible</a> Satchel's right about Sin-eaters not seeing the time until someone's death, like in Death Note or <a href=\"https://youtu.be/jPc-o-4Nsbk\" target=\"_blank\">the Saving Me music video</a>. It's more of a health meter, showing how injured someone is, and how much closer they are to inching towards their natural death. It shows how long they <i>have</i> lived, how injured they are, and if they've been stained by Death in some way. I liken it to being able to view health bars. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I definitely don't recall anything about being able to see what threshold someone <i>would</i> become. That wouldn't even work with anything other than Stricken.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5803_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5803\" data-vbnamecard=\"5803\">Taidragon</a> Beast is like Geist 2: Electric Boogaloo. A lot of the same problems of lack of focus, mostly due to having no social groups.<br /> <br /> Which on that note... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12259-gimpinblack\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12259\" data-vbnamecard=\"12259\">GimpInBlack</a> will Geist 2e keep that whole &quot;no social groups&quot; thing? I feel like not having a Y-Splat really hurt 1e, and having Carnivals or something as dedicated sociopolitical groups would really help Geist, even if it's closer to Changeling 2e's Courts, and more of a local thing than a global thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:35:49-07:00","id":978923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=978913#post978913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> I definitely don't recall anything about being able to see what threshold someone <i>would</i> become. That wouldn't even work with anything other than Stricken.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Even living people have a Threshold, though they don\u2019t know it until the moment of their demise. Sin-Eaters can sense imminent death as plain as day, and a man two days away from being stabbed to death over a card game is no less one of the Torn than the Sin-Eater who took a bullet in the lung.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Once the Sin-Eater arrives at the location, it becomes a matter of discerning who the potential victim will be. Sometimes it is easily apparent, as the geist comes upon a car accident, a gang fight, or a bout of domestic violence. Other times it is as easy as looking for a person tainted by death (see Morbid Reality).&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-30-2016, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T01:36:43-07:00","id":978924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=978913#post978913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which on that note... GimpInBlack will Geist 2e keep that whole &quot;no social groups&quot; thing? I feel like not having a Y-Splat really hurt 1e, and having Carnivals or something as dedicated sociopolitical groups would really help Geist, even if it's closer to Changeling 2e's Courts, and more of a local thing than a global thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they had a Y-Splat, the Archetypes. It's just more like 2e changeling seemings/promethean refinements/demon's agenda's rather than vampires covenants/mage's orders. I don't think geists should have a vampire-like y-splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T08:52:58-07:00","id":979076,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'd seriously rethink Archetypes in light of ChroD's Aspirations and Anchors changes. Heck, with all the terminology changes we're likely to get, I wouldn't mind if \u201cThreshold\u201d and \u201cArchetype\u201d instead became \u201cDeath\u201d and \u201cLife\u201d, and were treated more like a second set of Anchors than like splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:26:31-07:00","id":979142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=979076#post979076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd seriously rethink Archetypes in light of ChroD's Aspirations and Anchors changes. Heck, with all the terminology changes we're likely to get, I wouldn't mind if \u201cThreshold\u201d and \u201cArchetype\u201d instead became \u201cDeath\u201d and \u201cLife\u201d, and were treated more like a second set of Anchors than like splats.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interesting idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T10:34:19-07:00","id":979146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977038#post977038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Manifestations, actually, not Numina--and Manifestation Conditions produce it on the regular as long as they last (though that may change if playtesting shows there's still not enough to go around). Haunted houses are very nice sources of Plasm, and Avernian Gateways are downright <i>soupy</i> with the stuff (though having a door to the Underworld in your backyard has its own problems).<br /> <br /> And unless there's a weird ghost-harvesting Merit tucked away in a book somewhere, you're misremembering re: Aether. Only angels spending Essence and the God-Machine directly manipulating reality via Infrastructure generate Aether, ghosts have nothing to do with it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Given that a Gravewright Changeling can cause and remove manifestations from a ghost, that means by spending Glamouring they can easily help generate Plasm.<br /> <br /> Actually so can Mages, they can do all kinds of manifestations. A Master of the Death Arcana should leave a trail, from summoning/creating ghosts, forcing them to manifest and possibly other magics, that a Sin Eater could vaccum up.<br /> <br /> Ghost Claimed would also be a good source.<br /> <br /> Actually a Gravewright with the Exotic Airs merit for Ghosts and one for Sin Eaters, should be able to gain glamour from them, then use that to add Manifestation conditions to Ghosts, to boost Plasm production.<br /> <br /> I could see a Glamour for Plasm trade between Sin Eaters and Gravewright Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-30-2016, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T06:43:16-07:00","id":979624,"title":"","content":"Travis, I know the official website development blogs for Geist won't be getting posted for a few months, but would you mind perhaps telling us the names of the Virtue/Vice anchors for Geist 2E you have in mind? and perhaps let us know if the &quot;Threshold&quot; &amp; &quot;Archetype&quot; titles will remain for the splats or if you and your team are changing them to different splat names? Hope the weekend is off to a good start!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:57:50-07:00","id":979898,"title":"","content":"hopes no one minds me asking another question. <br /> Travis how will Psychopomp be handled in Geist 2? Will they become more important maybe become guides in the underworld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T23:59:51-07:00","id":981301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=979076#post979076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd seriously rethink Archetypes in light of ChroD's Aspirations and Anchors changes. Heck, with all the terminology changes we're likely to get, I wouldn't mind if \u201cThreshold\u201d and \u201cArchetype\u201d instead became \u201cDeath\u201d and \u201cLife\u201d, and were treated more like a second set of Anchors than like splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am in total agreement on archetypes needing rethinking. Geist was the game that introduced me to tabletop RPGs so I was pretty ignorant to its problems until recently, but even from the beginning, archetypes were never really well-developed, particularly since they're supposed to help define a character. I understand the spirit behind them (no pun intended) but in practice they were too broad, and really, with things like advocate and gate keeper in particular, those are things I envision every sin eater doing at some point anyway.<br /> <br /> I think the problem is, unlike changeling kiths and and promethean refinements, there's no in-story reason for the delineation. I understand them being kind of nicknames, but there's no reason that as a whole, sin-eaters would consider these archetypes as sweeping categories for themselves unlike kiths which have physical manifestations and refinments, which while similar, actually affect the prometheans abilities. I think folding them into the anchor system would make more sense, in fact they actually wouldn't need any significant changes.<br /> <br /> On another note, I'm glad the tone for Geist will still be hopeful and leaning to a lighter shade of grey. That was always my favorite thing about Geist-that unlike werewolf or vampire, your character can actually have a happy ending. Or at least a not violent and horrific one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T02:57:26-07:00","id":981364,"title":"","content":"I think a case could be made that <i>every</i> archetype is something that any given Sin-Eater is likely to engage in at some point or another. I suppose the idea is that each player is supposed to pick which segment of Sin-Eater life his character finds most enjoyable (and thus gets Plasm for)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T13:06:56-07:00","id":982289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=977660#post977660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plasm also counts as Open for ghosts, so if one ghost possesses something and gets it covered it gunk then leaves, another ghost can have a go without building up the Conditions.<br /> <br /> (The plasm in a Sin Eater is already being used. By their Geist.)<br /> <br /> The two spells in mage that produce &quot;ectoplasm&quot; are, yes, making Plasm as in the Bound fuel trait. Mages are just sufficiently up themselves to not shorten the word.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does Plasm count as Anchor for ghosts? That is, does being close enough to Plasm stop a ghost's Essence bleed, even if the ghost hasn't manifested in one of the ways that prevent it?<br /> <br /> If so, how long does &quot;natural&quot; Plasm last?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:12:12-07:00","id":982385,"title":"","content":"I can see Sin-Eaters being the mercs of CoD, its so easy for other splats to create plasm.<br /> <br /> Mage creates plasm which Sin Eater eats up, which a Beast watches, sharing in the feast, which a Changeling with the exotic airs merit for Beasts harvests for the emotinal impact on the Beast, which a Vampire with the right merit sees, which incites them to feed on the Changeling.<br /> <br /> The CoD cycle of (un)life.<br /> <br /> Also for some reason I never made the ectoplasm=plasm connection before David pointed it out for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 10-05-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T20:11:54-07:00","id":984191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=982385#post982385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Sin-Eaters being the mercs of CoD, its so easy for other splats to create plasm.<br /> <br /> Mage creates plasm which Sin Eater eats up, which a Beast watches, sharing in the feast, which a Changeling with the exotic airs merit for Beasts harvests for the emotinal impact on the Beast, which a Vampire with the right merit sees, which incites them to feed on the Changeling.<br /> <br /> The CoD cycle of (un)life.<br /> <br /> Also for some reason I never made the ectoplasm=plasm connection before David pointed it out for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Vampire uses Blood Tenebrous to create Essence to give to a Werewolf, who in turn feeds it to a spirit, who is hit by a ghost with the Drain Numen, who then creates Plasm for a Sin-eater, who then goes off to party with his Changeling buddies, producing Glamour for them, then they trade it to a Mage for protection, who uses a Fate spell to convert it to Mana, and later converts that Mana, all while a Beast follows it around and gorges himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:19:32-07:00","id":984515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=984191#post984191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Vampire uses Blood Tenebrous to create Essence to give to a Werewolf, who in turn feeds it to a spirit, who is hit by a ghost with the Drain Numen, who then creates Plasm for a Sin-eater, who then goes off to party with his Changeling buddies, producing Glamour for them, then they trade it to a Mage for protection, who uses a Fate spell to convert it to Mana, and later converts that Mana, all while a Beast follows it around and gorges himself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which all some how creates new inferstructure of Godmachine, which feeds Angels, which gets stolen by that damn Ghost, which starts the whole process again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:26:31-07:00","id":984811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=979076#post979076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I'd seriously rethink Archetypes in light of ChroD's Aspirations and Anchors changes. Heck, with all the terminology changes we're likely to get, I wouldn't mind if \u201cThreshold\u201d and \u201cArchetype\u201d instead became \u201cDeath\u201d and \u201cLife\u201d, and were treated more like a second set of Anchors than like splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Threshold makes too much sense as a splat, I think, and in 1st Ed governs a lot more than types of sineater. For Archetype, though, I'd be interested to see it become the Virtue analogue, with something related to the geist's impulses becoming the Vice analogue, so you get small doses of willpower from following your geist's whims in the moment, but more when you fulfill the core of your new life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T04:37:18-07:00","id":984816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=984811#post984811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threshold makes too much sense as a splat, I think, and in 1st Ed governs a lot more than types of sineater. For Archetype, though, I'd be interested to see it become the Virtue analogue, with something related to the geist's impulses becoming the Vice analogue, so you get small doses of willpower from following your geist's whims in the moment, but more when you fulfill the core of your new life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heh, to keep in with the general <i>Persona</i>-like vibe of the game, how about &quot;Persona&quot; for the Virtue analogue and &quot;Shadow&quot; for the Vice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12307-frishman","name":"Frishman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T06:52:21-07:00","id":987727,"title":"","content":"Will this book might dabble or mention how the Bound view or react Death Mages (and Liches) or in even rarer cases Prometheans and Mummies? Or is that sort of stuff being saved for the Crossover Chronicle? Figure they do some degree ping up on Bound senses on the rare occasion that one would be in the same area as another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5557,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","user":"Runcible","date":". 10-15-2016, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:11:15-07:00","id":987756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Runcible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=987727#post987727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will this book might dabble or mention how the Bound view or react Death Mages (and Liches) or in even rarer cases Prometheans and Mummies? Or is that sort of stuff being saved for the Crossover Chronicle? Figure they do some degree ping up on Bound senses on the rare occasion that one would be in the same area as another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin-Eaters tend to be really unpredictable in their outlook on other Splats. Some might just see Death Mages as just another type of medium, some might be tempted to bug them for help with their condition, some might consider them blasphemous.<br /> <br /> Same with Created and Mummies. Some Sin-Eaters might empathize with Prometheans (especially ghost-focused ones), some might feel the need to destroy them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T14:40:53-07:00","id":987943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=987756#post987756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sin-Eaters tend to be really unpredictable in their outlook on other Splats. Some might just see Death Mages as just another type of medium, some might be tempted to bug them for help with their condition, some might consider them blasphemous.<br /> <br /> Same with Created and Mummies. Some Sin-Eaters might empathize with Prometheans (especially ghost-focused ones), some might feel the need to destroy them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also would depend on how they in turn were treated by those splats. A Death Mage who sees a Sin Eater's soul as ripe for experimentation would probably be a bad starting point for a functional working relationship, just as how Vampires leaving a lot of angry ghosts in their wake would probably sour any real relations between them, masquerade aside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T02:53:11-08:00","id":1004312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GimpInBlack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/399463-will-geist-get-the-2e-treatment?p=962818#post962818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I offered some feedback on it, but that was written before there was officially a Geist 2e and before I was officially the developer on it. So it's... close-ish in some respects, but it's also very much an outsider's view.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Keys are still in, but the powers are getting a major overhaul. It's still too early for me to want to talk about mechanics, but it's not going to be the same system as 1e. For one thing, trying to design and balance a full set of powers for every Key/Haunt* combo is an incredibly difficult task, and leads to a lot of weird, athematic powers. For another, space is a concern for PoD books. Geist 1e spent 37,000 words in Manifestations and Keys; we have about 25k for the topic. And finally, I'd like Geist to get some actual supplements this time around, and the logistics of trying to add new powers to a grid like that is a nightmare.<br /> <br /> So expect a tighter, more thematic power set this time around. We're experimenting with some pretty cool stuff, though comma that I think will make them feel pretty mechanically distinct from the other spots.<br /> <br /> * Spoiler. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know Geist 2e has only been on the official Monday Meetings' list for a short space of time (as creating game books goes 2 months and some change is barely any time at all) but i was wondering if another hint or sneak peak into the Key/Haunt relationship could be possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}